window.DOCS_INDEX=[{"u":"index.html","p":"Welcome","s":"Reazix Billing documentation","t":"Make GST invoices, keep track of who owes you, and prepare your GST returns. On your own computer, with no account and no monthly fee."},{"u":"index.html#what-it-does","p":"Welcome","s":"What it does","t":"what-it-does\"> Reazix Billing is invoicing and GST software for small businesses in India, and for anyone billing in other currencies: 20 are supported. It runs on your computer and opens in your web browser, the way a website does, but nothing leaves your machine. Invoices : tax invoices, bills of supply, proforma estimates, credit notes and delivery challans, with CGST, SGST, IGST and UTGST worked out for you. Getting paid : record payments, print receipts, see who is overdue and by how much. GST returns : GSTR-1 and GSTR-3B built from your invoices and purchases, as files you upload to the "},{"u":"index.html#requirements","p":"Welcome","s":"What you need","t":"requirements\"> Computer Windows 10 or 11, macOS, or Linux (a NAS works too). Browser Chrome, Edge, Firefox or Brave. The app opens in it. Disk space Roughly 200 MB once installed. Internet Only for the first install and for updates. Everything else works offline. Account or signup None."},{"u":"index.html#your-data","p":"Welcome","s":"Where your data lives","t":"your-data\"> Every invoice, client and setting is saved as plain files inside the app's folder, in _system\\data . They never leave your computer unless you turn on Google Drive backup yourself. That also means backing up is your job, and it is easy. See Backups, updates and moving PC ."},{"u":"index.html#is-it-free","p":"Welcome","s":"What does it cost?","t":"is-it-free\"> One payment, and the app is yours for life. There is no subscription, no invoice limit and no advertising, and your purchase includes 3 years of updates. Ask us at contact@reazix.com ."},{"u":"index.html#get-help","p":"Welcome","s":"Getting help","t":"get-help\"> Every screen in the app with a ? button links to the matching part of these pages. If something is missing here, or the app does something these pages don't describe, email us with a screenshot. Many features began as someone's request."},{"u":"first-run.html","p":"First-run setup","s":"The first-run setup","t":"The screens you see the first time the app opens: a four-step welcome for your business details, then a three-step setup for how your invoices look. Both can be skipped and changed later."},{"u":"first-run.html#welcome","p":"First-run setup","s":"Step 1 of the welcome: where you invoice from","t":"welcome\"> The first screen explains what the app does, and asks Where will you be invoicing from? A small Safe and private box on it sums up how your data is kept: on this computer, with no account, working offline, with no tracking. Its How we keep it safe link opens Is it safe? Security and privacy . 🇮🇳 India GST, GSTR-1 and 3B, UPI. The default. 🌍 Outside India VAT and other local taxes 🌐 Both India, with clients abroad Get Started carries on. Skip Setup goes straight to the app; fill in Settings later."},{"u":"first-run.html#business-details","p":"First-run setup","s":"Step 2: business details","t":"business-details\"> These print at the top of every invoice. Only the Business Name is required. Business Name Required Address Your full address State Needed to work out CGST and SGST versus IGST GSTIN Leave blank if you are not registered PAN, Phone, Email Optional Next stays greyed out until a Business Name is typed. Back returns to the first screen without losing what you typed. Getting it right State is where your business is registered. The app compares it with each client's state: same state means CGST + SGST, a different state means IGST. A wrong state here makes the tax wrong on every "},{"u":"first-run.html#bank-upi","p":"First-run setup","s":"Step 3: bank and UPI","t":"bank-upi\"> Where clients should pay you: bank name, account number, IFSC code and UPI ID. A UPI ID puts a scan-to-pay QR code on your invoices. You can also upload your logo and signature here, up to 500 KB each, and choose Show my business name and logo in the app's menu (ticked to start; change it any time in Settings → Company → Branding ). Skip, I’ll add later leaves it all for Settings . Something wrong? \"Image must be under 500KB\". The logo or signature file is too big. Open it in Paint (or any photo app), make it smaller, save it as PNG or JPG, and choose it again. A typing mistake in t"},{"u":"first-run.html#all-set","p":"First-run setup","s":"Step 4: you're all set","t":"all-set\"> A short list of what to do next: make your first invoice, download or share it, check the GST reports, and file your returns. Start Billing saves everything; your bank details become your first payment account . You see Setup complete! Start creating invoices. and the app opens. If you see Failed to save. Try again. , the app's engine stopped: check it is still running (see Failed to fetch ) and click Start Billing again. Next: make your first invoice ."},{"u":"first-run.html#setup-wizard","p":"First-run setup","s":"Then: setting up your invoices","t":"setup-wizard\"> Next, a three-step window sets up printing. What kind of business do you run? Pick one: Retail shop / kirana, Freelancer / consultant, Restaurant / cafe, Wholesale / trading, Manufacturing, Service / repair shop, or Everything. It decides which features the app shows: a freelancer, for example, does not see Products or Purchases. See Business type for what each one shows and hides; nothing is deleted, and you can change it any time in Settings. It also sets an invoice style to match (see Print and PDF: business type ). Or choose None of these to keep every feature as it is and s"},{"u":"first-run.html#wizard-business-type","p":"First-run setup","s":"What kind of business do you run?","t":"wizard-business-type\"> Click the card that fits you best; it turns blue. Each card has a one-line hint: Step 1 of 3: the picked card turns blue. Continue moves to paper size and language. Card For Retail shop / kirana Selling from a counter, keeping stock, buying from suppliers. Freelancer / consultant Billing for your time or services, no stock. Restaurant / cafe Quick bills, UPI payments, buying supplies. Wholesale / trading Buying and selling goods in bulk and sending them with e-way bills. Manufacturing Making products from raw material. Service / repair shop Repairs and services, spare pa"},{"u":"first-run.html#wizard-paper-language","p":"First-run setup","s":"Paper size + language","t":"wizard-paper-language\"> Paper size : what you mostly print on. It becomes the paper size of every new invoice; you can still change it on any one invoice. A4 · Standard Normal office paper and laser or inkjet printers. The usual choice. A5 · Compact Half of A4. For short bills. 80mm Thermal The common shop receipt printer (about 8 cm wide roll). 58mm Thermal Small receipt printers (about 6 cm wide roll). Not sure which thermal printer you have? Measure the paper roll, or see Thermal printing . Section label language : the language of the printed headings such as BILL TO and TOTAL: English, हिन"},{"u":"first-run.html#wizard-ready","p":"First-run setup","s":"Ready to go","t":"wizard-ready\"> A summary of the three choices: Business type , Default paper size and Section label language . Check them, then click Finish setup . You see Setup complete! Your defaults are configured. and land on the Dashboard. Your next new invoice uses these settings. Something wrong? A screen I need is missing from the sidebar. Your business type hid it. Turn it back on in Settings → Features . Invoices print on the wrong paper. Change the paper size on the invoice ( Paper / print size ), or the default in Print and PDF settings ."},{"u":"first-invoice.html","p":"Your first invoice","s":"Your first invoice","t":"From a blank app to a GST tax invoice you can send, in about five minutes."},{"u":"first-invoice.html#before-you-start","p":"Your first invoice","s":"Before you start","t":"before-you-start\"> Have these to hand: your business name, address and GSTIN, and your bank account or UPI ID if you want clients to pay you directly from the invoice. None of it is compulsory, and all of it can be added later."},{"u":"first-invoice.html#walkthrough","p":"Your first invoice","s":"Make the invoice","t":"walkthrough\"> Add your business details If you skipped the welcome, open Settings and fill in Company Details . This is the header of every invoice. Your state matters: it decides whether GST is split into CGST and SGST, or charged as IGST. Start a new invoice Click New Invoice in the sidebar. Tax Invoice is already selected, which is the right choice for a normal GST sale. Add the client Under Billed To , type the client's name. If they are registered for GST, type their GSTIN and their state fills in by itself. A mistyped GSTIN is caught straight away. Add what you sold For each line, give a"},{"u":"first-invoice.html#send","p":"Your first invoice","s":"Send it","t":"send\"> WhatsApp opens a message to the client. On a phone the PDF is attached for you; on a computer, WhatsApp does not let websites attach files, so download the PDF and drag it into the chat. Print opens your printer directly, including thermal receipt printers. Or attach the downloaded PDF to an email yourself."},{"u":"first-invoice.html#get-paid","p":"Your first invoice","s":"When the client pays","t":"get-paid\"> On the Dashboard , find the invoice and record the payment. A printable receipt opens straight away, and the invoice's status changes to Partial or Paid . Unpaid invoices past their due date are marked Overdue for you."},{"u":"first-invoice.html#whats-next","p":"Your first invoice","s":"What to do next","t":"whats-next\"> Add your products and services , so you pick them from a list instead of typing them each time. Add your bank or UPI , so a payment QR code prints on every invoice. Add your logo, signature and stamp . At the end of the month, prepare your GST returns from the invoices you have made. New to GST? Read GST basics for new business owners : registration, rates, HSN codes, returns and due dates. The Getting started list on the Dashboard tracks these for you, and ticks each one off once it is done."},{"u":"gst-basics.html","p":"GST basics","s":"GST basics for new business owners","t":"GST in plain words for a first-time shop owner, freelancer or small manufacturer: whether you need to register, which rate to charge, how to find your HSN or SAC code, which bill to give, returns and due dates, exports and LUT, and a checklist for your first week."},{"u":"gst-basics.html#what-is-gst","p":"GST basics","s":"What GST is","t":"what-is-gst\"> GST (Goods and Services Tax) is a tax on selling goods and services in India. Your customer pays it to you on top of your price. You pay it to the government. Before you pay, you take off the GST you yourself paid on things you bought for the business. That is called input tax credit . Who gets the tax depends on where your customer is: Customer in your own state : the tax is split in two equal halves, CGST (for the Centre) and SGST (for your state). Customer in another state : the whole tax is IGST (Integrated GST). In Union Territories without their own legislature, such as Cha"},{"u":"gst-basics.html#registration","p":"GST basics","s":"Do I need GST registration?","t":"registration\"> It depends on your aggregate turnover : the total of all your sales in a financial year (April to March), across India, on your PAN. It counts taxable sales, exempt sales, exports and sales to other states. It does not count the GST itself. You must register once that total crosses the limit in this table: What you sell Limit in most states Where the limit is lower Goods only ₹40 lakh ₹20 lakh in Arunachal Pradesh, Meghalaya, Puducherry, Sikkim, Telangana and Uttarakhand. ₹10 lakh in Manipur, Mizoram, Nagaland and Tripura. Services, or goods and services together ₹20 lakh ₹10 la"},{"u":"gst-basics.html#registration-compulsory","p":"GST basics","s":"When you must register whatever your turnover","t":"registration-compulsory\"> Some businesses must register from the first rupee: You sell goods to a buyer in another state. Service providers are let off: inter-state services alone do not force you to register while you are under the ₹20 lakh limit. You sell through an online marketplace that collects TCS (tax collected at source) from your payouts. One relief: since 1 October 2023, a small seller of goods who stays under the turnover limit, sells only inside one state and has no inter-state sales can sell through such a marketplace without GST registration, using an enrolment number from the G"},{"u":"gst-basics.html#voluntary-registration","p":"GST basics","s":"Registering before you have to","t":"voluntary-registration\"> You can register even below the limit. It is worth it when: most of your customers are GST-registered businesses. They can claim back the GST on your bill, so they often prefer a registered supplier; you want to claim back the GST you pay on stock, machines or services; you want to sell goods to other states, or on online marketplaces. The cost: once registered, you must charge GST on taxable sales (your price to consumers goes up) and file returns on time every month or quarter, even when you sold nothing."},{"u":"gst-basics.html#how-to-register","p":"GST basics","s":"How to register, step by step","t":"how-to-register\"> Registration is free and done online on the GST portal. Keep these ready first: Document Notes PAN Of the business. For a proprietor, your own PAN. Aadhaar Of the owner or partners and the authorised signatory, with the mobile number linked, for OTP checks. Photographs Of each owner, partner and the authorised signatory. JPG, up to 100 KB. Proof of business address Property tax receipt, municipal khata copy or electricity bill. If rented: the rent or lease agreement. If someone lets you use their place free: a consent letter from them, with their proof. Proof of the business'"},{"u":"gst-basics.html#composition","p":"GST basics","s":"Regular scheme or composition scheme?","t":"composition\"> Once registered you are in the regular scheme unless you choose composition . Composition is a simpler scheme for small local businesses: you pay a small flat percentage of your sales, out of your own pocket, and file fewer returns. Regular Composition Who can choose it Anyone registered Turnover last year up to ₹1.5 crore (₹75 lakh in Arunachal Pradesh, Manipur, Meghalaya, Mizoram, Nagaland, Sikkim, Tripura and Uttarakhand). For service providers: up to ₹50 lakh. Tax you pay The GST rate of each item, charged to your customer A flat share of your turnover: 1% for manufacturers a"},{"u":"gst-basics.html#which-rate","p":"GST basics","s":"What GST rate do I charge?","t":"which-rate\"> The rate depends on what you sell, not on who you are or how big you are. Every product and service has a code ( HSN or SAC ), and the government sets the rate for each code. You do not choose it. From 22 September 2025 the rates were simplified (\"GST 2.0\"). The main rates are now 5% , 18% and 40% . The old 12% and 28% slabs were removed for almost everything. From 1 February 2026 , pan masala, cigarettes and other tobacco products also moved to 40% (biris to 18%) and the old compensation cess on them ended. Rate Used for Examples Nil (0%) Basic necessities Fresh fruit and vegetab"},{"u":"gst-basics.html#find-rate","p":"GST basics","s":"Finding the rate for your item","t":"find-rate\"> Find the code first Look up the HSN code (goods) or SAC code (services) as described below . The rate follows from the code. Look at your supplier's bill A GST bill from your supplier shows the HSN code and the rate they charged. If you resell the same item unchanged, that is usually your code and rate too. Check the official list The GST Council's item-by-item list for the 22 September 2025 changes (linked below) gives the new rate by HSN code. The rate notifications are on CBIC's Tax Information portal, taxinformation.cbic.gov.in . Still not sure? Ask A CA or GST practitioner can"},{"u":"gst-basics.html#exempt-nil-zero","p":"GST basics","s":"Exempt, nil-rated, zero-rated and non-GST","t":"exempt-nil-zero\"> Term What it means for you Exempt or nil-rated No GST is charged, such as on fresh vegetables. You cannot claim input tax credit on purchases used for these sales. If you sell only these, give a Bill of Supply . Zero-rated Exports and sales to SEZ units. No GST in the end, and you keep your input tax credit. See Exports . Outside GST Petrol, diesel, natural gas, aviation fuel and liquor for drinking. They carry other taxes, not GST."},{"u":"gst-basics.html#hsn-sac","p":"GST basics","s":"Finding your HSN or SAC code","t":"hsn-sac\"> HSN (Harmonised System of Nomenclature) codes classify goods. They are used around the world, and each extra pair of digits narrows the item down: the first 2 digits are the chapter, 4 digits the heading, 6 the sub-heading and 8 the exact tariff item. For example, 3306 is toothpaste and other dental preparations, and 8712 is bicycles. SAC (Services Accounting Code) codes classify services. They start with 99. For example, 998314 is IT design and development services, and 9963 is hotel and restaurant services. Official sources: GST Council 56th meeting annexures (HSN-wise lists)"},{"u":"gst-basics.html#hsn-digits","p":"GST basics","s":"How many digits to print","t":"hsn-digits\"> It depends on your AATO , your aggregate turnover in the last financial year: Turnover last year Bills to registered businesses (B2B) Bills to consumers (B2C) Up to ₹5 crore At least 4 digits Optional Above ₹5 crore At least 6 digits At least 6 digits More digits are always allowed, and are often clearer. The same rule applies to the HSN summary in your GSTR-1; tell the app which applies to you in GSTR filing details . Official sources: Notification 78/2020-Central Tax · CGST Rules, rule 46"},{"u":"gst-basics.html#hsn-search","p":"GST basics","s":"Searching the official list","t":"hsn-search\"> Open the search On gst.gov.in, without logging in, go to Services › User Services › Search HSN Code . The direct address is services.gst.gov.in/services/searchhsnsac . Search by name or by number Choose HSN for goods or SAC for services, then type a plain word such as toothpaste or repair , or the first digits of a code. Pick the closest description Read the results and choose the most specific one that fits. Check the chapter it sits in makes sense for your item. Want the whole list? The same page has Download HSN Directory in Excel Format . Search by what it is made of and what "},{"u":"gst-basics.html#invoices","p":"GST basics","s":"Which bill to give, and what goes on it","t":"invoices\"> Document When Tax invoice You are registered (regular scheme) and sell something taxable. Bill of supply You are in the composition scheme, or you sell only exempt or nil-rated items. No GST is shown. Credit note To reduce an invoice you already gave: goods returned, a discount after the sale, or you charged too much. Debit note To increase an invoice you already gave, when you charged too little. Delivery challan Moving goods without selling them: to a job worker, on approval, or between your own places. If you are not registered, give an ordinary bill or cash memo without GST. It "},{"u":"gst-basics.html#invoice-contents","p":"GST basics","s":"What a tax invoice must show","t":"invoice-contents\"> Your name, address and GSTIN. An invoice number of up to 16 characters (letters, numbers, - and / ), never repeated within a financial year, and the date. The buyer's name, address and GSTIN, if they are registered. For an unregistered buyer, their name, address, delivery address and state when the bill is ₹50,000 or more (or whenever they ask). The HSN or SAC code, description, quantity and unit of each item. The total value, the taxable value after any discount, and the rate and amount of CGST, SGST, IGST and cess. The place of supply and its state, for a sale to another s"},{"u":"gst-basics.html#b2b-b2c","p":"GST basics","s":"B2B, B2C and the buyer's GSTIN","t":"b2b-b2c\"> B2B means your buyer is GST-registered. Put their GSTIN on the invoice. They can only claim back the GST you charged if the invoice carries their correct GSTIN and you report it in your GSTR-1. A wrong GSTIN costs your buyer their credit. The app checks a GSTIN's format as you type it: see What the GSTIN check tells you . B2C means your buyer is a consumer or an unregistered business. These sales are reported as totals, except an inter-state sale to an unregistered buyer above ₹1 lakh, which is reported bill by bill."},{"u":"gst-basics.html#place-of-supply","p":"GST basics","s":"Place of supply, in plain words","t":"place-of-supply\"> The place of supply decides whether you charge CGST and SGST or IGST. Goods : generally where the goods are delivered, where their journey ends. Services : generally where your registered buyer is. For an unregistered buyer, their address if you have it, otherwise your own location. Exceptions : some services follow their own rule. For example, work on a building is supplied where the building is, and a restaurant meal where it is served. Same state as yours: CGST and SGST. Different state: IGST. In the app, the Place of Supply field starts with the client's state; change it "},{"u":"gst-basics.html#itc","p":"GST basics","s":"Input tax credit (ITC)","t":"itc\"> Input tax credit means you take the GST you paid on business purchases off the GST you owe on your sales. You pay only the difference. Example. You buy stock for ₹10,000 plus 18% GST, ₹1,800. You sell it for ₹15,000 plus 18% GST, ₹2,700. You owe ₹2,700, take off the ₹1,800 credit, and pay ₹900. Official sources: CGST Act section 16"},{"u":"gst-basics.html#itc-conditions","p":"GST basics","s":"When you can claim it","t":"itc-conditions\"> You have the supplier's tax invoice (or debit note), with your GSTIN on it. The supplier has reported it in their GSTR-1, so it shows in your GSTR-2B on the portal. You have received the goods or the service. For goods that come in lots, after the last lot. The supplier has paid the tax to the government. You file your own GSTR-3B. You pay the supplier within 180 days of the invoice date. If you do not, you must pay the credit back, with interest, and can claim it again when you pay. You claim it by 30 November after the financial year ends, or by the date you file your annual"},{"u":"gst-basics.html#itc-blocked","p":"GST basics","s":"What you cannot claim credit on","t":"itc-blocked\"> Cars and other vehicles for people with up to 13 seats, and their insurance and repairs, unless you sell vehicles, carry passengers for a fare, or run a driving school. Food and drinks, outdoor catering, beauty treatment, health services, cosmetic surgery, and life and health insurance, unless you supply the same thing yourself or a law makes you provide it to staff. Club, gym and fitness memberships, and holiday travel for employees. Building or renovating your own shop or office (other than plant and machinery). Anything for personal use. Goods lost, stolen, destroyed, written "},{"u":"gst-basics.html#returns","p":"GST basics","s":"Returns and due dates","t":"returns\"> A return is a form you file on the GST portal to report your sales and pay the tax. The dates below are the usual ones; the government sometimes extends them, so check the portal. Return Due Who files it What it is GSTR-1 11th of the next month Regular, monthly Your sales, bill by bill for B2B GSTR-3B 20th of the next month Regular, monthly Summary of sales and credit; you pay the tax with it GSTR-1 (QRMP) 13th of the month after the quarter Turnover up to ₹5 crore who chose quarterly filing Sales for the quarter IFF 13th of the next month QRMP Optional: B2B bills for month 1 or 2 of"},{"u":"gst-basics.html#returns-in-app","p":"GST basics","s":"How the app helps","t":"returns-in-app\"> The app does not log in to the portal or file for you. It prepares the figures and the files from what you have entered: GSTR-1 and GSTR-3B , as JSON files you upload on the portal, for a month, a quarter or a year ( Choosing the period ). GSTR-2B matching , to see which purchase credits your suppliers have reported. The Filing Guide , with step-by-step portal instructions for regular and nil returns."},{"u":"gst-basics.html#eway-einvoice","p":"GST basics","s":"E-way bill and e-invoicing","t":"eway-einvoice\"> E-way bill. Before goods worth more than ₹50,000 are moved in one consignment, an e-way bill is generated on ewaybillgst.gov.in , with the vehicle details. Some states set a higher limit for movement within the state. Services do not need one. The app can make the file for the e-way bill portal: see E-way bill . E-invoicing. If your aggregate turnover has been above ₹5 crore in any financial year since 2017-18, your B2B invoices and exports must be registered on the e-invoice portal, which gives each one an IRN and a QR code. Below ₹5 crore you do not need it. See E-invoicing ("},{"u":"gst-basics.html#exports","p":"GST basics","s":"Exports and foreign clients","t":"exports\"> Exports, and sales to units in a Special Economic Zone (SEZ), are zero-rated : no GST in the end, and you still get credit for the GST on your purchases. There are two ways to do it: Under a LUT, without paying IGST. The simple way for most small exporters. Paying IGST on the invoice, then claiming that IGST back as a refund. Selling a service to a foreign client counts as an export when you are in India, the client is outside India, the place of supply is outside India, you are paid in foreign currency (or in rupees where the RBI allows it), and the client is not your own branch abr"},{"u":"gst-basics.html#lut","p":"GST basics","s":"LUT: exporting without paying IGST","t":"lut\"> A Letter of Undertaking (form GST RFD-11 ) is a promise to the department that you will follow the export rules. With it you export without paying IGST, so no money is stuck waiting for a refund. Any registered business can file one, unless it has been prosecuted for tax evasion of more than ₹2.5 crore. It costs nothing. A LUT is valid for one financial year. File a fresh one every year, before the first export of the year; the start of April is a good habit. Open the form Log in to gst.gov.in and go to Services › User Services › Furnish Letter of Undertaking (LUT) . Choose the year Pick"},{"u":"gst-basics.html#export-invoice","p":"GST basics","s":"What to print on an export or SEZ invoice","t":"export-invoice\"> Rule 46 says the invoice must carry this declaration, word for word: Under a LUT: \"SUPPLY MEANT FOR EXPORT/SUPPLY TO SEZ UNIT OR SEZ DEVELOPER FOR AUTHORISED OPERATIONS UNDER BOND OR LETTER OF UNDERTAKING WITHOUT PAYMENT OF INTEGRATED TAX\" Paying IGST: \"SUPPLY MEANT FOR EXPORT/SUPPLY TO SEZ UNIT OR SEZ DEVELOPER FOR AUTHORISED OPERATIONS ON PAYMENT OF INTEGRATED TAX\" For an export it must also show the buyer's name and address, the delivery address and the country of destination. Many exporters also print their LUT's ARN and the year it covers. The rule does not ask for it, bu"},{"u":"gst-basics.html#sez","p":"GST basics","s":"Selling to an SEZ","t":"sez\"> A unit or developer in a Special Economic Zone has a GSTIN like any other business. A supply to it for its authorised operations is zero-rated, even when it is in your own state: either under your LUT with no tax, or with IGST (never CGST and SGST) that the buyer or you then claim back. Keep the buyer's proof that the goods or services were received in the SEZ for its authorised operations."},{"u":"gst-basics.html#tds-tcs","p":"GST basics","s":"TDS and TCS: when tax is cut from your payment","t":"tds-tcs\"> Three different things are called TDS or TCS. A small business usually meets them like this:"},{"u":"gst-basics.html#income-tax-tds","p":"GST basics","s":"A client deducts income-tax TDS from your payment","t":"income-tax-tds\"> Many business clients must deduct income tax (TDS) when they pay you for contract work, professional or technical fees, rent, commission, or large purchases of goods. They pay you the rest and deposit the TDS with the income tax department against your PAN. Example. You bill ₹1,00,000 plus GST. Your client deducts ₹10,000 as TDS and pays you the rest. The ₹10,000 is not lost: it is credited to your PAN, and you claim it in your income tax return. When your invoice shows GST separately, TDS is worked out on the amount before GST. Check it reached your PAN : log in at incometax."},{"u":"gst-basics.html#gst-tds-tcs","p":"GST basics","s":"GST TDS and GST TCS","t":"gst-tds-tcs\"> GST TDS : government departments and some public bodies deduct 2% GST TDS when a contract with them is worth more than ₹2.5 lakh. It shows on the portal as a credit you can use to pay your GST. GST TCS : an online marketplace keeps 0.5% of the net value of your taxable sales through it (since 10 July 2024; it was 1% before). Accept it on the portal and it is added to your cash ledger, to pay your GST with. Official sources: CGST Act sections 51 and 52, on the CBIC Tax Information portal · Notification 15/2024-Central Tax (TCS 0.5%)"},{"u":"gst-basics.html#first-week","p":"GST basics","s":"Your first week: a checklist","t":"first-week\"> Work out your turnover Estimate a year's sales and check the table in Do I need GST registration? and the list in When you must register . Get your PAN and a bank account Open a separate current account for the business, so business and personal money never mix. Choose your scheme Regular or composition: see which one suits you . Register On gst.gov.in ( steps ). Add your bank account on the portal, display your registration certificate, and, under composition, put \"Composition Taxable Person\" on your signboard. Set up the app Go through the first-run setup . Set your state and GS"},{"u":"gst-basics.html#glossary","p":"GST basics","s":"Words you will meet","t":"glossary\"> Word Meaning AATO Annual aggregate turnover: all your sales in a financial year, on all GSTINs under one PAN. Decides your HSN digits, QRMP and e-invoicing. ARN Application Reference Number: the receipt number the GST portal gives when you submit something, such as a registration or a LUT. GSTIN Your 15-character GST number. The first two digits are your state code, the next ten your PAN. HSN The code for a kind of goods. Decides the rate. ITC Input tax credit: GST you paid on business purchases, taken off the GST you owe. LUT Letter of Undertaking (form RFD-11), filed every year to"},{"u":"install.html","p":"Install on Windows","s":"Install on Windows, step by step","t":"Paste one line and press Enter. About 3 minutes, no technical knowledge needed, no administrator password, and no \"Windows protected your PC\" warning. Every step below says what to press and what you will see."},{"u":"install.html#before","p":"Install on Windows","s":"Before you start","t":"before\"> Windows 10 or Windows 11. To check: press Windows + R , type winver , press Enter . Internet for the install only (it downloads about 25 MB). After that the app works offline. About 600 MB of free space."},{"u":"install.html#one-line","p":"Install on Windows","s":"Install with one line","t":"one-line\"> Copy this line Click the Copy button at the right end of the line below. (Or select all of it with the mouse and press Ctrl + C .) powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -c \"[Net.ServicePointManager]::SecurityProtocol='Tls12'; irm https://billing.reazix.com/install.ps1 | iex\" Press Windows + R Hold the Windows key (the one with the Windows logo) and press R . A small Run box opens at the bottom left. Paste and press Enter Click in the box, press Ctrl + V , then press Enter . Watch it work A blue or black window shows four steps, each ending in OK : [1/4] Checking this computer ... OK [2"},{"u":"install.html#zip","p":"Install on Windows","s":"Other way: download the ZIP","t":"zip\"> For offices that copy the app from a USB stick, or where the line above is blocked. It takes a few more clicks and Windows shows a warning the first time."},{"u":"install.html#download","p":"Install on Windows","s":"Step 1: Download","t":"download\"> Click this button Download Reazix Billing Wait for the download to finish Your browser shows it at the top right (Chrome and Edge) or bottom left. The file is called Reazix-Billing.zip . Open your Downloads folder Click the folder icon next to the download, or open File Explorer (the yellow folder on the taskbar) and click Downloads on the left."},{"u":"install.html#extract-first","p":"Install on Windows","s":"Step 2: Unzip (extract) it","t":"extract-first\"> A ZIP is a packed folder. Windows can open it, but the app cannot run from inside it, so it has to be unpacked first. Right-click the ZIP Right-click Reazix-Billing.zip and choose Extract All… . (On Windows 11 it may be under Show more options .) Choose where Click Browse… and pick Documents , or a drive like D:\\ . Not Downloads : things there get deleted when people tidy up. Do not choose C:\\Program Files . Click Extract A new folder called Reazix-Billing opens. Inside you see Reazix Billing - WINDOWS , READ ME FIRST , and launchers for Mac and Linux. If you double-click the l"},{"u":"install.html#launch","p":"Install on Windows","s":"Step 3: Open the launcher and click Install","t":"launch\"> Double-click \"Reazix Billing - WINDOWS\" In the Reazix-Billing folder. If Windows warns you See \"Windows protected your PC\" just below: click More info , then Run anyway . If it asks Do you want to run this file? , click Run or Open . Click Install A small window opens with one big button. Click Install . There is nothing to fill in. Leave the black window alone A black window appears and does the work: it may get Node.js (the engine the app runs on, about 30 MB, kept inside the app folder). This takes 1 to 3 minutes. Don't close it; it closes by itself. The app opens by itself in its "},{"u":"install.html#windows-protected","p":"Install on Windows","s":"\"Windows protected your PC\"","t":"windows-protected\"> This blue box appears the first time for any program that is not signed with a paid certificate (a certificate Reazix does not have yet). It does not mean anything is wrong. More in Is the install safe? Click the small link More info . Click the button Run anyway . If the file will not open at all: right-click Reazix Billing - WINDOWS , choose Properties , tick Unblock at the bottom, click OK , and double-click it again. If your antivirus deletes a file during the install, add the Reazix-Billing folder to its exclusions (often under Exclusions or Allowed apps ) and click In"},{"u":"install.html#every-day","p":"Install on Windows","s":"Every day after that","t":"every-day\"> Double-click the \"Reazix Billing\" icon on your Desktop The install put this icon (the blue R ) there and in the Start menu. It starts the app and opens it in its own window. There is nothing else to click. Update, back up, restore, restart and stop the app from the Control Panel in the app's menu. Restarting the computer also stops it. The launcher, Reazix Billing - WINDOWS in the Reazix-Billing folder, stays there for updates and repairs. Your data is in the _system\\data folder inside Reazix-Billing; see Backups . Use only this icon. If you also have a Reazix Billing app icon made"},{"u":"install.html#what-install-does","p":"Install on Windows","s":"What the installer does","t":"what-install-does\"> Checks your PC : Windows 10 or 11, enough free space, a folder it can write to, and the internet. Sets up Node.js inside the app folder if the PC does not have a recent one. It is downloaded once from nodejs.org into _system\\node . Nothing is installed into Windows and no administrator password is needed. If that download fails, it asks before using Windows' own installer (winget), and otherwise opens the download page. Adds a Reazix Billing shortcut to your Desktop and Start menu. Opens the app in your browser. The app's parts come inside the ZIP, so nothing else is downlo"},{"u":"install.html#one-command","p":"Install on Windows","s":"For IT people","t":"one-command\"> The one line can also be pasted into an open PowerShell window. To install into another folder, set it first: $env:REAZIX_DIR = 'D:\\Apps\\Reazix Billing' . If that folder already has the app, it is updated in place."},{"u":"install.html#uninstall","p":"Install on Windows","s":"Removing the app","t":"uninstall\"> Back up your data first if you may want it again. See Export everything to one file . The easy way: in the app, open Control Panel and use Remove… . Tick what else to delete (your data, PDFs, backups) and click Remove the app . See Remove the App . Or, with the app closed, double-click Reazix Billing - WINDOWS in the app folder, click More options , then Remove the app... : the same tick boxes, then Remove the app . Or with one line: press Windows + R , paste this line and press Enter : powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -c \"[Net.ServicePointManager]::SecurityProtocol='Tls12'; & (["},{"u":"install-mac.html","p":"Install on a Mac","s":"Install on a Mac, step by step","t":"Paste one line into Terminal and press Return. About 3 minutes, no password, and no \"Apple cannot check it\" message. Every step says what you will see."},{"u":"install-mac.html#before","p":"Install on a Mac","s":"Before you start","t":"before\"> macOS 11 Big Sur or newer. To check: click the Apple menu (the apple logo at the top left), then About This Mac . Internet for the install. After that the app works offline. About 600 MB of free space."},{"u":"install-mac.html#one-line","p":"Install on a Mac","s":"Install with one line","t":"one-line\"> Copy this line Click the Copy button at the right end of the line below. (Or select all of it and press Cmd + C .) curl -fsSL https://billing.reazix.com/install.sh | bash Open Terminal Press Cmd + Space , type Terminal and press Return . A plain text window opens. (More help: Opening Terminal on a Mac .) Paste and press Return Press Cmd + V , then Return . Watch it work It shows four steps, each ending in OK : [1/4] Checking this computer , [2/4] Downloading (also Node.js, the engine the app runs on, if this Mac does not have it), [3/4] Installing , [4/4] Adding icons . Answer two q"},{"u":"install-mac.html#uninstall-mac","p":"Install on a Mac","s":"Removing the app","t":"uninstall-mac\"> The easy way: in the app, open Control Panel and use Remove… , then tick what else to delete. See Remove the App . Or paste this into Terminal and press Return : curl -fsSL https://billing.reazix.com/install.sh | bash -s -- --uninstall It removes the app and its icon. Your invoices are kept unless you type DELETE when it asks. If the app is in the Dock, drag it out."},{"u":"install-mac.html#zip","p":"Install on a Mac","s":"Other way: download the ZIP","t":"zip\"> Three parts: install Node.js, download the app, open it. About 10 minutes."},{"u":"install-mac.html#node","p":"Install on a Mac","s":"Part 1: Install Node.js (once)","t":"node\"> Node.js is free software the app runs on. It installs like any other Mac app. Go to nodejs.org Open nodejs.org/en/download in Safari or Chrome. Download the macOS Installer Click the button for the macOS Installer (.pkg) of the LTS version. (LTS means the stable version.) Open the downloaded file Click the download arrow in your browser, or open Finder → Downloads , and double-click the file whose name starts with node-v and ends in .pkg . Click through the installer Continue , Continue , Agree , Install . Type your Mac password when asked and click Install Software . Then Close . (If i"},{"u":"install-mac.html#download","p":"Install on a Mac","s":"Part 2: Download and unzip the app","t":"download\"> Download Download Reazix Billing Find it in Downloads Open Finder (the blue face in the Dock) and click Downloads on the left. Safari usually unzips it for you, so you see a folder called Reazix-Billing . If you see Reazix-Billing.zip instead, double-click it to unzip. Move the folder to Documents Drag the Reazix-Billing folder onto Documents on the left of Finder, so it is not deleted when Downloads is cleared. Your invoices will be kept inside it."},{"u":"install-mac.html#open","p":"Install on a Mac","s":"Part 3: Open it the first time","t":"open\"> Apple asks you to confirm apps that are not from the App Store. This is needed once . Control-click the launcher In the Reazix-Billing folder, hold the Control key and click Reazix Billing - MAC (or right-click it, or click with two fingers on a trackpad). Choose Open . Confirm A box says macOS cannot check the developer. Click Open . On macOS 15 Sequoia or newer, if there is no Open button Click Done . Open the Apple menu (the apple logo) → System Settings → Privacy & Security , scroll down to the message about Reazix Billing - MAC , click Open Anyway , type your password, then Open An"},{"u":"install-mac.html#mac-messages","p":"Install on a Mac","s":"If the Mac shows a message","t":"mac-messages\"> \"could not be executed because you do not have appropriate access privileges\" : you have a download from before v1.10.82. Download it again (Part 2), or fix this copy: open Terminal (see Opening Terminal on a Mac ), type chmod +x and a space, drag Reazix Billing - MAC from Finder into the Terminal window, press Return , then go back to Part 3. \"Node.js is not installed\" in the Terminal window: do Part 1, then open the launcher again. If it asks Open the Node.js download page now? [y/N] , type y and press Return . \"Node.js ... is too old\" : install the current LTS from nodejs.org"},{"u":"install-mac.html#every-day","p":"Install on a Mac","s":"Every day after that","t":"every-day\"> Double-click \"Reazix Billing - MAC\" After the first time, a normal double-click works. If the app is already running it just opens your browser. Tip: make a Desktop shortcut. Control-click the launcher → Make Alias , and drag the alias to your Desktop. You can also bookmark http://localhost:47371 in your browser; it works while the app is running. To stop the app: in the app open Control Panel in the sidebar and click Stop Server . Restarting the Mac also stops it. Your data is in Reazix-Billing/_system/data . Updating: see Updating on a Mac ; never drag a new download over the old"},{"u":"install-linux.html","p":"Install on Linux / NAS","s":"Install on Linux or a NAS, step by step","t":"For Ubuntu, Linux Mint, Debian, Fedora and similar: paste one line into the Terminal and press Enter. No password needed. Each step is explained."},{"u":"install-linux.html#terminal","p":"Install on Linux / NAS","s":"Open the Terminal","t":"terminal\"> Press Ctrl + Alt + T . A window opens where you type commands. New to this? Read Using the Terminal first; it takes two minutes. To paste a command into the Terminal, use Ctrl + Shift + V (not Ctrl + V ), then press Enter ."},{"u":"install-linux.html#one-line","p":"Install on Linux / NAS","s":"Install with one line","t":"one-line\"> Copy this line, paste it into the Terminal, press Enter curl -fsSL https://billing.reazix.com/install.sh | bash Watch it work It shows four steps, each ending in OK : [1/4] Checking this computer , [2/4] Downloading (also Node.js, the engine the app runs on, if the computer does not have version 18 or newer; it is kept inside the app folder), [3/4] Installing , [4/4] Adding icons . Answer one question Open Reazix Billing by itself when this computer starts? [y/N] : type y and press Enter , or just Enter for no. The app opens In its own window if you have Chrome, Chromium or Edge, or"},{"u":"install-linux.html#zip","p":"Install on Linux / NAS","s":"Other way: download the ZIP","t":"zip\"> Install Node.js yourself, then unzip and start the app."},{"u":"install-linux.html#node","p":"Install on Linux / NAS","s":"Step 1: Install Node.js 20","t":"node\"> The Node.js in Ubuntu's own store is often too old for the app, so it comes from NodeSource, the official source for Linux. Paste these one at a time, pressing Enter after each: sudo apt install -y curl unzip curl -fsSL https://deb.nodesource.com/setup_20.x | sudo -E bash - sudo apt install -y nodejs When it asks for your password , type the password you use to log in and press Enter . Nothing appears while you type , not even dots; that is normal. Check it worked: node -v It should print v20 or higher, for example v20.19.0 . Fedora: sudo dnf install nodejs npm . Arch: sudo pacman -S no"},{"u":"install-linux.html#download","p":"Install on Linux / NAS","s":"Step 2: Download and unzip","t":"download\"> Download Download Reazix Billing It goes into your Downloads folder. Unzip it Paste this in the Terminal and press Enter : it unpacks the app into a folder in your home folder. cd ~ && unzip -o ~/Downloads/Reazix-Billing.zip"},{"u":"install-linux.html#start","p":"Install on Linux / NAS","s":"Step 3: Start the app","t":"start\"> cd ~/Reazix-Billing && bash \"Reazix Billing - LINUX.sh\" Wait up to a minute When it says Server running , the app opens in your browser at http://localhost:47371 . You can close the Terminal; the app keeps running. (A download from before version 1.10.83 first asks Install now? [Y/n] : press Enter .) Every day after that , open the Terminal and run the same command. Or bookmark http://localhost:47371 ; it works while the app is running. To stop the app: Control Panel in the app → Stop Server , or restart the computer."},{"u":"install-linux.html#nas","p":"Install on Linux / NAS","s":"On a NAS or server (for IT people)","t":"nas\"> unzip Reazix-Billing.zip cd Reazix-Billing bash \"_system/start-unix.sh\" The ZIP carries the app's packages, so there is no npm install ; any Node.js 18 or newer runs it. The app listens on 127.0.0.1:47371 only (it has no login, so it is never opened to the network). Updating from inside the app needs unzip or python3."},{"u":"update.html","p":"Updating","s":"Updating the app, step by step","t":"Your purchase includes 3 years of updates. Updating keeps all your invoices, clients and settings, and the app backs them up first. The easiest way is one button inside the app."},{"u":"update.html#in-app","p":"Updating","s":"The easy way: the Update button (Windows, Mac, Linux)","t":"in-app\"> Open the app When a new version is out, the sidebar shows Update to v… (you can also go to Settings → App Updates ). Read what is new and click Update Now A window shows what changed. Click Update Now . Wait about a minute A window shows the progress; it backs up your data first, then updates. Reload the page Press F5 (on a Mac Cmd + R ). The version at the bottom of the Dashboard shows the new number. Changes still look the same? Press Ctrl + F5 (Mac: Cmd + Shift + R ) to make the browser load the new version."},{"u":"update.html#update-window","p":"Updating","s":"The \"Update available\" window","t":"update-window\"> It opens when you click Update to v… in the sidebar. At the top it shows the new version and the one you are on, with the date it was released. Part What it means Your data is safe. Updating replaces only the app itself. Your data folder (invoices, clients, products, settings) and your Saved Invoices PDFs are never touched. The release notes What changed in this version. Recommended: export a backup Open Settings → Data Management takes you to Export Backup . Worth doing before any update, just in case. Skip this version Hides the Update to v… button for this version. The next "},{"u":"update.html#one-line","p":"Updating","s":"Also easy: the install line again","t":"one-line\"> The line that installs the app also updates it, and repairs it if it will not start. It finds your install, backs up your data first, replaces only the app's own files and opens the new version. Windows: press Windows + R , paste this, press Enter : powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -c \"[Net.ServicePointManager]::SecurityProtocol='Tls12'; irm https://billing.reazix.com/install.ps1 | iex\" Mac and Linux: open Terminal, paste this, press Return : curl -fsSL https://billing.reazix.com/install.sh | bash"},{"u":"update.html#windows","p":"Updating","s":"Windows: other ways","t":"windows\"> From the launcher: double-click Reazix Billing - WINDOWS in the Reazix-Billing folder → More options → Update to the latest version → then Open App . By hand, with the ZIP (if the app does not open at all): Download Download Reazix Billing Stop the app Launcher → More options → Stop the app . Extract into the same place as before Right-click the ZIP → Extract All… → Browse… → choose the folder that contains your Reazix-Billing folder (for example Documents ) → Extract . Replace the files Windows asks about files that already exist: choose Replace the files in the destination . On Win"},{"u":"update.html#mac","p":"Updating","s":"Mac: other ways","t":"mac\"> Use the Update button in the app. That is the safe way on a Mac. Never drag a new download over your old folder on a Mac On a Mac, Finder's Replace swaps the whole folder, including _system/data with all your invoices. (Windows merges folders; the Mac does not.) If the app will not open and you need the new download: Back up first If the app opens: Settings → Data Management → Export Backup… . Download and unzip the new version It appears as a new folder (macOS may call it Reazix-Billing 2 ). Move your data across In your old folder open _system (if you cannot see it, press Cmd + Shift +"},{"u":"update.html#linux","p":"Updating","s":"Linux: other ways","t":"linux\"> Use the Update button, or in the Terminal: sh ~/Reazix-Billing/_system/update-unix.sh It downloads the newest version, checks every file, keeps _system/data , and rolls back if anything fails. Restart the app afterwards."},{"u":"terminal.html","p":"Using the Terminal","s":"Using the Terminal, for beginners","t":"Some fixes ask you to type a command. The Terminal (Command Prompt on Windows) is just a window where you type an instruction and press Enter. This page shows how, on every computer."},{"u":"terminal.html#what","p":"Using the Terminal","s":"What it is","t":"what\"> A plain window with a blinking cursor. You type (or paste) one line, press Enter (Mac: Return ), and the computer does it and prints the result. You cannot break anything by opening it, and closing the window is always safe."},{"u":"terminal.html#windows","p":"Using the Terminal","s":"Opening it on Windows","t":"windows\"> Press Windows + R A small Run box opens at the bottom left. Type cmd and press Enter A black Command Prompt window opens. To paste a command: Ctrl + V , or right-click inside the window. Then press Enter . Example: to see your Node.js version, type node -v and press Enter . It prints something like v20.19.0 . If it prints not recognized , Node.js is not installed for the whole PC, which is fine: the app keeps its own copy."},{"u":"terminal.html#mac","p":"Using the Terminal","s":"Opening it on a Mac","t":"mac\"> Press Cmd + Space The Spotlight search bar opens in the middle of the screen. Type Terminal and press Return A white or black Terminal window opens. Or: Finder → Applications → Utilities → Terminal . To paste a command: Cmd + V , then Return ."},{"u":"terminal.html#linux","p":"Using the Terminal","s":"Opening it on Linux","t":"linux\"> Press Ctrl + Alt + T , or search for Terminal in your apps. To paste: Ctrl + Shift + V , then Enter ."},{"u":"terminal.html#tips","p":"Using the Terminal","s":"Four things worth knowing","t":"tips\"> Drag a file in to type its location. Instead of typing a long folder path, drag the file from Finder or File Explorer into the Terminal window; its full path appears, ready to use. Passwords are invisible. When it asks for your password, nothing appears as you type, not even dots. Type it anyway and press Enter . Names with spaces need quotes. \"Reazix Billing - MAC.command\" . Dragging the file in adds what is needed for you. To stop a command that keeps running, press Ctrl + C ."},{"u":"terminal.html#example","p":"Using the Terminal","s":"Example: fixing the Mac launcher","t":"example\"> If a Mac says the launcher could not be executed because you do not have appropriate access privileges : Open Terminal Cmd + Space , type Terminal , Return . Type the start of the command Type chmod +x and then one space. Do not press Return yet. Drag the launcher in Drag Reazix Billing - MAC from your Reazix-Billing folder into the Terminal window. The line now ends with its location. Press Return Nothing is printed: that means it worked. Close Terminal and open the launcher again (Control-click → Open )."},{"u":"invoices.html","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Making an invoice","t":"Every card of the New Invoice screen, from top to bottom: the toolbar, the document type, the client, invoice details, ship-to and order details, the items, discounts, GST, TDS and TCS, terms, extra pages, and what happens when you save, print or share."},{"u":"invoices.html#screen-layout","p":"Making an invoice","s":"How the screen is laid out","t":"screen-layout\"> Open it with New Invoice in the sidebar, or Ctrl + N . The same screen opens when you edit, duplicate or convert an invoice from the Dashboard. The form is on the left and a live preview of the printed invoice is on the right. From top to bottom, the form has these cards: Invoice Type : the kind of document, and whether it is for goods or services. The Customize panel opens inside this card. Billed To : the client's name, address, state and GSTIN. Invoice Details : number, dates, place of supply, the Ship to address and the optional order, dispatch and reference details . Line "},{"u":"invoices.html#toolbar","p":"Making an invoice","s":"The toolbar","t":"toolbar\"> The toolbar stays at the top of the screen as you scroll, so Save, Print and the rest are always in reach on a long invoice. Button What it does ← Back Leaves the invoice. If you have changed something that is not saved, you are asked first (see Leaving with unsaved changes ). ? Opens this guide. Save status A small coloured badge that tells you whether the invoice is saved. See Saving as you go . Save Saves the invoice without making a PDF. Ctrl + S does the same. Save & Download Saves the invoice and downloads the PDF. See Save & Download . Print Saves the invoice, then prints it. "},{"u":"invoices.html#invoice-types","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Invoice Type: choosing the document","t":"invoice-types\"> The chips at the top of the first card decide the printed title, the number series, whether GST is charged, and whether the document counts as a sale in your totals and GST returns. Hover over a chip to see a one-line description; the same line shows under the chips for the one you picked. Chip Prints as Numbered Use it for GST Counts as a sale? Tax Invoice TAX INVOICE INV… A normal sale by a GST-registered business Yes Yes Quotation QUOTATION QUO… A priced offer for work or supply. Convert it to a tax invoice when the client accepts. Shown No Proforma / Estimate PROFORMA INVOI"},{"u":"invoices.html#goods-services","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Goods, services or both","t":"goods-services\"> Under the type chips, This invoice is for: sets which units the Unit list offers and which unit a new row starts with. It does not change the tax. Chip Units offered Good for 📦 Goods Pcs, Nos, Kg, g, Tonne, Ltr, ml, Mtr, cm, Ft, In, Sq.ft, Sq.m, Box, Dozen, Pair, Set, Bag, Roll, Bottle and the like. The default. Shops, traders, manufacturers ⏱ Services Hrs, Day, Week, Month, Year, Visit, Session, Project, Word, Page, plus Nos, Sq.ft and Sq.m. A reminder appears to use a SAC code (the services version of HSN) in the HSN/SAC box. Terms print in the Formatted layout unless you c"},{"u":"invoices.html#billed-to","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Billed To: the client","t":"billed-to\"> This card says who the invoice is for. Their name, address, state and GSTIN print in the BILL TO block. The state matters most: it decides whether GST is charged as CGST + SGST or as IGST (see How GST is worked out ). Field What to enter Client Name Click it to see your saved clients, or type to search. Pick one to fill in everything below. You can also bill a name that is not saved. Pencil button Appears beside the name once a saved client is picked. Opens their full details for editing (see Adding and editing a client ). Typing a different name unlinks the saved client and the pe"},{"u":"invoices.html#client","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Picking a saved client, or saving a new one","t":"client\"> Click Client Name Your saved clients drop down, each with their city and state, and their GSTIN when they have one. Type to narrow the list Any part of the name works. Use ↓ ↑ to move and Enter to pick, or click one. Esc closes the list. Each row has its own pencil to edit that client straight away. Check what was filled in Picking a client fills in their address, country, city, PIN, state and GSTIN, and a message says Loaded client: name . Or save someone new Type their name; at the bottom of the list click Save \"name\" as new client . The client form opens with what you have typed so"},{"u":"invoices.html#gstin-check","p":"Making an invoice","s":"What the GSTIN check tells you","t":"gstin-check\"> When you leave the GSTIN box, the app reads the number. The first two digits are the state code, and the last character is a check character. This works offline, with no GST portal lookup. Message under the box Meaning What to do ✓ Registered in state — state filled in. The State was blank, so it has been filled in from the GSTIN. Nothing. ✓ Registered in state . The GSTIN and the State agree. Nothing. ⚠ This GSTIN is registered in state , but the state says other state . The two disagree. Check which is right. The tax split follows the State and Place of Supply, not the GSTIN. ⚠"},{"u":"invoices.html#client-credit","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Using a client's credit","t":"client-credit\"> If the client paid more than they owed on earlier invoices, a blue banner appears at the top of Billed To on a new invoice: 💳 Client has ₹… credit , with the invoices the overpayment came from. Choose how much to use Type an amount in the box, or click Apply full to use as much as this invoice needs. It can never be more than the credit or the invoice total. Check the line under it It says how much will be applied and how much credit will remain. Save The credit is recorded as a payment on this invoice, and taken off the invoices it came from. A message says which ones. Skip ("},{"u":"invoices.html#details","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Invoice Details","t":"details\"> The number, the dates and where the supply happens. Under them are the Ship to box and the order, dispatch and reference details . Field What to know Invoice Number Filled in with the next number for this type. It is only taken when you first save, so an invoice you abandon does not use up a number. If another invoice took it meanwhile, yours gets the next free number and you are told. You can also type your own number, such as the next page of a paper bill book: a number you type is kept. See Invoice number format . Invoice Date Today, unless you change it. A duplicated or converted"},{"u":"invoices.html#lut","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Exports and SEZ supplies under a LUT","t":"lut\"> When the client is abroad (its country is not India) or is an SEZ unit or developer (the SEZ tick on the client), a box appears in Invoice Details: Export under LUT (no IGST) , or SEZ supply under LUT (no IGST) . Ticked : the supply is zero-rated. No IGST (and no cess) is charged, the items keep their GST rate for the returns, and the total is the taxable value. The invoice prints, word for word, the declaration Rule 46 requires: SUPPLY MEANT FOR EXPORT/SUPPLY TO SEZ UNIT OR SEZ DEVELOPER FOR AUTHORISED OPERATIONS UNDER BOND OR LETTER OF UNDERTAKING WITHOUT PAYMENT OF INTEGRATED TAX - LU"},{"u":"invoices.html#ship-to","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Ship to: a different delivery address","t":"ship-to\"> Ship to same as bill-to address is ticked to start, so the invoice has only a BILL TO block. When the goods go somewhere else, such as a site, a warehouse or the client's customer, untick it and fill in: Field What to enter Shipping Address The delivery address, warehouse or consignee location. Can run to two lines. Shipping City The delivery city. Shipping PIN The 6-digit delivery PIN. Shipping State The delivery state. Same as billing state leaves it as the client's state. The invoice then prints a separate SHIP TO block beside BILL TO. The ship-to state does not change the tax CGS"},{"u":"invoices.html#order-details","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Order, dispatch and reference details","t":"order-details\"> At the bottom of Invoice Details, click Order, dispatch & reference details to open a set of optional boxes, the ones a Tally invoice carries. It shows how many are filled, and stays open on an invoice that has any of them. Box For example Work details Supply and installation of high mast lights, scope as per annexure Revision No Rev-1, when you reissue a corrected quotation Vehicle No TS09AB1234 Service period from / to The period a service bill covers, such as a monthly AMC. A warning appears if the end is before the start. Buyer's Order No and Order date The client's purchas"},{"u":"invoices.html#scan-barcode","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Scanning barcodes","t":"scan-barcode\"> With a barcode scanner, each scan adds a product to the invoice. Give your products their barcodes first: see Barcode on the Products page. Click Scan barcode The box at the top of Line Items . Scan The product is added with its price, GST rate and unit. Scan the same product again and its quantity goes up by one; a different product gets its own row. Keep scanning The cursor stays in the box, so you can scan the next item straight away. A code no product has shows No product has barcode … and adds nothing. Add the barcode to the product under Products , then scan again. Scanned"},{"u":"invoices.html#items","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Line Items","t":"items\"> One row for each thing you are selling. The amount for each row and the totals are worked out for you and shown in the preview. Field What to know Item The item name. Typing searches your products by name or HSN and shows up to five, with their HSN and price. Pick one with the mouse, or with ↓ ↑ and Enter . Picking fills in the HSN, selling price, unit and GST rate, and links the row to the product so its stock is counted. You can also type any name that is not a product. HSN/SAC The goods (HSN) or services (SAC) code. GST returns need it. For common codes the app knows the usual GST r"},{"u":"invoices.html#delivery-charges","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Delivery charges","t":"delivery-charges\"> Delivery charges adds one Delivery charges line with SAC 996812. Type the amount in its Rate . The button goes away once the line is there; remove the line with its bin to add it again. Delivery that comes with the goods is a composite supply , taxed like the goods, so the line starts at the highest GST rate among the goods on the invoice (18% if there are none). A note under the buttons says so. Change its GST % if your delivery is a separate service. It counts in the total and in GST returns, and never touches stock. Picking a product in its Item box turns it into an ordin"},{"u":"invoices.html#tax-inclusive","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Prices that already include GST","t":"tax-inclusive\"> If your rates already include GST, such as an MRP or a counter price, tick Prices include tax at the top right of the Line Items card. The box only shows when the invoice charges GST. The GST is then worked out backwards from each rate: a ₹1,180 item at 18% is ₹1,000 taxable value plus ₹180 GST. The printed Subtotal is the value before tax, so Subtotal + tax = Total, and the client pays exactly the price you typed."},{"u":"invoices.html#discounts","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Discounts","t":"discounts\"> There are two kinds, and they do different things to the GST. On a line (before tax) In the row's Discount box, type the amount and choose ₹ or % in the small list beside it. For a ₹ amount, a second list chooses what it comes off: Choice Means Example: 10 pcs at ₹100, 18% GST, discount 50 Net ₹ off the row's total (quantity × rate). The default. ₹50 off ₹1,000: taxable ₹950 Unit ₹ off each unit. ₹50 × 10 = ₹500 off: taxable ₹500 W/Tax ₹ off the total including tax, so the client's total drops by exactly that much. ₹50 off ₹1,180: taxable about ₹957.63 A % discount is a percentage "},{"u":"invoices.html#gst","p":"Making an invoice","s":"How GST is worked out","t":"gst\"> You never choose between CGST, SGST and IGST. The app decides from your state and the place of supply (the client's state, unless you set Place of Supply): Situation Charged as Client in your state CGST + SGST, half each Client in another state IGST Within a Union Territory without a legislature (Chandigarh, Ladakh, Lakshadweep, Andaman and Nicobar, Dadra and Nagar Haveli and Daman and Diu) CGST + UTGST SEZ client IGST Client outside India (an export) IGST, unless you set an Indian state as Place of Supply (goods delivered in India for a foreign buyer) If a state is blank, the first two "},{"u":"invoices.html#reverse-charge","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Reverse charge","t":"reverse-charge\"> Under reverse charge (RCM), the buyer pays the GST to the government instead of you, under section 9(3) or 9(4). Common cases are goods transport (GTA) services, legal services from an advocate, and supplies from an unregistered person to a registered one. Ask your CA whether it applies. Open Customize Click Customize in the toolbar. Tick reverse charge Under Compliance flags (India) , tick Reverse Charge applies (Section 9(3)/9(4)) — recipient pays GST . Check the preview The invoice now says Reverse Charge: Yes and prints a notice that the recipient pays the GST. The GST is "},{"u":"invoices.html#tds-tcs","p":"Making an invoice","s":"TDS and TCS","t":"tds-tcs\"> Both are in the Customize panel, for Indian businesses. They show unless your business type hides them; the switch is TDS / TCS in Settings, Features . An invoice that already has TDS or TCS keeps its box, so it can still be changed. TCS , tax you collect from the client, is added to the invoice total. See TCS . TDS , tax your client deducts when paying you, is for information: the total does not change. See TDS . Each has a section list and a Rate % box beside it. Picking a section fills in its usual rate; you can type another rate. TDS is worked out on the value before GST, as CBDT"},{"u":"invoices.html#tcs","p":"Making an invoice","s":"TCS: tax collected at source","t":"tcs\"> Tick TCS — Tax Collected at Source (marked Adds to invoice total ), then pick the section: Section Starting rate Worked out on CGST 52 — E-commerce operator 0.5% (since 10 July 2024; it was 1%. Invoices made earlier keep their rate) The taxable value, without GST 206C(1) — Tendu leaves / scrap / minerals (varies) 1% (type the right rate for your goods) The amount including GST Custom rate Type it The amount including GST The TCS prints as its own line and is added to the total. Section 206C(1H), TCS on sale of goods, was removed from 1 April 2025, so new invoices cannot choose it; invoic"},{"u":"invoices.html#tds","p":"Making an invoice","s":"TDS: tax deducted at source","t":"tds\"> Tick TDS — Tax Deducted at Source (marked Buyer deducts; informational ), then pick the section your client deducts under: Section Starting rate 194Q — Purchase of goods (buyer turnover ₹10cr) 0.1%, only above ₹50 lakh a year 194C — Contractor / sub-contractor 1% 194C — Contractor (company) 2% 194J — Professional / technical services 10% 194J — Technical services (lower rate) 2% 194I — Rent (land / building) 10% 194I — Rent (plant / machinery) 2% 194H — Commission / brokerage 5% 194O — E-commerce participant 1% 195 — Payments to non-residents (varies) Type it Custom section / rate Type i"},{"u":"invoices.html#currency","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Billing in another currency","t":"currency\"> If you bill clients abroad, you can make the invoice in their currency: US dollars, euros, pounds, dirhams and the other currencies of the countries the app supports. Where the currency box is A Currency box (for example $ USD ) sits in the Invoice Details card, next to the dates, when any of these is true: Settings, Region is International or Both / Auto . The client's country is not India. The invoice is already in a currency other than rupees. If your Region is India only and you bill an Indian client in rupees, the box stays out of the way. It is always in Customize at the top o"},{"u":"invoices.html#terms-notes","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Terms & Conditions, notes and a private note","t":"terms-notes\"> The fourth card holds three boxes: the Terms that print at the foot of the invoice, Notes / Remarks for the client, and a Private Note only you see. Terms A text box with a small toolbar: B , I , U , • List , 1. List , H for a heading, ¶ for a normal paragraph, 🔗 to turn the selected words into a link, and ✕ to clear formatting. You can paste from Word or Google Docs. Insert preset (by business type) fills in India-specific starter wording: Generic SME / Trader, Freelancer / Consultant, Manufacturer / Wholesale, Retail Shop, Restaurant / Café, IT / Software Services, Constructio"},{"u":"invoices.html#terms-layout","p":"Making an invoice","s":"PDF layout: Compact or Formatted","t":"terms-layout\"> On the right of the Terms & Conditions title, PDF layout chooses how the terms and notes print: Choice Prints Good for Compact Small footer text, to save paper Standard boilerplate terms on goods invoices Formatted Larger, readable paragraphs with lists kept Long service terms, scope and payment schedules Until you choose, the layout follows Print Settings , and a Services invoice starts as Formatted."},{"u":"invoices.html#private-note","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Private Note (not shown on invoice)","t":"private-note\"> The yellow box at the bottom of the card is only for you, such as Client asked for 15-day credit, follow up on 20th, referred by Ravi . It is saved with the invoice but never prints or goes to the client. On the Dashboard, a yellow note icon next to the client shows it."},{"u":"invoices.html#extra-pages","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Additional Pages / Sections","t":"extra-pages\"> Extra pages printed after the invoice, such as a scope of work, a delivery timeline, a warranty card or a price breakup. Each section prints as its own page in the PDF. Add a section Click Add Section at the top right of the card. Give it a title For example Scope of Work or Delivery Timeline . It prints as the page heading. Write or paste the content Type, or paste formatted text, lists and tables from Word or Google Docs; the formatting is kept. Order them The up and down arrows move a section. The red bin removes it. Removing a section is immediate The bin does not ask first a"},{"u":"invoices.html#preview","p":"Making an invoice","s":"The live preview","t":"preview\"> The Live preview on the right shows the invoice exactly as it will print, with the paper size, style and options you chose, and updates as you type. − and + zoom out and in from 50% to 200%, and Fit fits it to the width of the space. The zoom is remembered. A cancelled invoice shows CANCELLED across it; a proforma shows a faint ESTIMATE. On a thermal paper size the preview is a narrow receipt. Full view opens the whole page in the print preview window, with Print and Download PDF . To give the form more room, click Hide Preview in the toolbar. If something prints differently from the"},{"u":"invoices.html#before-saving","p":"Making an invoice","s":"What must be filled in","t":"before-saving\"> A new invoice needs a client name and at least one item with a name, a quantity and a rate. Otherwise Save , Save & Download and Print stop with Add a client name before saving. or Add at least one item with a quantity and rate before saving. Click the amber Draft — click to complete badge in the toolbar to jump to what is missing. This is so a blank invoice never takes an invoice number: GST expects numbers without gaps."},{"u":"invoices.html#save-download","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Save & Download","t":"save-download\"> Save & Download (or Ctrl + P ) does all of this in one go: Saves the invoice, giving a new invoice its number, and counts it as printed once more. Downloads the PDF, showing that saved number, named after the type and number, such as INV_INV-2026-27-0001.pdf . Keeps a copy of the PDF in the app's Saved Invoices folder, in a folder for that client and month. Uploads it to Google Drive, if you have connected Drive in Settings . Prints it, if auto-print is on in Print Settings or for this client. Saving takes the items out of stock, for rows picked from your products; saving again"},{"u":"invoices.html#print","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Printing","t":"print\"> On A4, A5 and other sheet sizes , Print saves the invoice, makes a sharp print copy and opens your browser's print window, which has its own page preview. On a thermal paper size , it first shows a Print preview of the receipt, with Print , Download PDF and Cancel . See Thermal receipt printing . Printing saves the invoice first, like Save & Download , so what you hand the client is always in your records with the same number. Something wrong? Nothing happens, or \"Print failed — try Download PDF instead\". Allow pop-ups for the app, or download the PDF and print that. See Print does not"},{"u":"invoices.html#whatsapp","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Sending on WhatsApp","t":"whatsapp\"> WhatsApp opens WhatsApp with this message typed in: the invoice number, date, client, subtotal and total, and your business name. If the client is saved with a phone number, the chat opens with them; otherwise you choose the contact. It does not save the invoice. From the invoice screen the PDF is not attached. Download it with Save & Download and drag it into the chat. The WhatsApp button on the Dashboard can attach the PDF on phones."},{"u":"invoices.html#eway-bill","p":"Making an invoice","s":"E-way bill","t":"eway-bill\"> An e-way bill is generally needed when goods worth more than ₹50,000 are moved. For tax invoices and delivery challans, E-Way Bill downloads a file, such as EWB-INV-2026-27-0001.json , in the format the NIC e-way bill portal accepts. Upload it there with its JSON upload option instead of typing everything again. The app makes the file; the e-way bill number itself comes from the portal (see what the app does not do ). Turn it on The button shows only while E-way bill is on in Settings, Features . Save the invoice first The file uses the number on screen, so save first to be sure it"},{"u":"invoices.html#autosave","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Saving as you go","t":"autosave\"> What you type is kept while the browser tab stays open. If you leave the screen by mistake and come back, the invoice is still there. A new invoice (or a duplicate or conversion) is not stored in your records until you first click Save , Save & Download or Print . It takes its number only then. After that, changes are saved automatically about two seconds after you stop typing. The badge beside Back tells you where you are: Badge Means Draft — click to complete (amber) A new invoice still missing a client name or an item. Click it to jump to the first missing box. Not saved yet Read"},{"u":"invoices.html#leaving","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Leaving with unsaved changes","t":"leaving\"> If you click Back after changing an invoice that has a client and an item, an Unsaved changes window asks what to do: Button What it does Keep editing Closes the window and stays on the invoice. Esc does the same. Discard & leave Leaves without saving. A new invoice that was never saved is gone, and its number is not used. On a saved invoice, only the changes since the last automatic save are lost. Save & leave Saves, then goes back. A new invoice takes its number now. If the save fails, you stay on the page so you can try again. Closing or reloading the browser tab asks too, with th"},{"u":"invoices.html#keyboard","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Keyboard shortcuts on this screen","t":"keyboard\"> Ctrl + S Save (once the invoice has a client and an item; before that the browser's own save window may open, just close it) Ctrl + P Save and download the PDF (not print) Ctrl + Enter Add an item row Ctrl + Shift + D Duplicate the last row Enter in the last row Add a row ↑ ↓ Enter Pick from the client or product suggestions Esc Close suggestions or a dialog On a Mac, use ⌘ instead of Ctrl . More shortcuts: Shortcuts, search and notifications ."},{"u":"invoices.html#read-only","p":"Making an invoice","s":"When an invoice cannot be changed","t":"read-only\"> Two kinds of document open read-only, with a blue note at the top: A cancelled invoice : This invoice is cancelled and read-only . Undo the cancel on the Dashboard to change it. A quotation, proforma or challan already converted : Converted to INV/…. This copy is read-only . You can still download or print them. Nothing is saved automatically, and Save explains why. To make a new document from one, use Duplicate on the Dashboard. An invoice with an IRN (e-invoice) shows an amber note instead: changes made here are not sent to the e-invoice portal. To correct an e-invoice, cancel it"},{"u":"invoices.html#credit-note","p":"Making an invoice","s":"How to make a credit note","t":"credit-note\"> Start a new invoice Choose Credit Note as the type. Point it at the original In Original Invoice Reference , enter the number of the invoice it corrects. Enter what is being credited Add the returned items, or the price difference, with the same GST rates as the original. Save Its total is subtracted from your sales on the Dashboard, returned goods go back into stock, and it goes into GSTR-1 as a credit note."},{"u":"invoices.html#proforma-to-invoice","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Turning a quote into an invoice","t":"proforma-to-invoice\"> When a client accepts a Quotation or a Proforma / Estimate, click Convert to Tax Invoice on it in the Dashboard. A new tax invoice opens with the same client and items, and gets its own number when you save it. The same works for a delivery challan. Once saved, the original shows Converted and its Convert button goes away, so it cannot be turned into a second invoice by mistake."},{"u":"invoices.html#cancel","p":"Making an invoice","s":"Cancelling an invoice","t":"cancel\"> An invoice number, once issued, has to stay in your records, so a saved invoice is cancelled rather than deleted. Cancel it from the Dashboard : it keeps its number, prints with CANCELLED across it, drops out of your totals and GST returns, and its stock goes back. To correct an invoice already sent to a client, the GST way is a credit note rather than a cancellation."},{"u":"invoice-options.html","p":"Customize panel","s":"Customize: what prints and how","t":"The Customize panel on the invoice screen: title, currency, style, colour, every show-or-hide option, paper size and thermal settings, and exactly what each part of the printed invoice shows."},{"u":"invoice-options.html#remembered","p":"Customize panel","s":"Your choices become the default","t":"remembered\"> Open the panel with Customize in the invoice toolbar. Whatever you change here is used for this invoice and remembered for your next new invoice , including the title, reverse charge, TDS and TCS. If a setting was only meant for one invoice, change it back afterwards. A saved invoice keeps the options it was saved with. These are per-invoice settings. The app-wide look, such as fonts, watermarks, copies and translated labels, is in Print and PDF settings . The Customize panel opens inside the Invoice Type card."},{"u":"invoice-options.html#title-currency","p":"Customize panel","s":"Title, currency and exchange rate","t":"title-currency\"> The first three boxes at the top of the Customize panel. Box What it does Invoice Title Replaces the printed title, such as TAX INVOICE. The box shows the type's own title in grey; leave it blank to use that. Useful for wording such as INVOICE CUM CHALLAN . Thermal receipts ignore it. Currency The same box as in Invoice Details. See Billing in another currency . 1 USD = ? INR Only for currencies other than rupees: how many rupees one unit was worth on the invoice date, such as 84.10. Kept with the invoice; returns and reports use it. A custom title is remembered for your next "},{"u":"invoice-options.html#recurring","p":"Customize panel","s":"Make this a recurring invoice","t":"recurring\"> Tick 🔁 Make this a recurring invoice to have the app create this invoice again on a schedule, with the same client, items and amounts, a fresh number and that day's date. Good for rent, retainers, AMCs and subscriptions. Box What to enter Frequency Weekly, Monthly (the default), Quarterly or Yearly Every N (interval) 1 to 12. Monthly with 3 means every three months. Next invoice date When the first copy is made. Starts one month after this invoice's date (31 January becomes 28 February, not 3 March). End condition Never (until I stop it) ; On a specific date , which adds a Stop ge"},{"u":"invoice-options.html#tds-tcs-account","p":"Customize panel","s":"TCS, TDS and the payment account","t":"tds-tcs-account\"> TCS — Tax Collected at Source and TDS — Tax Deducted at Source : see TCS and TDS . Payment account on this invoice : which bank account and UPI ID print. See below ."},{"u":"invoice-options.html#payment-account","p":"Customize panel","s":"Payment account on this invoice","t":"payment-account\"> If you have saved bank accounts in Settings, Bank accounts and UPI , this list chooses which one prints in the bank block and the UPI QR. Each is shown by its label and bank, with ⭐ before your default. With no accounts saved, the list is not shown. New invoices start with your ⭐ default account (or, with no default, the one you used last). The preview changes as soon as you pick another account. The bank details and UPI ID are copied onto the invoice when you save it, so editing or removing the account in Settings later never changes an invoice you have already sent."},{"u":"invoice-options.html#style","p":"Customize panel","s":"PDF style and accent colour","t":"style\"> PDF Style picks the design. Hover over a chip for a one-line description. The preview changes straight away. Style Look Classic Clean, with a coloured bar across the top. The default. Modern A solid colour block behind your business name, with the logo in white. Minimal Simple, with no borders. Boxed grid Every section in ruled boxes: your name large at the top, seller and document details side by side, Billing To and Shipping To, a Work Details line, and an item table filled with empty rows to a fixed height, like a printed quotation pad. Tally style The Tally layout: reference and di"},{"u":"invoice-options.html#accent-colour","p":"Customize panel","s":"Accent Color","t":"accent-colour\"> The row of round swatches sets the colour of headings, bars and lines on the invoice. Auto , the multicoloured swatch, gives each type its own colour, such as blue for tax invoices, purple for proformas, teal for bills of supply and red for credit notes, so you can tell them apart at a glance. The default. The other eight are fixed colours: blue, purple, teal, red, orange, green, sky and dark. Hover over one to see its name. Pick one to use it on every type, for example to match your logo. The chosen swatch has a white ring inside it. The colour is remembered for your next invo"},{"u":"invoice-options.html#show-hide","p":"Customize panel","s":"Showing and hiding parts of the invoice","t":"show-hide\"> Below the style, the panel lists tick boxes in groups. Each one shows or hides one part of the printed invoice. Hiding something never deletes it: tick it again and it comes back. Each group title has its own ? that opens the part below about it. Group Options Off to start Header & branding Logo, Business name, Business address, Business phone, Business email, Business state, Tax ID (GSTIN/VAT/etc.) Client / Bill-to Client address, Client phone, Client email, Place of Supply Invoice meta Invoice number, Invoice date, Due date Items table HSN/SAC column, Qty column, Unit suffix (nex"},{"u":"invoice-options.html#show-header","p":"Customize panel","s":"Header & branding","t":"show-header\"> Your side of the top of the invoice: Logo , Business name , Business address , Business phone , Business email , Business state and Tax ID (GSTIN/VAT/etc.) . All on to start. The logo, name and address come from Settings . Business state off also hides the client's state, on the invoice and in the Billed To card. Tax ID off also hides the client's GSTIN, on the invoice and in the Billed To card. A GST tax invoice must show both GSTINs, so keep it on for tax invoices. Using a printed letterhead? Turn the header items off, or set a letterhead in Print Settings ."},{"u":"invoice-options.html#show-client","p":"Customize panel","s":"Client / Bill-to","t":"show-client\"> Client address , Client phone , Client email and Place of Supply , in the BILL TO block. All on to start. The client's name always prints. Place of Supply off also hides the Place of Supply box in Invoice Details; the tax then follows the client's state. Choosing a type without GST turns it off for you."},{"u":"invoice-options.html#show-meta","p":"Customize panel","s":"Invoice meta","t":"show-meta\"> Invoice number , Invoice date and Due date on the invoice's side of the header. All on to start. A GST tax invoice must show its number and date, so keep those on. The due date only prints when one is set."},{"u":"invoice-options.html#show-items","p":"Customize panel","s":"Items table","t":"show-items\"> Option Turning it off HSN/SAC column Hides the column on the invoice and the HSN/SAC box in each row of the form. GST rules require HSN for most businesses, so keep it on for tax invoices. Qty column Hides the quantity column on the invoice (the unit goes with it). The form keeps its Qty box. Useful for a fixed-fee job billed as quantity 1. Unit (Hrs, Nos...) next to Qty Prints \"5\" instead of \"5 Hrs\". In Classic, Modern, Minimal and on thermal receipts the unit is part of the Qty column; in Boxed grid the UNIT column goes away, and in Tally style the \"per\" column goes away. It tur"},{"u":"invoice-options.html#show-totals","p":"Customize panel","s":"Totals","t":"show-totals\"> Subtotal row : the value of the items before tax. Amount in words : the total written out in words, in the invoice's currency. Round-off line : rounds the grand total to the nearest rupee and shows the difference. The default for new invoices is set in Print & PDF ; a saved invoice keeps what it was saved with. HSN/SAC tax summary table : the tax grouped by HSN code and rate, as on a Tally invoice. On to start only in Tally style. Tax amount in words : the total GST in words. On to start only in Tally style."},{"u":"invoice-options.html#show-footer","p":"Customize panel","s":"Footer","t":"show-footer\"> Option What it prints Bank details The BANK DETAILS block from the payment account , with your PAN. Off hides the PAN too. Show \"Pay via: account \" label The account's label above the bank block. Off to start. UPI QR (rupee invoices) A Scan to pay QR with the amount filled in. Needs a UPI ID on the account and a rupee invoice. Signature block Your signature and stamp, uploaded in Settings . Prints only when one is uploaded. Show \"Authorized Signatory\" caption The words under the signature. Terms & Conditions, Notes / Remarks What you typed in the Terms & Conditions card . Note: s"},{"u":"invoice-options.html#system-generated-note","p":"Customize panel","s":"The \"system-generated invoice\" note","t":"system-generated-note\"> In the Footer group, Note: system-generated invoice adds this line below the terms: Note: This is a system-generated invoice. No signature or stamp is required. It is off unless you turn it on. If you use it, consider turning the signature block off too, so the invoice does not contradict itself."},{"u":"invoice-options.html#paper-size","p":"Customize panel","s":"Paper size","t":"paper-size\"> Option Size A4 Portrait (default) 210 × 297 mm A4 Landscape 297 × 210 mm A5 Portrait (compact) 148 × 210 mm A5 Landscape (2 per A4 sheet) 210 × 148 mm US Letter 216 × 279 mm US Legal 216 × 356 mm B5 176 × 250 mm 80mm Thermal (POS receipt) 72 mm printable 76mm Thermal (kitchen printer) 68 mm printable 58mm Thermal (compact / mobile) 48 mm printable 112mm Thermal (wide receipt) 104 mm printable Custom size Width 30 to 500 mm, height 50 to 1200 mm For a custom size, enter the printer's printable width, not the roll width. Anything under 100 mm wide prints as a receipt. The quick butt"},{"u":"invoice-options.html#thermal-options","p":"Customize panel","s":"Thermal printer settings","t":"thermal-options\"> When a thermal size is chosen (or a custom size under 100 mm wide), a Thermal printer settings box appears under the paper size: Font size Small (fits more per page), Medium (recommended, the default) or Large (easier to read) Compact mode Tighter item rows, to save paper on long orders. Off to start. Whether HSN and the quantity × rate line print is set in Print Settings. Cut mark at bottom Prints a CUT HERE line to tear against. On to start. Turn it off if your printer cuts the paper itself. More receipt settings are in Print Settings . See also Thermal receipt printing ."},{"u":"invoice-options.html#printed-header","p":"Customize panel","s":"What prints: the header","t":"printed-header\"> Your side : logo, business name, address with city and PIN, state, GSTIN, email and phone. Each can be hidden. The invoice's side : the title; for a proforma, \"This is not a tax invoice\"; for a credit note, \"Against Invoice\" and the original number; then the number, date and due date; and, for tax invoices and credit notes in India, Reverse Charge Yes or No. With a letterhead set in Print Settings, the header is replaced by your letterhead."},{"u":"invoice-options.html#printed-parties","p":"Customize panel","s":"What prints: Bill To, Ship To and Place of Supply","t":"printed-parties\"> BILL TO : the client's name, address, state, GSTIN, email and phone. SHIP TO : only when a different delivery address is entered. PLACE OF SUPPLY : the state, with Interstate (IGST) or Intrastate (CGST + SGST) beside it."},{"u":"invoice-options.html#printed-items","p":"Customize panel","s":"What prints: the items table","t":"printed-items\"> Columns, left to right: # , Description (with its longer note underneath), HSN/SAC , Qty with the unit, Rate , Disc. (only when a line has a discount), the tax columns, and Amount . Within your state: CGST and SGST , each with its rate and amount. Another state: one IGST column. Outside India: one column with the local tax name, such as VAT. Amount is the line's value after discount and before tax. The tax is in the columns beside it."},{"u":"invoice-options.html#printed-totals","p":"Customize panel","s":"What prints: the totals","t":"printed-totals\"> On the left, the amount in words and a Scan to pay (UPI) QR code with your UPI ID and the amount. The QR only prints on rupee invoices, with a UPI ID set and a total above zero. On the right, in order: Subtotal, Discount, CGST and SGST or IGST, GST Cess, TCS, Discount on total, Round-off, and Total Due . For a credit note, the last line reads Credit Amount . With TDS, Less: TDS and Net Receivable follow."},{"u":"invoice-options.html#printed-footer","p":"Customize panel","s":"What prints: notices and footer","t":"printed-footer\"> Reverse charge notice , when turned on. Composition declaration , always on composition bills: \"Composition taxable person, not eligible to collect tax on supplies.\" BANK DETAILS : \"Pay via\" label if on, account name, bank, account number and type, IFSC, SWIFT, and your PAN. EXCHANGE RATE , on foreign-currency invoices. TERMS & CONDITIONS and NOTES , compact or formatted. Signature block : your signature and stamp side by side, \"Authorized Signatory\", and your business name. It only prints when a signature or stamp has been uploaded. Export and SEZ invoices print no LUT declar"},{"u":"invoice-options.html#watermarks","p":"Customize panel","s":"Watermarks","t":"watermarks\"> CANCELLED , in red, on a cancelled invoice. ESTIMATE , very faint, on a proforma. Your own watermark, copy labels such as ORIGINAL and DUPLICATE, REPRINT, page numbers and QR codes come from Print Settings , and only on sheet paper, not receipts."},{"u":"thermal-printing.html","p":"Thermal receipts","s":"Thermal receipt printing","t":"Printing bills on a 58 mm or 80 mm receipt printer at a shop counter, from setting it up to what the receipt shows."},{"u":"thermal-printing.html#setup","p":"Thermal receipts","s":"Setting it up","t":"setup\"> Install the printer in Windows Use the driver that came with it, set the paper size in the driver to your roll width, and make it your default printer, or pick it in the print window each time. Choose the receipt size On an invoice, open Customize and set Paper / print size to 80mm Thermal or 58mm Thermal . The app remembers it for your next invoice. Try a test print In Print Settings , pick the Thermal (80mm) preview tab and click Test Print . Print a real bill Save the invoice, then click Print . A preview of the receipt opens; click Print again. Picking the Retail Shop or Restaurant"},{"u":"thermal-printing.html#print-preview","p":"Thermal receipts","s":"The print preview","t":"print-preview\"> On a receipt size, Print shows the receipt at 160% so you can read it. Its buttons: Print Sends it to the printer. Shows \"Sending…\" while it works. Download PDF Saves and downloads a PDF instead, the same as Save & Download. Cancel Closes it. So does Esc ."},{"u":"thermal-printing.html#auto-print","p":"Thermal receipts","s":"Printing straight after saving","t":"auto-print\"> At a busy counter, turn on Auto-print on save : Save & Download then prints the receipt as well, with no extra click. It can also be turned on for just one client, in their details."},{"u":"thermal-printing.html#receipt-contents","p":"Thermal receipts","s":"What a receipt shows","t":"receipt-contents\"> Your logo (if turned on in Print Settings), business name in capitals, tagline, address, GSTIN and phone. The document type, such as TAX INVOICE, then the invoice number, reverse charge, date, and the client's name, GSTIN and phone. Each item: its name, then quantity × rate, GST rate and HSN, with the amount on the right. The amount is quantity × rate, before discount and tax. Subtotal, discount, CGST, SGST or IGST, cess, round-off and TOTAL . Amount in words, bank details, a UPI QR code with \"Scan to pay via UPI\", and notes. Your footer message, such as \"Thank you for your "},{"u":"thermal-printing.html#not-on-receipts","p":"Thermal receipts","s":"What a receipt leaves out","t":"not-on-receipts\"> To fit a narrow roll, receipts do not print: terms and conditions, the signature and stamp, extra pages, the due date, place of supply, client address, TCS, TDS, whole-bill discount lines, the exchange rate, watermarks, the reverse charge and composition notices, or the PDF style and colour. The custom invoice title is not used either. If you need any of these, print that invoice on A4 or A5 instead."},{"u":"thermal-printing.html#receipt-settings","p":"Thermal receipts","s":"Changing how receipts look","t":"receipt-settings\"> Font, boldness, capitals, spacing, darkness, what is shown, the QR size, the footer message, the cut mark and feed lines are all in Print Settings, Thermal receipts ."},{"u":"thermal-printing.html#receipt-problems","p":"Thermal receipts","s":"When a receipt prints badly","t":"receipt-problems\"> Problem Try Text is cut off on the right Use a smaller printable width: most 80 mm printers print 72 mm, and most 58 mm printers print 48 mm. Use Custom size if yours differs. Print is faint Set Font weight to Bold or Ultra bold, and Thermal ink darkness to Dark. The printer jams or stops half-way Turn on Buffer-safe mode . Blurry text, or nothing prints Set Thermal print method to Via PDF . Paper does not feed far enough to tear Increase Feed lines after cut ."},{"u":"dashboard.html","p":"Dashboard","s":"Dashboard","t":"Your invoices at a glance: what you have sold, what you are owed, what is overdue, and every action you can take on an invoice."},{"u":"dashboard.html#header","p":"Dashboard","s":"At the top","t":"header\"> The Dashboard is the first screen you see. It lists every invoice of the business selected in the sidebar, with the totals above and the actions on each row. If you run more than one business, switch business in the sidebar and the Dashboard shows only that business's invoices straight away. An old invoice that cannot be matched to any business is shown under every business, so nothing is ever hidden. The count beside the title (for example 42 invoices ) is every document of that business: tax invoices, quotations, proformas, challans, credit notes and cancelled invoices too. The butt"},{"u":"dashboard.html#welcome-card","p":"Dashboard","s":"The welcome note","t":"welcome-card\"> A new install shows a large note at the top: Welcome to Reazix Billing . It says the app is yours for life with one payment, your data stays on your own computer and works offline, your purchase includes 3 years of updates, and help is one email away. Button What it does Help & Support Opens Help & Support , with our email address. Start billing or ✕ Closes the note for good on this computer and browser. It shows only while the business has fewer than 10 documents."},{"u":"dashboard.html#getting-started","p":"Dashboard","s":"The Getting started list","t":"getting-started\"> A new install also shows four things to do before the app is really useful. Each one ticks itself off when it is really done (the app checks what is saved, not whether you opened a screen), and has a button that takes you there. The top right shows how many are done, such as 2 of 4 done . Step Done when Button Add your business details A business name is saved Open Settings Make your first invoice Any invoice exists Start Add your products or services At least one product is saved Open (opens Products) Add bank details or UPI A bank account or UPI ID is saved Open Settings Bu"},{"u":"dashboard.html#overdue","p":"Dashboard","s":"Overdue invoices and reminders","t":"overdue\"> An invoice is overdue when its due date has passed and it is not fully paid. Each time the Dashboard opens, every Unpaid or Partial tax invoice, bill of supply or composition bill whose Due Date is before today is marked Overdue for you. Quotations, proformas, challans and credit notes are never overdue, and neither is a cancelled invoice or one with no due date. When at least one invoice is overdue, a red banner shows above the totals, for example 3 overdue invoices — ₹41,300 outstanding . The amount is what is still owed on them (less any TDS the client deducts); foreign-currency i"},{"u":"dashboard.html#remind-all","p":"Dashboard","s":"Send Payment Reminders","t":"remind-all\"> Remind All on the red banner opens this window. It lists every overdue invoice on its own line: the client, the invoice number, the balance still owed in red (or Overpaid ₹… in blue if the client paid too much), and the client's phone number when one is saved. Pick a client Click Remind on their line. WhatsApp opens In a new tab, with the client's chat and a polite message already written, such as \"Hi Sharma Traders, this is a gentle reminder that Invoice INV/0012 for ₹11,800 was due on 5/9/2026. Kindly arrange the payment at your earliest convenience. Thank you! - Your Business\"."},{"u":"dashboard.html#totals","p":"Dashboard","s":"The four totals","t":"totals\"> The four cards under the banner add up your sales. They cover only the business selected in the sidebar, and only real sales : Tax invoices, bills of supply and composition bills count . Credit notes are subtracted (money given back to clients). Quotations, proforma estimates and delivery challans are left out : they are not sales yet. Cancelled invoices are left out . The totals are for all years together and do not follow the filters on the invoice list. For one month, quarter or year, use Reports or GST Returns . Sales in a foreign currency get a line of their own on each card (for"},{"u":"dashboard.html#total-invoiced","p":"Dashboard","s":"Total Invoiced","t":"total-invoiced\"> The grand total of your sales, including GST : the final amount printed on each invoice, added up, less credit notes. It is what you have billed, not what you have received. When you bill in more than one currency, each currency has its own line, and a small line under them gives ≈ ₹ in all : every invoice in rupees at its own exchange rate. Invoices without a rate are left out of that line and counted beside it."},{"u":"dashboard.html#tax-collected","p":"Dashboard","s":"Tax Collected","t":"tax-collected\"> The GST on those sales: CGST + SGST (or UTGST) on sales within your state, IGST on sales to other states, and cess, less the GST on credit notes. This is tax you collected for the government, not your income. Bills of supply and composition bills carry no GST, so they add nothing here. For what you actually have to pay after input tax credit (ITC, the GST you paid on purchases), see GSTR-3B ."},{"u":"dashboard.html#outstanding","p":"Dashboard","s":"Outstanding","t":"outstanding\"> What clients still owe you: for every sale not marked Paid, the invoice total less any TDS the client deducts (see TDS and TCS ), less what has been received. An overpaid invoice counts as zero here, not as a minus. Credit notes are not taken off this card. To see who owes what and for how long, use Reports, Outstanding & Aging or a client's account ."},{"u":"dashboard.html#invoice-count","p":"Dashboard","s":"Invoices","t":"invoice-count\"> How many sales documents the totals are made of: tax invoices, bills of supply, composition bills and credit notes, not cancelled. It is usually smaller than the count beside the Dashboard title, which also counts quotations, challans and cancelled invoices. Something wrong? A total looks too high or too low? Check the business selected in the sidebar first. Then look for a quotation or challan that should have been converted to a tax invoice (they do not count until converted), or a wrong invoice that should be cancelled (see Cancelling an invoice )."},{"u":"dashboard.html#low-stock","p":"Dashboard","s":"Low stock","t":"low-stock\"> If low-stock alerts are on in Settings (they are on to start, with a limit of 5), every product whose stock is at or below your limit is listed in one line under Low stock (n) , where n is how many there are. Each shows the product name, its HSN code if it has one, and either Out of Stock in red (0 or less) or Stock: 3 in amber. When the list is wider than the screen, it scrolls past slowly like a news ticker; point at it with the mouse to stop it. A short list stays still. If your computer is set to reduce motion, it does not move and you scroll it sideways instead. Click any prod"},{"u":"dashboard.html#invoice-list","p":"Dashboard","s":"Finding an invoice","t":"invoice-list\"> The Invoices card lists every document of the business, newest first. Above the list are the filters. They work together: for example \"Overdue\" and \"FY 2026-27\" shows only this year's overdue invoices. Filter What it does Search client or invoice... Type part of a client's name or of an invoice number, such as sharma or 0012 . Capital letters do not matter. All Years Pick one financial year (1 April to 31 March). All Types Pick one document type: Tax Invoice, Quotation, Proforma / Estimate, Bill of Supply (No GST), Composition (Bill of Supply), Credit Note or Delivery Challan. A"},{"u":"dashboard.html#columns","p":"Dashboard","s":"Choosing the columns","t":"columns\"> Columns at the right end of the filters opens Pick columns to show . Tick or untick: Column Shows To start Date The invoice date Shown Invoice # The invoice number, with IRN when it has one Shown Type Tax Invoice, Quotation and so on Shown Client The client's name and the private-note icon Shown Amount The invoice total Shown Currency INR, USD and so on, in its own column Hidden Status The status dropdown (see Status ) Shown Due date The due date, or — Hidden Print count How many times it was printed or downloaded, such as 2× Hidden Actions The buttons for each invoice (see What you "},{"u":"dashboard.html#status","p":"Dashboard","s":"Status","t":"status\"> Each sale is Unpaid , Partial (part paid), Paid , Overdue or Cancelled , shown in a coloured dropdown on its row. Recording payments sets it for you: nothing received is Unpaid, some is Partial, the full balance is Paid. Each time the Dashboard opens, unpaid and part-paid invoices past their due date become Overdue, and the row shows how many days late they are. You can also change it yourself from the dropdown: Choose What happens Paid Records a payment for the rest of the balance (mode Other, note \"Marked paid\", today's date), so your payment history, Receipts and reports stay compl"},{"u":"dashboard.html#payments","p":"Dashboard","s":"Recording a payment","t":"payments\"> When a client pays you, by UPI, bank transfer, cash or cheque, record it against the invoice. The status then changes for you, a receipt is made, and the payment appears in Receipts , the client's account and Outstanding . Open it Click the green ₹ button on the invoice's row. The Record Payment window opens. Its top line shows the invoice number, the Total , what is Paid so far, and the Balance (in red while something is owed, green when nothing is). Amount Received Type the amount received. The box shows the balance as a hint; for a full payment, type that amount. Payment Date Tod"},{"u":"dashboard.html#payment-foreign","p":"Dashboard","s":"Payments from abroad","t":"payment-foreign\"> On an invoice billed in another currency (for example US dollars), the Record Payment window has an extra, optional box, Received from abroad : Box What to type Amount Received The amount in the invoice's currency, as before (for example 1,000 USD). This is what marks the invoice paid. Credited to your bank (₹) The rupees that reached your account, from your bank statement. Bank charges (₹) What the banks took on the way, if anything. FIRC / e-BRC number The number on the Foreign Inward Remittance Certificate or e-BRC your bank issues. For an export of services it is the proo"},{"u":"dashboard.html#payment-tds","p":"Dashboard","s":"TDS when recording a payment","t":"payment-tds\"> A business client often pays less than the invoice because it kept back income-tax TDS (for example 10% of the value before GST for professional fees under 194J) and deposited it against your PAN. Record that TDS so the invoice shows Paid instead of Partial for ever. On an Indian tax invoice, bill of supply or composition bill that does not already show TDS, the Record Payment window has a box Client deducted TDS : Tick it Tick Client deducted TDS . A section list and a rate box appear. Section and rate Pick the section the client used (it is on their payment advice or TDS certif"},{"u":"dashboard.html#payment-history","p":"Dashboard","s":"Payment History","t":"payment-history\"> Once an invoice has payments, the Record Payment window lists them under Payment History : date, amount, mode and note. Each line has three buttons: Button What it does Receipt Opens the payment receipt for that payment, to view or print it again. Pencil Opens Edit Payment to correct the amount, date, mode or note. Bin (red) Deletes the payment after asking Delete this payment? . Its receipt is removed from Receipts too. After any change the paid amount and the status are worked out again: deleting the only payment makes the invoice Unpaid again (or Overdue the next time the "},{"u":"dashboard.html#edit-payment","p":"Dashboard","s":"Edit Payment","t":"edit-payment\"> The pencil on a payment opens Edit Payment , showing the invoice number and total. Change the Amount , Date , Mode or Note / reference and click Save changes ; Cancel or ✕ closes it without saving. Use it to fix a typing mistake instead of deleting and recording again. If the new amount takes the total received above the invoice total, you are asked Save as overpayment? first. The receipt in Receipts is updated to match, and keeps its receipt number. A payment made by choosing Paid from the status dropdown becomes an ordinary payment once you edit it, so choosing Unpaid later no"},{"u":"dashboard.html#receipt","p":"Dashboard","s":"The payment receipt","t":"receipt\"> A receipt is the paper you give a client to say you have received their money. It opens by itself after Record Payment , and again from Receipt under Payment History . It shows: Your business name, address, GSTIN, phone and email, as saved on the invoice. PAYMENT RECEIPT , with the Receipt No. (such as RCPT-LZ8K2M4A), Payment Date , Against Invoice , Payment Mode and the Ref / Note if you gave one. \"Received with thanks from\" the client's name, address and phone. The Amount Received , and for rupees the amount in words. The Invoice Total , Total Paid so far, and the Balance still owe"},{"u":"dashboard.html#row-actions","p":"Dashboard","s":"What you can do with an invoice","t":"row-actions\"> The row shows the actions you use most as buttons. The rest are in the ⋯ menu at the end of the row; it closes with Esc or a click elsewhere, and the arrow keys move through it. Action What it does 👁 View Shows the invoice exactly as it prints, without opening the editor. See The print preview . Edit (pencil) Opens it on the invoice screen to change it. See Making an invoice . Undo cancel (curved arrow) Only on a cancelled invoice. See Cancelling an invoice . ₹ Payment Record a payment. See Recording a payment . Convert to Tax Invoice Quotations, proformas and delivery challans "},{"u":"dashboard.html#print-preview","p":"Dashboard","s":"The print preview","t":"print-preview\"> The Print preview window shows an invoice exactly as it will print, on the paper size chosen for it, with the same design, logo, QR code and totals. A cancelled invoice shows CANCELLED across it, and an invoice with an IRN shows the IRN and QR code. It opens in three places: From the 👁 View button on a Dashboard row, for any invoice, to check it without opening the editor. From Full view in the Live preview bar while you make or edit an invoice, on any paper size. See The live preview . From Print on the invoice screen when the invoice is on a receipt (thermal) paper size. On "},{"u":"dashboard.html#share","p":"Dashboard","s":"Sending an invoice by WhatsApp or email","t":"share\"> WhatsApp (in the ⋯ menu) sends a message with the invoice number, date and due date, client, total, what is paid or still due (or \"FULLY PAID\"), the status, and your business name. On a phone or tablet (Chrome or Safari): the app makes the PDF and opens your phone's share menu with it attached. Pick WhatsApp and the client. On a computer : WhatsApp does not let any website attach a file. So the client's chat opens in a new tab with the message, using the phone number saved for them, and the PDF is downloaded to your Downloads folder. Drag that PDF into the chat and send. If no number i"},{"u":"dashboard.html#cancel","p":"Dashboard","s":"Cancelling an invoice","t":"cancel\"> Under GST an invoice number, once issued, must stay in your books, so an issued invoice is cancelled , never deleted. Cancel one that was made by mistake, or for a sale that did not happen. (If goods came back after a real sale, issue a credit note instead.) Choose Cancel invoice In the ⋯ menu on the row, click Cancel invoice . (Choosing Cancelled in the status dropdown does the same at once, without asking.) Confirm The window Cancel this invoice? explains what happens, and that you can undo it with the Undo cancel arrow among the row's actions. Click Cancel invoice to go ahead, or c"},{"u":"dashboard.html#csv","p":"Dashboard","s":"Importing and exporting invoices as CSV","t":"csv\"> For moving many invoices in from Excel, Tally or another program, including old invoices from before you started using the app, or out to your CA, in one go. A CSV file is a plain spreadsheet file that Excel and Google Sheets can open and save. Open it Click CSV import / export at the top of the Dashboard. The window Sales invoices: CSV import / export opens. Start from the template Template downloads Sales-import-template.csv with the right columns and one example invoice of two items. Open it in Excel or Google Sheets, replace the example with your invoices, and save it as CSV (Comma d"},{"u":"dashboard.html#quick-print","p":"Dashboard","s":"Printing many invoices as one PDF","t":"quick-print\"> The Quick print row above the list combines invoices into one PDF file, without ticking anything. It uses the list as it is filtered now , so set the filters first: for example From 1 October To 31 October, then All shown gives October's invoices for your CA. Button Puts in the PDF All shown (n) Every invoice in the list Unpaid only (n) Only those marked Unpaid, not part-paid or overdue Overdue (n) Only overdue ones, for chasing payments Paid (n) Only fully paid ones The number in brackets is how many will go in. Each invoice starts on a new A4 page; a long one takes as many page"},{"u":"dashboard.html#bulk","p":"Dashboard","s":"Ticking several invoices","t":"bulk\"> Tick the box at the start of each row, or the box in the header to tick every row in the list as filtered. For a set of dates, such as one month, fill in From and To in the filters first, then tick the header box. A blue bar appears above the list with how many are ticked, such as 3 selected , and these buttons: Button What it does Mark paid , Mark unpaid , Mark overdue Change them all, after asking. Mark paid records a payment for each balance (note \"Marked paid (bulk)\"); Mark unpaid takes such payments back, as the status dropdown does. Only tax invoices, bills of supply and compositi"},{"u":"dashboard.html#einvoice","p":"Dashboard","s":"E-invoicing from the Dashboard","t":"einvoice\"> E-invoicing is only for businesses whose yearly turnover has crossed ₹5 crore: their B2B invoices must be registered on the government's e-invoice portal, which gives each one an IRN (Invoice Reference Number) and a signed QR code. If that is not you, leave it off. When E-invoicing (IRN) is on in Settings, Features , the Dashboard gets two extra buttons: E-invoice JSON Tick the invoices to register and click E-invoice JSON in the bar. A JSON file downloads with every invoice that passed the checks. Upload it on einvoice1.gst.gov.in (e-Invoice, Bulk Upload). Import IRN Download the r"},{"u":"clients.html","p":"Clients","s":"Clients","t":"Everyone you bill, what each one owes, their account statement, and how quickly they pay."},{"u":"clients.html#client-list","p":"Clients","s":"The client list","t":"client-list\"> Clients in the sidebar opens a list of everyone you sell to. Use it to see at a glance who owes you money, to open one client's account, and to keep their address and GSTIN ready for the next invoice. Every client you have saved, and every name you have ever invoiced, appears as a card. The clients who owe you the most are at the top, so the people to call first are always first. The buttons at the top of the screen: Button What it does Import CSV Adds many clients at once from a spreadsheet. See Importing clients . Add Client Opens the client form for a new client. See Adding an"},{"u":"clients.html#client-card","p":"Clients","s":"What a client card shows","t":"client-card\"> On the card Meaning Letter in a circle The first letter of the name. Name The client's name, exactly as written on the invoices. N invoices | state | GSTIN How many sales and credit notes they have, then the state and GSTIN of a saved client. Total Everything you have billed them, less credit notes. Paid (green) What they have paid you on those invoices. Outstanding (red) What they still owe. TDS that the client deducted is not counted as owed, since they pay it to the government for you. Green ₹0 means all settled. Overpaid (blue) Shown instead of Outstanding when they paid more"},{"u":"clients.html#unsaved-clients","p":"Clients","s":"Names you invoiced but never saved","t":"unsaved-clients\"> An invoice can go to a name that is not in your saved list, for example a walk-in customer. That name still gets a card, so you can see what they owe, but it shows no state or GSTIN. Open the card and click Save as Client at the bottom to save them: the form opens with the name filled in. Something wrong? One client shows as two cards. Cards are matched by name. \"Sharma Traders\" and \"Sharma Traders Pvt Ltd\" are two different names, so they make two cards. If you renamed a saved client, old invoices keep the name they were made with and stay on a card of their own. Small and c"},{"u":"clients.html#client-form","p":"Clients","s":"Adding and editing a client","t":"client-form\"> Save a client once and you never type their details again: on a new invoice, pick them from the list under Client Name and their address, state, GSTIN and preferences are filled in. Open the form Click Add Client at the top of the Clients screen. To change a saved client, open their card and click Edit Client . The same form opens from the invoice screen, from the pencil next to a saved client or when you save a new one there. Fill in the name Client / Business Name is the only required field. Use the name you want printed on the invoice. Address and state Fill in the address, ch"},{"u":"clients.html#foreign-client","p":"Clients","s":"Clients abroad","t":"foreign-client\"> Pick the client's country. For a country other than India: No GSTIN and no state are needed. The state box is marked optional, and the postal code box takes that country's name for it (ZIP Code, Postcode...). The tax ID box is named after their country's tax ID (VAT Number, EIN / TIN, TRN...). If the client gave you one, type it: it prints on the invoice with that name. It is optional. Their country prints under their address, and the place of supply prints as Outside India (country) , because an export is supplied outside India. Preferred currency lists every currency the app"},{"u":"clients.html#client-gstin","p":"Clients","s":"The GSTIN check","t":"client-gstin\"> A GSTIN is the 15-character GST number of a registered business. Its first two digits are the state code (03 is Punjab, 27 is Maharashtra), the next ten are the PAN, and the last is a check character. When you click out of the GSTIN box, the app reads it. This works offline; nothing is looked up on the GST portal. What happens Meaning The State fills in by itself The state was blank, so it was taken from the first two digits. ⚠ GSTIN format looks unusual. Expected like: 22AAAAA0000A1Z5 It is not 15 characters in the GSTIN pattern. Check for a missing or extra character, or the l"},{"u":"clients.html#client-state","p":"Clients","s":"Why the state matters (place of supply)","t":"client-state\"> The place of supply is where a sale is treated as happening for GST. For most sales it is the client's state: Client in your own state : the invoice charges CGST + SGST (half each). Client in another state , an SEZ, or abroad: the invoice charges IGST . A wrong state on the client quietly gives the wrong tax on every invoice to them, and puts the sale in the wrong place in GSTR-1. If goods go somewhere other than the client's address, set Place of Supply on that invoice instead. See How GST is worked out and the glossary . Something wrong? IGST where you expected CGST + SGST, or"},{"u":"clients.html#client-sez","p":"Clients","s":"SEZ clients","t":"client-sez\"> Tick SEZ unit / Developer for a client in a Special Economic Zone. Supplies to them are charged IGST whatever their state, even if they are in your own state (section 16 of the IGST Act). The box only shows when the country is India."},{"u":"clients.html#client-print-prefs","p":"Clients","s":"Print preferences","t":"client-print-prefs\"> Some clients always want the same thing: a thermal receipt, an A5 bill, or an invoice in dollars. Set it once here and every new invoice for them starts that way. All three are optional; leave them blank to use your normal settings. Field What it does Preferred paper size A4, A5, US Letter, 80mm or 76mm thermal and the other sizes. Use app default keeps your usual size. Preferred currency INR, USD, EUR, GBP, AED, SGD or AUD. Use invoice default keeps the invoice's normal currency. Auto-print on save for this client Sends the invoice to the printer each time you save one fo"},{"u":"clients.html#ledger","p":"Clients","s":"A client's account","t":"ledger\"> Click a client's card to open their account. It shows everything about this one client in one place. A client opened, with their invoices, ageing strip and PDFs. From top to bottom: Statement PDF and Aging PDF : see Statement and ageing PDFs . The Aging strip, when they owe you anything: see Ageing . Their address, email and phone, if saved. All their invoices, newest first. Edit Client and Delete Client , or Save as Client . A client with no invoices shows No invoices for this client yet. and a Create Invoice button."},{"u":"clients.html#client-invoices","p":"Clients","s":"The invoice rows","t":"client-invoices\"> Each row has the Date , Invoice No. , Type (Tax Invoice, Quotation, Credit Note and so on), Amount , Status and these buttons: Button What it does Edit Invoice (pencil) Opens the invoice on the invoice screen to change it. Duplicate Invoice A new invoice with the same client and items, a new number and today's date. WhatsApp Opens WhatsApp with a short message: invoice number, amount, date and status. It goes to the phone number saved on that invoice. The PDF is not attached; send it from the invoice screen if you need it (see WhatsApp ). Email Opens your email program with a"},{"u":"clients.html#client-status","p":"Clients","s":"Changing the status","t":"client-status\"> The coloured box in the Status column is a dropdown: Unpaid , Partial , Paid or Overdue . It works as on the Dashboard: Paid records a payment for the rest of the balance, so the client's Paid and Outstanding update. Unpaid on a paid invoice takes back the payment that marking it Paid recorded. Payments you recorded yourself stay. Partial and Overdue only change the label. To record part of a payment with its amount and mode, use the ₹ button on the Dashboard . A cancelled invoice shows Cancelled and cannot be changed here; undo the cancel from the Dashboard. See Status ."},{"u":"clients.html#client-actions","p":"Clients","s":"Edit, delete or save the client","t":"client-actions\"> Button What it does Edit Client Opens the client form with their details. Delete Client Asks Remove this saved client? , then removes them from your saved list. Their invoices stay untouched, and the name still shows as a card while it has invoices. You can add them again any time. Save as Client Shown instead of the two above for a name you invoiced but never saved. Opens the form with the name filled in. Something wrong? WhatsApp opens but not to the client's chat. The phone number on the invoice needs the country code: 919876543210 or +91 98765 43210, not just 98765 43210. "},{"u":"clients.html#ageing","p":"Clients","s":"Ageing: who is slow to pay","t":"ageing\"> When a client owes you money, an Aging strip under the PDF buttons splits what they owe by how late it is: Group Holds unpaid amounts that are Current (green) Not yet due, or up to 30 days past due 31-60d (amber) 31 to 60 days late 61-90d (orange) 61 to 90 days late 90+ d (red) More than 90 days late. Call these first. Lateness is counted from the invoice's due date , or from the invoice date when it has none. Only unpaid sales are counted; TDS the client deducted is not. The strip is hidden when nothing is owed. The strip adds up unpaid invoices one by one, and does not take credit n"},{"u":"clients.html#statement","p":"Clients","s":"Statement and ageing PDFs","t":"statement\"> Two buttons at the top of an opened client make PDFs you can send them or keep. Each one downloads straight away, and you see \"Statement PDF generated\" or \"Aging report for name downloaded\". If you set your own PDF colours in Print Settings , the coloured bands and lines follow them."},{"u":"clients.html#statement-pdf","p":"Clients","s":"Statement PDF","t":"statement-pdf\"> The client's whole account, like a bank passbook. Send it when a client disputes a bill or asks \"how much do I owe?\". It contains: Your business ( FROM ) and theirs ( BILL TO ), with addresses and GSTINs. A summary: Invoices , Total Billed , Paid and Outstanding . A table with Date , Particulars (number and type), Debit , Credit and Balance , oldest first. Each invoice is a debit. Under it, what was paid against it shows as Payment recd against above , and TDS they deducted as TDS deducted by client , both as credits. A credit note is a credit. The running balance after each li"},{"u":"clients.html#aging-pdf","p":"Clients","s":"Aging PDF","t":"aging-pdf\"> Only what is still unpaid, for collection calls. It lists each unpaid invoice with its Invoice # , Date , Due date, Age in days, Total and Outstanding . Amounts more than 60 days old are in red. Below the list, an AGING SUMMARY gives the four groups (0–30, 31–60, 61–90 and 90+ days) and the TOTAL OUTSTANDING . The file is named like Aging-Sharma_Traders-2026-10-29.pdf . Something wrong? \"No invoices for this client\" or \" name has no outstanding balance.\": there is nothing to put in that PDF. A paid-up client has no Aging PDF. Nothing downloads: your browser may be asking where to s"},{"u":"clients.html#import-csv","p":"Clients","s":"Importing clients from a spreadsheet","t":"import-csv\"> Moving from another program or an Excel list? Import CSV adds many clients at once, one per row. Open the window Click Import CSV on the Clients screen. The window Import clients from CSV opens. Get the sample file Click Download sample file . Clients-sample.csv lands in your Downloads folder, with the right column headings and two demo clients. Fill it in Open it in Excel or Google Sheets. Replace the demo rows with your clients, one per row. Keep the first row (the headings) as it is. Save as CSV In Excel, File → Save As → CSV UTF-8 (Comma delimited) or CSV (Comma delimited) . I"},{"u":"products.html","p":"Products and stock","s":"Products and stock","t":"Save what you sell once, then pick it on every invoice. Stock goes down as you sell and up as you buy."},{"u":"products.html#product-list","p":"Products and stock","s":"The product list","t":"product-list\"> Products in the sidebar opens your catalogue: the goods and services you sell or buy, with their prices, GST rate and stock. Save an item here once, and on every invoice you just type a few letters of its name to fill in the HSN, rate, unit and GST. The product list. Low stock shows in amber, none in red. The buttons at the top of the screen: Button What it does Import CSV Adds many products at once from a spreadsheet. See Importing products . Bulk edit Turns the list into a grid you can type in, to change many products at once. See Bulk edit . Greyed out until you have a produc"},{"u":"products.html#product-export","p":"Products and stock","s":"Printing or exporting the list","t":"product-export\"> Print / PDF , Excel and CSV beside the table title save the products shown, with name, type (Goods or Service), HSN/SAC, purchase price, selling price, GST %, unit and stock. Search first to save only some. Print / PDF opens the print window, where you can choose a printer or Save as PDF . The buttons are hidden during a bulk edit. A CSV saved here can be opened in Excel, and is a handy way to send your price list to an accountant. It can also be brought back in with Import CSV , or into another copy of the app."},{"u":"products.html#product-delete","p":"Products and stock","s":"Deleting a product","t":"product-delete\"> The bin asks Delete this product? first. Deleting removes it from your catalogue only: invoices and purchase bills that used it keep their lines unchanged. If it is a raw material of a product made here, the message names those products: remove it from their raw materials list too. A product deleted here is not in the Trash; to get it back, add it again."},{"u":"products.html#add-product","p":"Products and stock","s":"Adding a product or service","t":"add-product\"> Open the form Click Add Product . To change a product, click its pencil instead; the form opens as Edit Product . Name it Type the name as you want it printed on the invoice, such as \"A4 Paper Ream 75 GSM\" or \"Website Maintenance\". Goods or service Under This is a , leave Goods (stock counted) for things you keep on a shelf, or click Service (no stock) for work you do, such as printing, repairs or consulting. See Goods or service . Codes and prices Fill in the HSN or SAC code, the purchase price, the selling price and the GST %. Unit and stock Choose the unit and, for goods, type"},{"u":"products.html#goods-or-service","p":"Products and stock","s":"Goods or service","t":"goods-or-service\"> Every product is either Goods , things you buy, keep and sell, whose stock is counted, or a Service , work you do, such as printing, repairs, design, consulting or transport, which has no stock. Goods (stock counted) Service (no stock) Stock box in the form Yes No Selling it on an invoice Takes the quantity out of stock Moves no stock, and never says \"out of stock\" Buying it on a purchase bill Adds the quantity to stock Moves no stock Low-stock alerts, the bell, the Dashboard low-stock strip, the stock report Included Never included Manufacturing Can be a raw material or be "},{"u":"products.html#product-hsn","p":"Products and stock","s":"HSN and SAC codes","t":"product-hsn\"> HSN (Harmonised System of Nomenclature) codes classify goods, such as 4802 for paper or 8471 for computers. SAC (Services Accounting Code) codes classify services and start with 99, such as 998314 for IT services. The code decides the GST rate and is reported in your GSTR-1, in the HSN summary. Businesses with a turnover up to ₹5 crore must show at least a 4-digit HSN on invoices to registered buyers; above ₹5 crore, 6 digits on every invoice. Find your code on your supplier's bill, from your accountant, or with the HSN search on the GST portal. On the invoice, the app knows the "},{"u":"products.html#barcode","p":"Products and stock","s":"Barcode","t":"barcode\"> Give a product its barcode once, and scanning it on an invoice adds the product. See Scanning barcodes on an invoice . Open the product Click Add Product , or the edit button on a product in the list. Click the Barcode box Then scan the product's barcode with your scanner, or type the number printed under the bars. Save Click Save . Pressing Enter in the Barcode box does nothing else, so a scan never saves the form half filled. One barcode belongs to one product. Saving a code another product already has shows which product has it, and nothing is saved. The barcode is kept exactly as"},{"u":"products.html#bulk-edit","p":"Products and stock","s":"Bulk edit: changing many products at once","t":"bulk-edit\"> Use it when prices go up across the board, after a GST rate change, or to correct stock after counting your shelves. Bulk edit turns the table into a grid of boxes: Name , HSN/SAC , Purchase price , Selling price , GST % , Unit and Stock . Narrow the list (optional) Search first, for example by an HSN code, to edit only those products. The search box is locked while you edit. Start Click Bulk edit . Type the changes Change any boxes, in any rows. Each changed row turns blue, and the bar at the top counts them: \"3 products changed\". Save once Click Save changes (3) . You see \"3 prod"},{"u":"products.html#stock","p":"Products and stock","s":"How stock is counted","t":"stock\"> Stock is counted for a line only when it is linked to a product: picked from your products on the invoice or bill, not just typed in. Selling : saving a Tax Invoice, Bill of Supply, Composition bill or Delivery Challan takes the quantity out. Change the quantity later and save, and only the difference moves. Returns : a Credit Note puts the quantity back. Quotations and proformas move no stock. The invoice you convert them into does. Buying : saving a purchase bill adds the quantity in, and adds any new item to your products. Cancelling an invoice puts its stock back; un-cancelling tak"},{"u":"products.html#stock-adjust","p":"Products and stock","s":"Correcting stock by hand","t":"stock-adjust\"> There is no separate stock adjustment screen. After counting your shelves, or for breakage, a free sample or opening stock: One product Click its pencil, type the real count in Stock Quantity , and click Update . Many products Click Bulk edit , type the counts in the Stock column, and click Save changes . Stock typed in by hand has no date, so the stock report counts it as if it changed today. Write the reason in the product's description if you want to remember it. Stock is one count per product. There are no batches, expiry dates, serial numbers or godowns. See Limitations ."},{"u":"products.html#low-stock","p":"Products and stock","s":"Low-stock alerts","t":"low-stock\"> A product at or below your threshold shows its stock in amber here, is listed on the Dashboard , and adds to the notification bell. The threshold is 5 to start; change it, or turn alerts off, in Settings . It is one threshold for every product. With alerts off, stock is still counted and Out of Stock still shows in red."},{"u":"products.html#import","p":"Products and stock","s":"Importing products from a spreadsheet","t":"import\"> Have your price list in Excel, or moving from another program? Import CSV adds all the products and services at once. Open the window Click Import CSV on the Products screen. The window Import products from CSV opens. Get the sample file Click Download sample file . Products-sample.csv lands in your Downloads folder, with the right column headings and two demo rows: a product (Goods) and a service. Fill it in Open it in Excel or Google Sheets. Replace the two demo rows with your own, one product or service per row. Keep the first row (the headings) as it is. Save as CSV In Excel, File"},{"u":"products.html#manufacturing","p":"Products and stock","s":"Manufacturing: making products from raw materials","t":"manufacturing\"> If you make what you sell (furniture, sweets, garments, printed boxes), the app can use up the raw materials and add the finished product to stock in one step, and tell you what each unit costs you to make. Turn it on first: Settings → Features , tick Manufacturing (bill of materials) and save. It is off to start, and turning it off again hides it without deleting anything. Once on, you get: a Made here (from raw materials) tick in the product form, for its bill of materials ; a Make button at the top of Products, to record production ; a Production list under the product table"},{"u":"products.html#bill-of-materials","p":"Products and stock","s":"1. Give the product its raw materials (bill of materials)","t":"bill-of-materials\"> A bill of materials is the recipe: which raw materials, and how much of each, go into one unit of the finished product. Add the raw materials Add each raw material as a normal product, with its purchase price and stock (or buy it in on a purchase bill). Open the finished product Click its pencil (or Add Product for a new one). Tick Made here Tick Made here (from raw materials) . A box opens: Raw materials used to make 1 unit of this product . List the materials On each line, choose the material under Choose a product… and type the quantity for one unit made; its unit shows "},{"u":"products.html#make-production","p":"Products and stock","s":"2. Make: record what you made","t":"make-production\"> Each time a batch is finished, record it so stock stays right. Open Make Click Make at the top of Products. The window is Make (record production) . Product made Choose the product. Only products with a raw materials list are offered. Quantity made How many you made, in the product's unit. Date Today to start. Change it if you are recording a batch made earlier. Note (optional) Anything to remember, such as \"Batch 12\". Check the table Each raw material shows Per unit , Will use , In stock and Left after ; the last row is the finished product with its stock after. Below it, Co"},{"u":"products.html#mfg-example","p":"Products and stock","s":"Worked example","t":"mfg-example\"> Reazix makes chairs. One chair takes 4 chair legs (₹50 each), 1 seat (₹300) and 0.2 kg screws (₹400 a kg), so the cost per unit is 4 × 50 + 300 + 0.2 × 400 = ₹580 . Stock before: 100 legs, 20 seats, 5 kg screws, 3 chairs. Make 10 chairs Used Stock after Chair leg 40 60 Seat 10 10 Screws 2 kg 3 kg Chair (made) +10 13 The entry's cost of materials is 10 × ₹580 = ₹5,800."},{"u":"products.html#production-list","p":"Products and stock","s":"3. The production list","t":"production-list\"> Under the product table, Production lists the entries of the business you have open, newest first: Date , Product , Qty made , Cost of materials and Note . Control What it does From / To Show only entries between these dates. Leave blank for all. Print / PDF , Excel , CSV Save the entries shown. Eye ( View ) Opens the entry: see below . Bin ( Delete ) Deletes the entry after asking, and puts its stock back exactly: in the example, 40 legs, 10 seats and 2 kg screws back, 10 chairs out. An entry cannot be edited: to change one, delete it and enter it again. The stock report cou"},{"u":"products.html#production-entry","p":"Products and stock","s":"Viewing a production entry","t":"production-entry\"> The eye opens Made 10 Nos of Chair (the quantity and product), with its date and note, and a table of each Raw material used with its Qty , Rate and Cost , and the Total cost of materials . The rates are the purchase prices on the day it was saved, so changing a price later does not change old entries. Delete deletes it as above; Close closes it."},{"u":"receipts.html","p":"Payment receipts","s":"Payment receipts","t":"Receipts for money you have received, whether against an invoice or not, ready to print."},{"u":"receipts.html#receipt-list","p":"Payment receipts","s":"The Payment Receipts list","t":"receipt-list\"> The Payment Receipts card lists every receipt of the business you are working in, newest date first. Receipts you make here and the ones made when you record a payment on the Dashboard both appear in it. Column What it shows Date The date on the receipt. Receipt No Its number, such as RCP/2026-27/0012 (made here) or RCPT-... (made from a Dashboard payment). See Receipt numbers . Client Who paid you ( Received From ). Against Invoice The invoice it was for, or a dash if none. Amount The money received. Mode Bank Transfer, UPI, Cash, Cheque, Card or Other. Actions The printer prin"},{"u":"receipts.html#unassigned","p":"Payment receipts","s":"Receipts not assigned to a business","t":"unassigned\"> Receipts saved before the app kept businesses separate do not say which business took the money, so they show under every business. If you have any, a blue strip above the list says, for example, \" 3 receipts are not assigned to a business, so they show under all of them\", with a button Assign to followed by the business you are working in. Click it only if those receipts belong to that business. The app asks you to confirm, naming the business, and then they show only under it. The app never does this by itself, because only you know which business received the money. See More th"},{"u":"receipts.html#new-receipt","p":"Payment receipts","s":"Making a receipt (New Payment Receipt)","t":"new-receipt\"> Make a receipt whenever a customer pays you and wants a slip, or when you want a record of money received: a payment against an invoice, an advance before you have billed, a security deposit, or any other money in. Paid against an invoice on the Dashboard? If you record the payment on the invoice itself (the ₹ Payment button on the Dashboard ), a receipt is made for you. You do not need to make another one here. Open the form Click New Receipt at the top right. A box titled New Payment Receipt opens, with the next receipt number and today's date filled in. Pick the invoice, if th"},{"u":"receipts.html#quick-select","p":"Payment receipts","s":"Quick Select — Unpaid Invoices","t":"quick-select\"> This list at the top of the form shows up to 50 sales invoices of this business that are not fully paid: tax invoices, bills of supply and composition bills. Quotations, proforma invoices, delivery challans, credit notes and cancelled invoices are left out, because no money is owed on them. Each line shows the client, the invoice number and, on the right, the amount still owed. The list scrolls if it is long. Clicking an invoice fills in Received From , the client's address (it prints on the receipt), Amount with what is still owed (less any TDS the client deducts, and never bel"},{"u":"receipts.html#against-invoice","p":"Payment receipts","s":"Against Invoice: what happens to the invoice","t":"against-invoice\"> When Against Invoice exactly matches the number of one of this business's invoices, saving the receipt also records the payment on that invoice, with the same amount, date and mode and the note \"Receipt RCP/... · ref ...\". The invoice's status on the Dashboard then becomes Partial or Paid , and you do not record the payment again there. A cancelled invoice stays Cancelled. If the number does not match any invoice (a typing mistake, or an invoice of another business), the receipt is still saved, and you see: \"No invoice numbered ... was found, so this receipt is saved on its o"},{"u":"receipts.html#edit-receipt","p":"Payment receipts","s":"Editing a receipt (Edit Payment Receipt)","t":"edit-receipt\"> Click the pencil on a receipt's row. The same form opens, titled Edit Payment Receipt , with everything filled in. Change what you need and click Save Receipt . The receipt keeps its number. Changing the Amount , Date or Payment Mode of a receipt against an invoice updates the same payment on that invoice. It is not added twice. Changing Against Invoice to another invoice moves the payment: it is taken off the old invoice and recorded on the new one. Emptying it takes the payment off the old invoice. The receipt stays with the business it was made for, even if another business i"},{"u":"receipts.html#numbers","p":"Payment receipts","s":"Receipt numbers","t":"numbers\"> Receipts made on this screen have their own series, starting RCP, and follow your invoice number format : separator, financial year (April to March) and digits, for example RCP/2026-27/0001. If you set a brand prefix, it is used for receipts too (ACME-RCP/...). A business with its own numbering numbers its receipts separately. Receipts never share a count with invoices. The number you see when the form opens is a preview. The number is only taken when you save, so two people saving at once never get the same one. If you typed your own number, yours is kept and the series does not mov"},{"u":"receipts.html#print","p":"Payment receipts","s":"Printing a receipt","t":"print\"> Click the printer on a receipt's row. The receipt opens in a new window and your browser's print box appears. Choose your printer, or Save as PDF to keep or send it on WhatsApp or email. The window closes after printing. The printed receipt shows: Your business name, address and GSTIN (from Company details of the business selected now), and the heading PAYMENT RECEIPT ; Receipt No , Date , Received From , the client's Address (when the receipt was made from Quick Select), Payment Mode , and Reference No and Against Invoice when filled in; the amount in large figures, and in words under"},{"u":"receipts.html#delete","p":"Payment receipts","s":"Deleting a receipt","t":"delete\"> Click the bin on the receipt's row. The app asks \"Delete this receipt?\"; click Delete to remove it. This cannot be undone. Deleting a receipt removes only the receipt. A payment it recorded on an invoice stays on the invoice, so the invoice stays Paid or Partial. If the payment itself was a mistake, delete it from the invoice's Payment History on the Dashboard ; that also removes its receipt."},{"u":"receipts.html#cash-receipts","p":"Payment receipts","s":"Cash receipts and the cash book","t":"cash-receipts\"> A receipt with Payment Mode Cash shows in the Cash book as money in, labelled with its receipt number, so you never type it there again. A receipt against an invoice and the payment it records on that invoice are the same money, and the cash book counts it once. To change it, change the receipt here; the cash book follows."},{"u":"cash-book.html","p":"Cash book","s":"Cash book","t":"Every rupee that comes in or goes out in cash, with names and notes, and how much cash you should have in the drawer right now."},{"u":"cash-book.html#what-it-is","p":"Cash book","s":"What the cash book is for","t":"what-it-is\"> Use it for cash that does not belong on an invoice or a bill: money taken at the counter, an advance from a customer, salary paid in cash, tea and snacks, auto fare, money you take home, or cash you deposit in the bank. Each entry is either Money in or Money out , with an amount, a date, a name (who or what) and a note if you like. Open it from Cash book in the sidebar. If you do not see it, tick Cash book under Menu in Settings, Features and save. It is on to start, whatever your business type. Each business has its own cash book, like its expenses and receipts. Switching the bus"},{"u":"cash-book.html#opening-balance","p":"Cash book","s":"Start with the cash you have today","t":"opening-balance\"> Count the cash in your drawer (or cash box) on the day you start, then add it as your first entry: Money in Make sure Money in is selected (it turns green). Amount Type the cash you counted, such as 12500. Category Click the Category box and pick Opening balance . Save Press Enter or click Save . From then on, Cash in hand is this amount plus everything that comes in, less everything that goes out. While the cash book is empty, the list reminds you: \"No cash entries yet. Add your cash in hand today as Money in, category Opening balance, to start.\""},{"u":"cash-book.html#add-entry","p":"Cash book","s":"Adding an entry","t":"add-entry\"> The New entry form is at the top of the screen, so you can add one entry after another without opening anything. In or out Click Money in (green) for cash you received, or Money out (red) for cash you paid. Amount Required. More than 0, in rupees and paise. Name Who paid you or whom you paid, or what it was for: \"Ramesh\", \"Milk\", \"Auto\". Your clients' names, and names you used before, appear as you type. Category Optional. Pick one of Opening balance, Sales, Advance, Salary, Tea & snacks, Transport, Owner drawing, Deposit to bank or Other, or type your own. Date Today to start. Cha"},{"u":"cash-book.html#from-elsewhere","p":"Cash book","s":"Cash already recorded in the app","t":"from-elsewhere\"> You do not type cash in twice. These show in the cash book on their own, with a small dashed label saying where they came from: Label Where it was made Shows when Invoice INV-5 payment A payment recorded on the Dashboard The payment mode is Cash (money in) Invoice CN-2 payment A refund recorded on a credit note The payment mode is Cash (money out) Receipt RCP/26-27/0012 A payment receipt ; the invoice number follows if it was against one The payment mode is Cash (money in) Expense An expense ; its category shows too The payment mode is Cash (money out) Purchase bill GS/0457 pa"},{"u":"cash-book.html#cash-in-hand","p":"Cash book","s":"Cash in hand and the totals","t":"cash-in-hand\"> The cards at the top show: Cash in hand : all money in, less all money out, up to today. Entries dated in the future are not counted until their day comes. It turns red if it goes below zero, which usually means an entry is missing or the opening balance was not added. Today : cash in and out today. This month : cash in and out since the 1st. These cards always count every line, whatever dates or search you choose for the list. Count the drawer at the end of the day and compare it with Cash in hand. If they differ, look for an entry you forgot. Something wrong? Cash in hand is r"},{"u":"cash-book.html#list","p":"Cash book","s":"The list and the running balance","t":"list\"> The list's title is the dates you chose (such as This month ) with the money in and out of the lines shown. The list is oldest first, like a paper cash book; on the same day, lines go in the order entered, money in before money out. Each line shows the date, name and note, category (or where it came from), the amount under Money in or Money out , and the Balance : the cash you had after that line. A line with no name shows \"Money in\" or \"Money out\". The first line, Opening balance (brought forward) , is the cash you had when the chosen dates begin. With All dates there is no such line. "},{"u":"cash-book.html#edit-entry","p":"Cash book","s":"Changing or deleting an entry (Edit entry)","t":"edit-entry\"> Your own entries have a pencil and a bin under Actions . The pencil opens the entry in the form at the top, now titled Edit entry . Change it and click Update , or Cancel to leave it as it was. After an update the form is ready for a new entry again, dated today. The bin deletes the entry. The app asks first, saying how cash in hand will change (\"Money out of ₹200.00 on 05 Oct 2026 (Auto) is removed from the cash book...\"). Click Delete . This cannot be undone. Lines from invoices, receipts and expenses have no pencil or bin. Change them where they were made ( see above )."},{"u":"cash-book.html#filters","p":"Cash book","s":"Choosing dates and searching","t":"filters\"> The bar between the form and the list chooses which lines the list shows. Choice Shows This month The 1st to the last day of this month. The choice when you open the screen. Last month The whole of last month. This financial year 1 April to 31 March of the current year. All dates Everything, from your first entry. Choose dates Two date boxes appear: a from date and a to date. Leave one empty for no limit on that side. The Search name, note, category... box finds lines by name, note, category, where they came from (such as a receipt or invoice number), or amount. While you search, the"},{"u":"cash-book.html#export","p":"Cash book","s":"Print, PDF and Excel","t":"export\"> Print / PDF , Excel and CSV above the list save the lines shown, with the dates and search you chose: the opening balance, each line with its balance, and the total. The columns are Date, Name, Note, Category, From (where the line came from, or \"Cash book\" for your own entries), Money in, Money out and Balance. To make a PDF, click Print / PDF and choose Save as PDF as the printer. The CSV opens in Excel too. Your cash book is also saved in your backups. In Export Backup it travels with Expenses . Something wrong? \"Nothing to export\": no lines are shown for the dates and search chosen"},{"u":"recurring.html","p":"Recurring invoices","s":"Recurring invoices","t":"Invoices that repeat on a schedule, such as a monthly retainer, rent or an annual maintenance contract."},{"u":"recurring.html#two-ways","p":"Recurring invoices","s":"Two ways to set one up","t":"two-ways\"> From an invoice (recommended): make the first invoice as usual, and under Customize tick Make this a recurring invoice . This keeps everything on the invoice, including HSN/SAC codes, discounts, taxes, place of supply, terms and options, and lets you set Every N and an end date or number of invoices. From the Recurring screen : New Template with a client, frequency, next date, when to stop, type and simple item lines ( below ). Quicker, but the item lines have no HSN/SAC code or discount. Both appear in the same Recurring Templates list and are made into invoices the same way."},{"u":"recurring.html#template-form","p":"Recurring invoices","s":"The New Recurring Invoice form","t":"template-form\"> Click New Template at the top right (or Create Template when the list is empty). A box titled New Recurring Invoice opens. Pick the client Click them under Quick Select Client ( why this matters ), or type the Client Name . Set the schedule Choose the Frequency and Every , and the Next Due Date : the date of the first invoice. Say when to stop Leave Stop at Never, or pick a date or a number of invoices. Add the items Fill in at least one line under Line Items . Save Click Save . You see \"Recurring invoice created\" and it appears in the list. Field What it does Quick Select Clie"},{"u":"recurring.html#quick-select-client","p":"Recurring invoices","s":"Quick Select Client","t":"quick-select-client\"> This list shows when you start a new template, you have saved clients , and Client Name is still empty. Each line shows the client's name, state and GSTIN. Clicking one fills in the form and hides the list. To pick someone else, empty Client Name and the list comes back. Why pick rather than type: the client's state, country and SEZ status decide the tax on each invoice: CGST + SGST for a client in your own state, IGST for another state, an SEZ or a client abroad. These are not shown in the form, so they are only kept when you pick the client from the list. A name typed b"},{"u":"recurring.html#line-items","p":"Recurring invoices","s":"Line Items","t":"line-items\"> Each line is one thing you bill every time: Field What to enter Description What it is, such as \"Monthly accounting retainer\" or \"Shop rent, Ground floor\". A line with no description is left out when you save. Qty How many, 1 to start. Rate The price of one, before GST. GST% The GST rate, 18 to start. Use 0 for exempt items or a bill of supply. Add Item adds another line. The red X at the end of a line removes it (it shows once there is more than one line). You need at least one line with a description and a rate, or you see \"Add at least one item with description and rate\". The a"},{"u":"recurring.html#list","p":"Recurring invoices","s":"The Recurring Templates list","t":"list\"> Every template of the business you are working in, by client name A to Z. Column What it shows Client Who is billed. Frequency Weekly, Monthly, Quarterly, Yearly, or \"Every 3 months\" and so on. Type The invoice type made. Amount The total of each invoice, with GST, in the template's currency. Next Due When the next invoice will be made. Shown in bold orange, and the row is highlighted, when it is due today or overdue. Status Active (green) or Paused (grey). Actions ▶ Generate Now (green), Pause or Activate, the pencil to edit , the bin to delete . The recurring template list."},{"u":"recurring.html#due-banner","p":"Recurring invoices","s":"Invoices due for generation","t":"due-banner\"> When an Active template's next date has come and its invoice has not been made yet, an orange box at the top says, for example, \" 2 invoices due for generation \", with one button per template showing the client and frequency (such as \"Sharma Traders — Monthly\"). Usually you do nothing: the app makes them by itself within the hour ( see below ). Click a button to make that invoice straight away; it works exactly like Generate Now . Paused templates never show here."},{"u":"recurring.html#automatic","p":"Recurring invoices","s":"How invoices are created automatically","t":"automatic\"> A few seconds after the app starts, and then every hour while it is running, every Active template whose next date has come, and which has not reached its end, creates its invoice: a fresh number in that type's series (and the business's own series, if it has one); that day's date, status Unpaid, and a due date the same number of days later as on the invoice it was made from (none for templates made on this screen); the client, items and full GST working: CGST + SGST or IGST, cess, TDS/TCS, discounts and round-off, as on the invoice screen. Its Next Due then moves on by the schedul"},{"u":"recurring.html#generate-now","p":"Recurring invoices","s":"Generate Now","t":"generate-now\"> ▶ creates the invoice straight away, even if the template is paused or not yet due, exactly as the automatic run would: same tax, a fresh number, today's date. You see \"Invoice INV/2026-27/0042 generated for ...\" Its next date moves on by the schedule and it counts towards \"After N invoices\". Once a template has reached its end, you see \"Failed to generate: This template has reached its end date or number of invoices\" instead. Open the new invoice from the Dashboard to check it before sending."},{"u":"recurring.html#edit-template","p":"Recurring invoices","s":"Editing a template (Edit Template)","t":"edit-template\"> Click the pencil on a template's row. The form opens titled Edit Template , with everything filled in. Change the schedule, stop condition, type or lines and click Update . You see \"Template updated\". Invoices already made do not change; the next one uses the new details. Everything the form does not show is kept: terms, notes, invoice options, HSN codes and discounts on the lines, tax-inclusive prices, place of supply, and the client's state and country. Changing Next Due Date also moves the day of the month the schedule comes back to. Quick Select Client does not show while e"},{"u":"recurring.html#pause-delete","p":"Recurring invoices","s":"Pause, Activate and Delete","t":"pause-delete\"> Pause (the pause button on an Active row) stops the automatic invoices but keeps the template; you see \"Paused\". The button becomes Activate (a play button); click it to start again (\"Activated\"). If the next date passed while it was paused, the invoice is made at the next check. Use Pause for a client who stops for a few months. Delete (the bin) asks \"Delete this recurring invoice?\"; click Delete template . No more invoices are made from it. Invoices already made stay on the Dashboard. This cannot be undone."},{"u":"recurring.html#unassigned","p":"Recurring invoices","s":"Templates not assigned to a business","t":"unassigned\"> Templates saved before the app kept businesses separate show under every business. If you have any, a blue strip says, for example, \" 2 recurring templates are not assigned to a business\", with a button Assign to followed by the business selected now. Click it only if they belong to that business; the app asks you to confirm first. See More than one business ."},{"u":"purchases.html","p":"Purchase bills","s":"Purchase bills","t":"Record every supplier bill, so the GST you paid comes back as input tax credit and your stock stays right. Includes reading a bill from a photo, importing bills from a CSV file, and purchase orders to send suppliers."},{"u":"purchases.html#purchase-list","p":"Purchase bills","s":"The purchase list","t":"purchase-list\"> Open Purchases from the menu. The screen is called Purchase Bills , or Purchases when purchase orders are turned on. Then two buttons sit under the title: Purchase bills (the list on this page) and Purchase orders . The buttons at the top right: Button What it does Import from image (OCR) Reads a photo of a supplier's bill and fills the form for you. See Reading a bill from a photo . CSV import / export Brings in many bills at once from a spreadsheet, or saves all of them as one CSV. See Importing purchase bills from CSV . Add Purchase Opens a blank purchase bill. See Adding a "},{"u":"purchases.html#view-bill","p":"Purchase bills","s":"Viewing a bill","t":"view-bill\"> Click the eye on a row. A window titled Purchase Bill · invoice number shows: the date, payment status, and Intrastate (CGST+SGST) or Interstate (IGST) ; the Supplier box: name, address and GSTIN; the items: # , Description , HSN , Qty , Rate , GST% and Amount (quantity × rate, plus GST); the totals: Taxable , then CGST and SGST (half each) or IGST , Cess and Round-off when there are any, and the TOTAL ; Less: TDS and Paid to supplier when you keep back TDS, then Paid (the payments added up) and Balance due ; Payments made : each payment's date, amount, mode and reference; the note"},{"u":"purchases.html#add-purchase","p":"Purchase bills","s":"Adding a purchase bill","t":"add-purchase\"> Click Add Purchase . The Add Purchase Bill form opens ( Edit Purchase Bill when you clicked a pencil). Copy the details from the supplier's bill. Field What to put in Date * The date on the supplier's bill. Today to start. This decides which month's GSTR-3B the credit goes into. Payment Status Unpaid (to start) or Paid. Paid records one payment for the whole amount. To record what you actually paid (a part payment, UPI, cash), save the bill and use the green ₹ button in the list. Once a bill has payments, this box only shows its status. See Paying suppliers . Supplier Name * Req"},{"u":"purchases.html#purchase-tds","p":"Purchase bills","s":"TDS on a purchase bill","t":"purchase-tds\"> If you must deduct income-tax TDS when you pay this supplier (a contractor under 194C, a professional under 194J, rent under 194I...), record it on the bill. Under the totals strip, tick TDS deducted : Section Pick the section. Its usual rate fills in. Rate or amount Check the Rate % : the TDS is worked out on the taxable value (before GST), and the amount box shows it as a hint. To use an exact figure instead, type it in the amount box. Check The strip shows Less TDS and Paid to supplier (the bill total less the TDS): that is what you pay the supplier. The bill's total itself d"},{"u":"purchases.html#purchase-items","p":"Purchase bills","s":"Items on the bill","t":"purchase-items\"> Each row of Items is one line of the supplier's bill. Column What to put in Name The item. As you type, your products and items from earlier bills are suggested (your Products list first). Picking one fills in its HSN , its purchase price as Rate , its Tax % and Cess % . Use the same name as in Products, so stock goes to the right product. HSN The HSN code (goods) or SAC code (services) printed on the supplier's bill. Qty How many. Decimals are fine: 2.5 kg, 0.75 m. Rate The price of one unit before GST , as on the supplier's bill. Tax % The GST rate: 0%, 0.1%, 0.25%, 3%, 5%, "},{"u":"purchases.html#round-off","p":"Purchase bills","s":"Round-off","t":"round-off\"> Most suppliers round their bill total to the nearest rupee. If yours did, tick Apply round-off under the items, so your total matches theirs: ₹1,234.56 becomes ₹1,235 (round-off +₹0.44), ₹1,234.40 becomes ₹1,234 (round-off −₹0.40). It is off to start, because many bills already match the items exactly. The round-off is kept separate: it changes the bill's total, not its GST, so your input tax credit stays exactly what the supplier charged. It shows on the view, the PDF and the purchase register. An old bill with a round-off amount saved on it opens with the box already ticked."},{"u":"purchases.html#interstate","p":"Purchase bills","s":"Suppliers in another state","t":"interstate\"> When a supplier is in your state, their bill charges CGST + SGST . When they are in a different state, it charges IGST instead. Tick Inter-state purchase for an IGST bill, so the credit goes to IGST in GSTR-3B rather than CGST and SGST. Getting it wrong puts the credit in the wrong column. You rarely need to tick it yourself: Typing the supplier's full GSTIN ticks or unticks it. The first two digits of a GSTIN are the state code (03 Punjab, 07 Delhi, 27 Maharashtra...), compared with the state of your business in Settings . Picking a supplier you have bought from before uses what "},{"u":"purchases.html#itc","p":"Purchase bills","s":"How the GST credit is used","t":"itc\"> Input tax credit (ITC) is the GST you paid on what you bought, which you subtract from the GST you collected on sales. The app adds up the GST on every purchase bill and every expense in the period, and puts it in Table 4 (Eligible ITC) of GSTR-3B : to IGST for an inter-state bill, otherwise half to CGST and half to SGST. Cess on purchase bills goes in as cess credit. The credit goes into the month of the bill's Date . The purchase form has no switch for reverse charge, blocked credit or a separate place of supply. Every bill's GST is counted as credit. So: Check against GSTR-2B. Only cr"},{"u":"purchases.html#payment-status","p":"Purchase bills","s":"Paying suppliers","t":"payment-status\"> Each time you pay a supplier, record the payment on their bill: how much, when, and how (cash, UPI, bank transfer, cheque, card). You can pay a bill in parts, and record as many payments as you made. The app then shows what each bill, and each supplier, still needs to be paid. Each bill has a status, shown in colour in the Status column of the list: Status Means Unpaid (amber) No payment recorded yet. The whole amount is still to pay. Partly paid (purple) Some payments are recorded, but they add up to less than the bill. Balance due shows what is left. Paid (green) The payment"},{"u":"purchases.html#record-payment","p":"Purchase bills","s":"Recording a payment to a supplier","t":"record-payment\"> In Purchase Records , find the bill and click the green ₹ button under Actions (or open the bill with the eye and click Payments ). The window Record payment to supplier opens. At the top it shows the bill number and supplier, the Total , Less TDS if you keep back TDS, what is Paid so far and the Balance still to pay. Amount paid It starts at the balance still to pay. Leave it to pay the bill off, or type what you actually paid, such as 5000. Payment date Today to start. Change it to the day the money left you. Payment mode Cash, UPI, Bank transfer, Cheque, Card or Other. Refe"},{"u":"purchases.html#part-payments","p":"Purchase bills","s":"Part payments","t":"part-payments\"> Pay a bill in as many parts as you like. Each part is one payment. For example, a bill of ₹11,800: First part Click ₹ , type 5000, pick UPI , add the UPI reference and click Record Payment . The bill is now Partly paid and its Balance due is ₹6,800. The rest Later, click ₹ again. The amount already says 6800. Pick Cash and click Record Payment . The bill is now Paid , and the ₹6,800 shows in the Cash book as money out. Payments made to a supplier in one go for several bills: record one payment on each bill, for the part of the money that went to it."},{"u":"purchases.html#payment-history","p":"Purchase bills","s":"Payment history: changing or deleting a payment","t":"payment-history\"> Every payment on a bill is listed under Payment History in the payment window, oldest first: date, amount, mode, and the reference and note. The status of the bill is under the list. The same payments show in the bill's view (eye) and on its PDF, under Payments made . Change a payment : click its pencil. The boxes above fill with that payment and the title becomes Edit payment . Change what you need and click Save payment , or Cancel edit to leave it as it was. Delete a payment : click its red bin. The app asks first, saying the amount and date. Click Delete payment . The bil"},{"u":"purchases.html#mark-paid","p":"Purchase bills","s":"Marking a bill paid from the list","t":"mark-paid\"> The Status dropdown on each row is a shortcut: Paid records one payment for the whole balance, dated today, mode Other and noted \"Marked paid\", and says Marked paid . Use it when you do not need the details. Mode Other is not counted as cash, so it does not show in the Cash book. Unpaid takes back that \"Marked paid\" payment. Payments you recorded yourself stay: the bill then stays Partly paid and the message says so; delete them from the ₹ window if they were wrong. Partly paid opens the payment window, because a part payment needs its amount. Choosing Paid in the bill form does th"},{"u":"purchases.html#owed-to-suppliers","p":"Purchase bills","s":"What you owe suppliers","t":"owed-to-suppliers\"> Four places show what is still to pay: The Owed to suppliers card above the list: the balance due on all the bills shown (it follows the year, search and filters; pick All years for everything). The Balance due column, with its total at the bottom. Pick Unpaid / Partly paid in the filters to see only those bills. The purchase register ( Print / PDF , Excel , CSV ), which has Paid and Balance due columns. See For your accountant . Reports, Party Outstanding with You owe suppliers : one row per supplier, month by month, like Tally. The balance of a bill is its total, less TDS"},{"u":"purchases.html#payments-cash-book","p":"Purchase bills","s":"Cash payments and the Cash book","t":"payments-cash-book\"> A payment with mode Cash shows in the Cash book by itself, as money out, labelled Purchase bill number payment , with the supplier's name and the reference. It is counted once. Do not also add it in the Cash book. To change or delete it, click its label in the Cash book (it opens Purchases), then use the ₹ button on the bill. The Cash book follows. If you added supplier cash payments to the Cash book by hand before this version, and now also record them on the bill, delete your own Cash book entry so the money is not counted twice. UPI, bank transfer, cheque, card and Othe"},{"u":"purchases.html#stock","p":"Purchase bills","s":"What saving does to your products","t":"stock\"> Each item on the bill is matched to your products by name (capitals do not matter): A product you already have : its stock goes up by the quantity, and its purchase price becomes this bill's rate. Its selling price is not touched. Its HSN, GST rate and cess are filled in from the bill only if the product had none. A new item : it is added to your products, with the rate as both purchase and selling price, unit Nos (or the unit from the purchase order), and the quantity as its stock. Check its selling price afterwards in Products, or you will sell at cost. Editing a bill : only the diff"},{"u":"purchases.html#ocr","p":"Purchase bills","s":"Reading a bill from a photo","t":"ocr\"> Instead of typing a long bill, let the app read it from a photo or scan. Click Import from image (OCR) . The window Import from bill image (OCR) opens. Choose the picture Click the dashed box, or drag a photo or scan of the bill onto it: PNG, JPG or WebP, up to 8 MB. PDFs are not accepted; take a screenshot of the page instead. A preview appears. Read it Click Extract fields . Reading image… shows a percentage. It takes a few seconds, longer on an older computer. Check everything The Extracted fields panel appears on the right. Correct anything it read wrong, and add or remove item rows."},{"u":"purchases.html#ocr-review","p":"Purchase bills","s":"Checking what was read","t":"ocr-review\"> The Extracted fields panel shows what the app found. Every box can be changed. Field What to check Supplier Read from the capital-letter line above their GSTIN. Often needs correcting. GSTIN The first GSTIN on the bill. If the bill shows your GSTIN before the supplier's, replace it with theirs. Invoice No. The number after \"Invoice\", \"Bill\" or \"No.\". Date Read day first, as on Indian bills (03/04/2026 is 3 April). Grand total The amount after \"Grand Total\", \"Amount Payable\", \"Total\" or \"Net Amount\". Used only when no item rows are found. Tax breakdown , when found, lists the Taxab"},{"u":"purchases.html#export","p":"Purchase bills","s":"For your accountant","t":"export\"> The Print / PDF , Excel and CSV buttons at the top of Purchase Records save the Purchase register : the bills shown, after the search, year, status and cost centre filters, oldest first, with a Total row. Your business name is at the top. Columns: Date , Supplier , GSTIN , Invoice No , Taxable Amount , CGST , SGST , IGST , Cess , Inter-state (Y or N), Round-off , Total , Paid (payments to the supplier), Balance due , Status and Note . Print / PDF opens the register on its own page in landscape. Choose your printer, or Save as PDF . If nothing opens, allow pop-ups for the app (the mess"},{"u":"purchases.html#csv-purchases","p":"Purchase bills","s":"Importing purchase bills from CSV","t":"csv-purchases\"> Use this to bring in many bills at once: from another billing program, from Tally, or a sheet your accountant keeps. Click CSV import / export at the top of Purchases. The window Purchase bills: CSV import / export opens. Button What it does Template Downloads Purchase-import-template.csv : the right columns and one example bill. Export all as CSV Downloads every purchase bill of this business as Purchase-bills- date .csv , one row per item, in the same columns. Good for a backup, or to move bills to another business. Choose CSV file Reads your file and shows what will happen. "},{"u":"purchases.html#purchase-orders","p":"Purchase bills","s":"Purchase orders","t":"purchase-orders\"> A purchase order (PO) is what you send a supplier before the goods come: what you want, how many, at what rate. It is not a bill, so it changes neither your stock nor your GST returns. When the goods come, you turn it into a purchase bill in one click. Turn it on in Settings, Features : tick Purchase orders under Purchases screen , and save. It is on to start if you picked Wholesale / trading or Manufacturing as your business type . Purchases then has two buttons under the title, Purchase bills and Purchase orders . On the purchase orders tab, the top-right button is New purc"},{"u":"purchases.html#po-list","p":"Purchase bills","s":"The purchase order list","t":"po-list\"> Search by PO number, supplier or GSTIN in Search PO number, supplier... , and filter by status with All statuses . The red ✕ clears both. The Purchase orders table lists PO number , Date , Supplier , Expected (delivery date), Total (with GST) and Status . The actions on each row: Button What it does Shown for Eye View the order Every order Pencil Edit the order Open orders only Green page Convert to purchase bill Open and Partly received ⋯ menu Duplicate , Print , Download PDF , WhatsApp , Email , Cancel order Received and Cancelled orders show only Duplicate With no orders yet, the "},{"u":"purchases.html#po-status","p":"Purchase bills","s":"Purchase order status","t":"po-status\"> The status is worked out from the purchase bills made from the order; you only set Cancelled yourself. Status Means Open No bill saved from it yet. You can edit it. Partly received Bills saved from it have less than was ordered. Convert to purchase bill again fills in only what is still to come. Received Bills saved from it cover every item. Cancelled You cancelled it with Cancel order in the row's ⋯ menu. It keeps its number. Received and cancelled orders can only be viewed and duplicated ( Duplicate starts a new PO with the same supplier, items and notes, and a new number). Items"},{"u":"purchases.html#new-po","p":"Purchase bills","s":"The purchase order form","t":"new-po\"> New purchase order opens New purchase order ( Edit purchase order from the pencil). It is the purchase bill form with a few changes: Field What to put in PO date * The date of the order. Today to start. Expected delivery Optional. When you want the goods. Printed on the PO as Expected by . Supplier Name * , Supplier GSTIN As on a bill. Suppliers from your purchase bills are suggested. Supplier Address (optional) Printed on the PO. PO number * Filled in for you as PO/26-27/0001 , counting up for each business and financial year. You can type your own. Notes / terms (optional) Delivery "},{"u":"purchases.html#po-view","p":"Purchase bills","s":"Viewing and sending a purchase order","t":"po-view\"> The eye opens Purchase order · PO number : the date, expected date, status and tax type, the supplier, the items with Unit , Taxable value , CGST and SGST or IGST, cess, TOTAL and your Notes / terms . Button What it does Close Closes the window. Duplicate A new PO with the same supplier and items. Edit Open orders only. WhatsApp On a phone that can share files, sends the PDF with a short message. On a computer, opens WhatsApp with the message (PO number, date, items, quantities, rates and total) for you to pick the supplier; attach the PDF yourself if you want it. Email Opens your em"},{"u":"purchases.html#convert-po","p":"Purchase bills","s":"Turning a purchase order into a bill","t":"convert-po\"> Click Convert Click the green Convert to purchase bill on the row, or the same button in the view. The bill form opens The Add Purchase Bill form shows From purchase order PO number , with the supplier, the items still to come, their rates, GST and cost centre filled in. The date is today. Type the supplier's bill number In Invoice Number , from the bill that came with the goods. Set the Date to the date on their bill. Change quantities If fewer came, change Qty to what actually came. Change a rate if the bill differs. Save The bill is saved, stock goes up, and the order becomes P"},{"u":"purchases.html#unassigned","p":"Purchase bills","s":"\"Not assigned to a business\"","t":"unassigned\"> This only matters if you keep more than one business in the app. Records saved before you began keeping businesses separate have no business recorded, so they show under every business. Nothing is hidden, so nothing goes missing. When there are any, a blue banner says, for example, 3 purchase bills are not assigned to a business, so they show under all of them. The same banner appears on Expenses , Recurring and Receipts , for their own records. Pick the right business Switch to the business those records belong to in the sidebar. Assign Click Assign to business name on the banner"},{"u":"expenses.html","p":"Expenses","s":"Expenses","t":"Costs that are not stock, such as rent, electricity, software or travel, for your profit and loss, your income tax and the GST credit on them."},{"u":"expenses.html#expense-list","p":"Expenses","s":"The expense list","t":"expense-list\"> Open Expenses from the menu. Add Expense at the top right opens a new expense. The three totals Total Expenses is everything you paid, with GST. GST Paid (ITC) is the GST inside those amounts, your input tax credit. Entries is how many expenses are shown. All three follow the search and filters. Search and filters Search expenses... : part of the description, the vendor's name or the bill number. All Categories : show one category only, such as Office Rent. Year : the current financial year (April to March) to start; one of the last five, or All years . Cost centre : only when c"},{"u":"expenses.html#add-expense","p":"Expenses","s":"Adding an expense","t":"add-expense\"> Click Add Expense . The Add Expense form opens ( Edit Expense from the pencil). Field What to put in Date * The date on the bill, or the day you paid. Today to start. It decides the month the GST credit goes into. Category What kind of cost it is. Other to start. See Categories . Description * Required. What it was for, such as \"Shop rent - October\" or \"AWS Hosting - March\". Amount (incl. GST) * Required, above zero. The full amount you paid, with GST. GST % (for ITC) The GST rate on the bill, such as 18. The GST inside the amount is worked out and shown underneath as GST: ₹... ."},{"u":"expenses.html#categories","p":"Expenses","s":"Categories","t":"categories\"> Office Rent, Utilities, Internet & Phone, Software & Tools, Travel, Meals & Entertainment, Office Supplies, Salary & Wages, Professional Fees, Insurance, Marketing & Ads, Raw Materials, Shipping & Courier, Repairs & Maintenance, Bank Charges, GST Paid, Asset Purchase, Personal / Drawings, and Other. The list is fixed; use Other with a clear description for anything else. Category Use it for Asset Purchase Things that last years: a computer, furniture, a machine, a vehicle. The Income Tax screen leaves these out of business expenses (assets are written off over years as depreciatio"},{"u":"expenses.html#gst-credit","p":"Expenses","s":"How the GST credit is used","t":"gst-credit\"> The GST on each expense is added to your input tax credit in Table 4 of GSTR-3B , in the month of its date: to IGST if Inter-state expense is ticked, otherwise half to CGST and half to SGST. It is added to the credit from your purchase bills . Every expense with a GST % is counted. Only claim credit you are entitled to: The vendor must be GST-registered, and their bill must show your GSTIN. Without the vendor's GSTIN, put the GST % as 0. Food and drinks, personal spending, club fees and most car costs usually do not qualify (blocked credit). Put the GST % as 0 for these. Check the"},{"u":"expenses.html#export","p":"Expenses","s":"For your accountant","t":"export\"> The Print / PDF , Excel and CSV buttons at the top of Expense Records save the Expense statement : the rows shown, oldest first, with a Total row. The heading names your business and what was chosen (the year, the category, the cost centre, the search), and so does the file name: for example Expenses-FY 2026-27, Office Rent . Columns: Date , Description , Category , Amount , GST Amount , GST % , Vendor , Vendor GSTIN , Invoice No , Payment Mode , Inter-state (Y or N) and Note . Choose what to include Pick the year, and a category or cost centre, or search. For example: all Rent for th"},{"u":"gst-returns.html","p":"GST returns","s":"GST returns","t":"GSTR-1 and GSTR-3B built from the invoices, purchases and expenses you have already entered, checked against GSTR-2B, and ready to upload to the GST portal."},{"u":"gst-returns.html#gst-terms","p":"GST returns","s":"GST words on this screen, in plain language","t":"gst-terms\"> You do not need to be an accountant to use this screen. These are the words it uses. The glossary has more. Word What it means for you GSTR-1 The return that lists your sales : who you billed, how much, and the GST on it. Filed every month (by the 11th) or every quarter under QRMP (by the 13th after the quarter). GSTR-3B The short summary return where you pay the tax: GST collected on sales, less the GST you paid on purchases. Filed by the 20th (monthly) or the 22nd/24th after the quarter (QRMP), depending on your state. GSTR-2B A statement the portal makes for you every month, lis"},{"u":"gst-returns.html#period","p":"GST returns","s":"Choosing the period","t":"period\"> The row at the top, next to GST Returns , chooses the period every tab shows. It opens on the current month. Control What it does First list: Monthly , Quarterly (QRMP) or Full Year How long the period is. Pick Monthly if you file every month, Quarterly (QRMP) if you file every quarter. Month and year (Monthly) January to December, and a year from this year back five years. Quarter and year (Quarterly) Q1 (Apr–Jun), Q2 (Jul–Sep), Q3 (Oct–Dec) or Q4 (Jan–Mar). The year is the calendar year of those months, so the Jan–Mar 2027 quarter is Q4 with 2027 , and Apr–Jun 2026 is Q1 with 2026 ."},{"u":"gst-returns.html#whats-included","p":"GST returns","s":"What is included","t":"whats-included\"> Tax tables (GSTR-1 and GSTR-3B) use tax invoices and credit notes only. Left out of the tax tables : proforma estimates, quotations, bills of supply, composition bills, delivery challans, and cancelled invoices. Document Summary (Table 13) also counts bills of supply, composition bills, delivery challans, and cancelled documents, as the portal asks. See Document Summary . B2B or B2C is decided by the client: a client with a GSTIN is B2B, one without is B2C. Exports (a client whose country is not India) are kept out of B2B and B2C and listed in the red box. See Exports and SEZ "},{"u":"gst-returns.html#top-bar","p":"GST returns","s":"Filed status, warnings and the summary strip","t":"top-bar\"> Above the tabs you see, from top to bottom: the period row, a red box and an amber box if anything needs fixing, a NIL banner if the period is empty, and a strip of four totals. Below them are the tabs: Tab What it is for GSTR-1 Your sales, in the portal's tables, with the JSON file to upload. See GSTR-1 . GSTR-3B Tax on sales, credit on purchases, and what you pay. See GSTR-3B . GSTR-2B Reconciliation Checks your purchase bills against GSTR-2B. Shown only while GSTR-2B matching is on in Settings, Features (it is on to start). See GSTR-2B . TDS / TCS Report TDS your clients deducted "},{"u":"gst-returns.html#filed-status","p":"GST returns","s":"Filed status (R1 and 3B)","t":"filed-status\"> The two small pills in the period row remember whether you have filed: R1 Pending (red) or R1 Filed (green): GSTR-1. 3B Pending (red) or 3B Filed (green): GSTR-3B. File on the portal first The app cannot see the portal, so it only knows what you tell it. Mark it Click the pill, or Mark Filed on the GSTR-1 or GSTR-3B tab. A message confirms \"GSTR1 marked as filed for this period\". Undo a mistake Click the green pill again: it goes back to Pending. The mark is kept in this browser, for each business (GSTIN) and each period. Monthly, quarterly and full-year periods are separate: ma"},{"u":"gst-returns.html#warnings","p":"GST returns","s":"The red and amber warning boxes","t":"warnings\"> The app checks the period's invoices and shows problems before you file. The red box is for problems that make the return wrong or that the portal rejects. The amber box is for things worth fixing. Each box shows the first three messages; fix them and the next ones appear (the amber box also says \"+N more\"). Message What to do \" N export invoice(s) (…) are not in the GSTR-1 file. Add them in Table 6A on the GST portal with the shipping bill details\" Nothing is wrong with the invoices. On the portal, enter each export in Table 6A with its shipping bill number, date and port code. See"},{"u":"gst-returns.html#summary-strip","p":"GST returns","s":"The summary strip","t":"summary-strip\"> Figure What it counts Invoices Tax invoices and credit notes in the period, exports included Taxable Taxable value of B2B and B2C sales, less credit notes (exports not included) Tax CGST + SGST + IGST on those sales, less credit notes Net Payable What is left to pay in cash after your input tax credit, as on the GSTR-3B tab"},{"u":"gst-returns.html#gstr-1","p":"GST returns","s":"GSTR-1: your sales","t":"gstr-1\"> The GSTR-1 tab lays your sales out in the same tables as the portal, so you can check them before you upload. At the top is a row of buttons (see GSTR-1 downloads ). Below are these cards: Card Portal table What is in it B2B Sales — Table 4A 4A Invoices to clients with a GSTIN, one row each Credit/Debit Notes — Table 9B 9B Credit notes issued in the period (shown only if there are any) B2C Sales — Table 7 7 and 5 Sales to buyers without a GSTIN, added up; B2C Large invoices listed under them HSN Summary — Table 12 12 Quantity, value and tax for each HSN/SAC code Document Summary — Tab"},{"u":"gst-returns.html#b2b","p":"GST returns","s":"B2B Sales — Table 4A","t":"b2b\"> Every tax invoice to a client with a GSTIN, one row each. Your client sees these in their GSTR-2B and claims the GST as credit, so they must be right. The heading shows how many invoices there are. Column Meaning GSTIN The client's GSTIN, from the invoice Client, Invoice No, Date As on the invoice POS Place of supply as a state code (27, 10, 07…) Type Intra (CGST + SGST) or Inter (IGST), exactly as the invoice charged it Taxable, CGST, SGST, IGST Taxable value and tax. UTGST (Union Territories) is shown under SGST, as the portal takes it. Total The invoice total The last row, B2B Total ,"},{"u":"gst-returns.html#credit-notes","p":"GST returns","s":"Credit/Debit Notes — Table 9B","t":"credit-notes\"> Shown only when the period has credit notes . One row per note: the client's GSTIN (or Unregistered ), client, note number, date, taxable value, tax and total. Credit notes reduce your sales and tax. They are subtracted in the Summary Totals , the HSN Summary and GSTR-3B. Notes to clients with a GSTIN go in the JSON file (CDNR). Notes to unregistered buyers are not in the JSON: download them with CDNR (the file GSTR1_CDNUR.csv ) and enter them on the portal under 9B (Unregistered), if the portal asks for them. The app does not make debit notes. If you issue one, add it on the po"},{"u":"gst-returns.html#b2c","p":"GST returns","s":"B2C Sales — Table 7","t":"b2c\"> Sales to buyers without a GSTIN. The portal does not want them one by one: it wants totals for each supply type , place of supply and tax rate , and that is how the card shows them. Column Meaning Type Intra-state , Inter-state , or Inter-state, large for a B2C Large invoice Place of supply State code and name, such as 10-Bihar Rate % The GST rate. For a large invoice this column shows its invoice number instead. Taxable, CGST, SGST, IGST, Total Added up for that row B2C Large (Table 5). An inter-state invoice to an unregistered buyer above ₹1 lakh (₹2.5 lakh for invoices before 1 August"},{"u":"gst-returns.html#hsn-summary","p":"GST returns","s":"HSN Summary — Table 12","t":"hsn-summary\"> One row for each HSN/SAC code, tax rate and unit, covering B2B, B2C, exports and credit notes together. The portal requires this table. Column Meaning HSN The code on the item. N/A means the item had none. Description The name of the first item with that code Qty Total quantity. Credit notes subtract. Taxable, CGST, SGST, IGST, Total Tax Added up, net of credit notes How many digits you need depends on your turnover: 4 digits up to ₹5 crore, 6 digits above. Tick Aggregate turnover (AATO) is above ₹5 crore in Settings, GSTR filing details if that is you, and the app checks for 6. "},{"u":"gst-returns.html#doc-summary","p":"GST returns","s":"Document Summary — Table 13","t":"doc-summary\"> The portal wants to know which document numbers you used in the period. One row per number series (the number without its last digits, such as INV/26-27/ ): Column Meaning Document Type Invoices for outward supply (tax invoices, bills of supply, composition bills), Credit notes or Delivery challans From, To The lowest and highest number in that series this period Total Issued How many numbers were used, cancelled ones included Cancelled How many of those were cancelled. The portal works out net issued as Total minus Cancelled. Quotations and proforma estimates are not reported. I"},{"u":"gst-returns.html#gstr-1-summary","p":"GST returns","s":"GSTR-1 Summary Totals","t":"gstr-1-summary\"> The last card adds up the return: a B2B Sales row, a B2C Sales row, and a Grand Total . The Grand Total takes credit notes off, so it can be lower than B2B plus B2C. Exports are not in it (they are in GSTR-3B 3.1(b)). After you upload the JSON, compare these figures with the summary the portal shows before you file."},{"u":"gst-returns.html#exports","p":"GST returns","s":"Exports and SEZ","t":"exports\"> Exports : an invoice to a client whose country is not India. It is kept out of B2B and B2C and out of the JSON file, because the portal's export table (6A) can need the shipping bill number, date and port code, which the app does not record. The Exports — Table 6A table on the GSTR-1 tab lists them, ready to type into Table 6A on the portal: type WPAY (IGST paid) or WOPAY (under a LUT, no IGST), invoice number and date, rate, taxable value, IGST and invoice value. Exports saves the same rows as GSTR1_Exports_6A.csv . For services no shipping bill is needed; for goods add it on the po"},{"u":"gst-returns.html#gstr-1-files","p":"GST returns","s":"GSTR-1 downloads","t":"gstr-1-files\"> The buttons at the top of the GSTR-1 tab: Button What it saves JSON Export The file you upload to the portal: GSTR1_ GSTIN _ MMYYYY .json . It is checked first: see Checks before the file is made . B2B GSTR1_B2B_Invoices.csv : one row per B2B invoice, in the portal's Table 4A layout B2C GSTR1_B2C_Small.csv (totals by type, place of supply and rate), and GSTR1_B2C_Large.csv if there are any large invoices HSN GSTR1_HSN_Summary.csv , in the column order of the portal's Table 12 template, with the unit code (UQC) CDNR GSTR1_CDNR.csv for credit notes to registered clients, GSTR1_CDN"},{"u":"gst-returns.html#json-checks","p":"GST returns","s":"Checks before the file is made","t":"json-checks\"> The portal rejects some mistakes outright, so JSON Export checks for them first. These stop the download until fixed (the message starts \"GSTR-1 export blocked — fix these first\"): An invoice or credit note number longer than 16 characters, or with anything other than letters, digits, - or / . The message names the first three. An item with a GST rate the portal does not accept. The portal takes 0, 0.1, 0.25, 1, 1.5, 3, 5, 6, 7.5, 12, 18, 28 and 40%. Your own GSTIN is not set in Settings, Company . Full year is chosen as the period. A GSTR-1 file is for one month, or one quarter "},{"u":"gst-returns.html#upload","p":"GST returns","s":"Uploading GSTR-1 to the portal","t":"upload\"> Fix the red box Clear the problems listed at the top first. Download the JSON JSON Export on the GSTR-1 tab, for the right month or quarter. Open the return Log in at gst.gov.in, go to Returns Dashboard , pick the financial year and period, and open GSTR-1. Upload it Choose Prepare Offline , upload the JSON, and wait for it to be processed. If the portal reports errors, it gives an error file to download: fix those invoices in the app and upload a fresh JSON. Add what the file cannot hold Exports in Table 6A, and anything else listed under What you add on the portal by hand . Check an"},{"u":"gst-returns.html#gstr-3b","p":"GST returns","s":"GSTR-3B: tax to pay","t":"gstr-3b\"> GSTR-3B is where you pay. The tab works it out in four steps: tax on sales (3.1 and 3.2), credit on purchases (4), the credit used against the tax (6), and what is left to pay in cash. Card What it shows Table 3.1 — Outward Supplies & Tax (a) taxable sales, (b) exports with their IGST, (c) nil and exempt Table 3.2 — Inter-state Supplies to Unregistered Persons Inter-state B2C sales, by state. Shown only if there are any. Table 4 — Eligible ITC Credit from purchases and expenses, by IGST, CGST and SGST Table 6 — Tax Payment Summary Tax, credit used, Net Tax Payable , and credit carrie"},{"u":"gst-returns.html#table-3-1","p":"GST returns","s":"Table 3.1 — Outward Supplies & Tax","t":"table-3-1\"> Row What is in it (a) Outward taxable supplies (other than zero-rated, nil-rated and exempted) B2B and B2C sales, less credit notes: the same as the GSTR-1 Grand Total. Taxable value, IGST, CGST and SGST. (b) Zero-rated supplies Exports: their taxable value and any IGST charged on them (c) Other outward supplies (nil rated, exempted) Always ₹0: the app does not separate exempt sales. If you have them, enter them on the portal. Reverse-charge purchases, 3.1(d), are not shown on screen, but the 3B JSON fills them from the period's purchase bills marked reverse charge. Pay that tax in"},{"u":"gst-returns.html#table-3-2","p":"GST returns","s":"Table 3.2 — Inter-state Supplies to Unregistered Persons","t":"table-3-2\"> Appears only when you sold to a buyer without a GSTIN in another state. One row per state (the client's state), with the taxable value and IGST. It should agree with the inter-state rows of B2C Sales . On the portal, add a row for each place of supply."},{"u":"gst-returns.html#table-4-itc","p":"GST returns","s":"Table 4 — Eligible ITC (from Expenses & Purchases)","t":"table-4-itc\"> The GST you paid, which you can take off the GST you owe. It adds up: Purchase bills dated in the period: their GST goes to IGST if the purchase is marked inter-state, otherwise half to CGST and half to SGST. Expenses dated in the period with a GST amount: the same way. The row (A) ITC Available — All other ITC is the portal's Table 4(A)(5), where ordinary purchase credit goes. Net ITC Available is the same figure, because the app does not reverse any credit. Cess on purchases is sent in the 3B JSON. Not all GST paid is credit The app counts every GST amount you entered. Some is "},{"u":"gst-returns.html#table-6-payment","p":"GST returns","s":"Table 6 — Tax Payment Summary","t":"table-6-payment\"> Row Meaning Output Tax Liability Tax on your sales: Table 3.1(a), plus IGST on exports Less: ITC utilised The credit from Table 4 used against it, in the order the law sets Net Tax Payable What is left, for each tax and in total. This is paid in cash. ITC carried forward Shown only when credit is left over. It stays in your credit ledger for next month. Credit is used in the order the law sets: IGST credit first (against IGST, then CGST and SGST), then CGST credit (against CGST, then IGST) and SGST credit (against SGST, then IGST). CGST credit never pays SGST, nor SGST credit"},{"u":"gst-returns.html#net-payable","p":"GST returns","s":"Net GST Payable","t":"net-payable\"> The big figure at the bottom of the GSTR-3B tab: the total to pay for the period. Underneath it says Pay via Electronic Cash Ledger (create a challan on the portal and pay by net banking, UPI, card or NEFT/RTGS), or ITC covers your liability when nothing is due in cash. Late payment carries interest at 18% a year on the cash amount, and a late fee for filing late. See the Filing Guide ."},{"u":"gst-returns.html#gstr-3b-files","p":"GST returns","s":"GSTR-3B downloads","t":"gstr-3b-files\"> Button What it saves 3B CSV GSTR3B_Summary.csv : rows for 3.1(a), 4(A) ITC available, 6.1 ITC utilised, 6.1 tax payable in cash, and ITC carried forward 3B JSON GSTR3B_ GSTIN _ MMYYYY .json in the portal's GSTR-3B format: 3.1(a), 3.1(b), reverse charge 3.1(d) and Table 4(A)(5) with cess. Other rows are sent as 0. Mark Filed Marks GSTR-3B filed for this period; use the 3B pill to undo 3B JSON says \"No data to export for this period\" when the period has no invoices and no expenses, even if it has purchase bills. In that case use 3B CSV , or type the credit in on the portal."},{"u":"gst-returns.html#gstr-2b","p":"GST returns","s":"Checking your credit against GSTR-2B","t":"gstr-2b\"> GSTR-2B lists the invoices your suppliers reported. The GSTR-2B Reconciliation tab compares it with the purchase bills you entered, so you claim only credit that is really there. (If the tab is missing, turn on GSTR-2B matching in Settings, Features .) Download GSTR-2B On the portal: Returns , GSTR-2B , pick the month, Download JSON . If it comes as a ZIP, extract it. Pick the same period here Choose the same month at the top of GST Returns. Import it Click Import 2B JSON and choose the file. A message says \"Imported GSTR-2B for GSTIN — N suppliers\". Read the results Each 2B entry is"},{"u":"gst-returns.html#gstr-2b-results","p":"GST returns","s":"Reading the GSTR-2B results","t":"gstr-2b-results\"> After an import you see Export reconciliation CSV , Clear (removes the imported file), and \"Imported for GSTIN · period MMYYYY \". Check that period matches the one you picked. The row of counts below works as a filter: click one to show only those rows, or Total entries to show all. Status Meaning What to do ✓ Matched In both, and the invoice value and taxable value agree to within ₹1 Nothing. This credit is safe to claim. ⚠ Amount mismatch In both, but the amounts differ by more than ₹1 Compare with the paper bill. Correct your purchase entry, or ask the supplier to amend th"},{"u":"gst-returns.html#tds-tcs","p":"GST returns","s":"TDS and TCS report","t":"tds-tcs\"> The TDS / TCS Report tab adds up the period's tax invoices and credit notes that have TDS or TCS on them. These are income-tax amounts, not GST. It has two cards. The CSV files list every invoice with quarter, section, rate, client, GSTIN, PAN, taxable value and amount. They are for your CA to prepare Form 26Q and Form 27EQ from (filed through tin-nsdl.com); they are not the forms themselves. Something wrong? A card says \"No invoices with TDS in this period\": no invoice in the period has TDS turned on. Turn it on in the invoice under Customize , then TDS, and save. Check the period t"},{"u":"gst-returns.html#tds-receivable","p":"GST returns","s":"TDS Receivable (deducted by clients)","t":"tds-receivable\"> Tax your clients should have deducted from what they pay you, under sections such as 194C, 194J or 194Q. You claim it against your own income tax, so check it shows in your Form 26AS / AIS. Three figures: Invoices with TDS , Taxable value , Total TDS receivable . A table by Quarter (Q1 is April–June) and Section , with the number of invoices, taxable value and TDS. An invoice with no section chosen is counted under 194Q. Export TDS CSV saves TDS_Receivable_Report.csv . It is greyed out when there is nothing to export."},{"u":"gst-returns.html#tcs-collected","p":"GST returns","s":"TCS Collected (from clients)","t":"tcs-collected\"> Tax you collected from buyers on top of the invoice. You must deposit it with the Income Tax Department and report it in Form 27EQ every quarter. Three figures: Invoices with TCS , Taxable value , Total TCS collected . A table by quarter and section. An invoice with no section chosen is counted under 206C(1H). Export TCS CSV saves TCS_Collected_Report.csv ."},{"u":"gst-returns.html#filing-guide","p":"GST returns","s":"The Filing Guide tab","t":"filing-guide\"> Step-by-step portal instructions inside the app. At the top a one-line reminder: review the GSTR-1 and 3B tabs, export the JSON, upload it, file GSTR-1 first and GSTR-3B after, with the usual due dates (GSTR-1 by the 11th, GSTR-3B by the 20th of the next month) and the late fee. Three buttons switch what is shown: Button What it shows Regular Filing (With Sales) GSTR-1 in 9 steps, GSTR-1 Pro Tips, GSTR-3B in 7 steps, GSTR-3B Pro Tips NIL Return (No Sales) When a NIL return applies, and how to file NIL GSTR-1 and NIL GSTR-3B. See NIL returns . Common Errors & Fixes Portal error m"},{"u":"gst-returns.html#guide-gstr1-steps","p":"GST returns","s":"GSTR-1 steps in the Filing Guide","t":"guide-gstr1-steps\"> The card GSTR-1 — Sales Return (File This First) walks through the portal: Log in to the GST portal. Select the return period, and choose Prepare Online or Prepare Offline. Table 4A, B2B invoices: what each portal field means. Table 5, B2C Large. Table 7, B2C (Others), entered as totals. Table 9B, credit and debit notes. Table 12, HSN summary, and how many digits your turnover needs. Table 13, documents issued. Preview, submit and file with DSC or EVC, and keep the ARN. If you upload the app's JSON, steps 3 to 8 are already filled in: just check them."},{"u":"gst-returns.html#guide-gstr3b-steps","p":"GST returns","s":"GSTR-3B steps in the Filing Guide","t":"guide-gstr3b-steps\"> The card GSTR-3B — Summary Return + Tax Payment (File After GSTR-1) : open GSTR-3B, check Table 3.1 and 3.2, claim credit in Table 4, Table 5 (exempt and non-GST purchases), Table 6 (paying the tax, and the order credit is used), then submit, pay and file. The last step lists what happens if you file late: a late fee per day, 18% a year interest on tax paid late, the next return blocked, and e-way bills blocked after two months."},{"u":"gst-returns.html#guide-pro-tips","p":"GST returns","s":"GSTR-1 and GSTR-3B Pro Tips","t":"guide-pro-tips\"> Two green and blue boxes in Regular Filing with practical tips: the quickest way to upload GSTR-1 (the JSON), opting for quarterly filing (QRMP) under ₹5 crore, where amendments, exports and advances go, why to check GSTR-2B before claiming credit, the order credit is used, how to pay through a challan, how interest is worked out, and where reverse-charge tax goes."},{"u":"gst-returns.html#guide-errors","p":"GST returns","s":"Common GST Portal Errors & How to Fix Them","t":"guide-errors\"> The card under Common Errors & Fixes lists the portal messages people meet most, each with the fix: Invalid GSTIN, invoice number already exists, place of supply mismatch, invoice date outside the return period, invalid HSN code, GSTR-3B blocked because GSTR-1 is not filed, credit more than GSTR-2B, previous period not filed, taxable value and tax mismatch, EVC or OTP problems, and challan amount not matching. For messages from the app itself, see Troubleshooting, GST and returns ."},{"u":"gst-returns.html#guide-rules","p":"GST returns","s":"Key GST Rules to Remember","t":"guide-rules\"> A short list of the rules behind the returns: the time limit to claim credit (Section 16(4)), the time limit for credit notes (Section 34), when an invoice must be issued (Section 31), the order credit is used (Section 49), credit only as in GSTR-2B, interest on late payment (Section 50), how long notices can come (Sections 73 and 74, keep records at least 6 years), cancellation of GSTIN for not filing (Section 29(2)(c)), and e-way bills blocked for unfiled GSTR-3B."},{"u":"gst-returns.html#nil-return","p":"GST returns","s":"NIL returns","t":"nil-return\"> If a period has no invoices, no purchase bills and no expenses, an amber banner says: \"No invoices, purchase bills or expenses found — file a NIL return on the GST portal. NIL returns are mandatory.\" A NIL return is only right when you had no sales, no credit to claim, no tax due and no reverse-charge purchases. A period with a purchase bill has credit to claim, so the banner does not appear: file a regular GSTR-3B for it. (A NIL GSTR-1 may still be right if you sold nothing.) Open the NIL guide On the Filing Guide tab, click NIL Return (No Sales) . The box When to File NIL Return"},{"u":"gst-returns.html#e-invoice","p":"GST returns","s":"E-invoicing (IRN)","t":"e-invoice\"> A business whose yearly turnover (aggregate, all GSTINs on one PAN) has been above ₹5 crore in any year since 2017-18 must register its B2B invoices on the e-invoice portal. The portal gives each invoice an IRN (Invoice Reference Number) and a signed QR code, and an invoice without them is not valid. Below ₹5 crore you do not need any of this. The app stays offline: it makes the file, you upload it, and you bring the IRN back. Turn on E-invoicing (IRN) in Settings, Features first; it is off to start. Download the e-invoice JSON For one invoice: open it, click E-invoice in the toolb"},{"u":"gst-returns.html#e-invoice-dialog","p":"GST returns","s":"The E-invoice (IRN) window","t":"e-invoice-dialog\"> Opens from E-invoice in the invoice toolbar (only while E-invoicing is on, and for tax invoices and credit notes). At the top it repeats the three steps: download, upload on einvoice1.gst.gov.in (e-Invoice → Bulk Upload), paste the reply. Below that, one notice tells you where you stand: Notice Meaning \"Save the invoice first, so its number is final.\" The invoice is new or unsaved. Save it, then open this window again. The download and Save IRN stay greyed out until then. \" Fix these first: \" and a list Problems the portal would reject, such as a missing PIN code or HSN code"},{"u":"gst-returns.html#e-invoice-report","p":"GST returns","s":"E-invoice results: invoices left out, IRNs not saved","t":"e-invoice-report\"> After E-invoice JSON or Import IRN on the Dashboard, a window lists any invoice that was not handled, each with the reason. Its title tells you what happened: Title Meaning \"N invoices were left out\" The file was made, but without these. Fix each one, then export them again. \"Nothing was exported\" None of the ticked invoices could go in the file. The reasons are listed. \"IRN saved on N invoices; M not saved\" Some IRNs from the portal's file were saved, the rest were not \"No IRN was saved\" None of the IRNs in the file matched an invoice Usual reasons an IRN is not saved: \"No "},{"u":"reports.html","p":"Reports","s":"Reports","t":"Profit and loss, who owes you and for how long, party outstanding by month, your best clients, your best-selling products, closing stock with its value, TDS and TCS, and profit by branch or project. Every report prints and downloads as Excel or CSV."},{"u":"reports.html#tabs","p":"Reports","s":"The report tabs","t":"tabs\"> Open Reports from the sidebar. A row of buttons at the top picks the report; the one you are on is filled in blue. The small ? at the end of that row opens the part of this guide for the report you are looking at. Tab What it answers Period Profit & Loss Did I make money? Sales minus expenses, without GST, and month by month. The period you choose Outstanding & Aging Who owes me money today, on which invoice, and how late is it? Every unpaid invoice, any date Party Outstanding The same money owed, one row per party and one column per month, the way Tally shows it. A financial or calenda"},{"u":"reports.html#included","p":"Reports","s":"What the reports include","t":"included\"> The sales tabs cover the business selected at the top of the sidebar, and count only real sales, as the Dashboard does: Counted: tax invoices, bills of supply and composition bills. Subtracted: credit notes (goods returned or a discount given after the sale) reduce the sales of the period they are dated in. Left out: proforma invoices and estimates (a quote is not a sale), delivery challans (goods moved, not sold) and cancelled invoices. Purchase bills are not part of these reports, except By cost centre ; they are in Income Tax, ITR Summary and the purchase register . Expenses are "},{"u":"reports.html#period","p":"Reports","s":"Choosing the period and currency","t":"period\"> Profit & Loss, Client Analytics, Product Performance and By cost centre share one period box at the top. Change it on one tab and the others follow. (Outstanding & Aging, Party Outstanding and Stock have their own choices, described in their sections.) Box What it does Filter By Fiscal Year (1 April to 31 March) or Month / Year (one calendar month). Fiscal Year Shows with Fiscal Year. The current financial year and the four before it, such as FY 2026-27. It starts on the current one. Month and Year Show with Month / Year. Any month of this year or the five years before. They start on "},{"u":"reports.html#export","p":"Reports","s":"Printing and downloading a report","t":"export\"> Every report table has three buttons at its top right: Button What you get Print / PDF Opens the table alone in a new window, with its title and a line saying the business and period, and the print box opens. Choose your printer, or Save as PDF as the printer to keep a PDF. Wide reports (outstanding, party outstanding, cost centres) print landscape. Excel Downloads an .xlsx file. Amounts are real numbers, so Excel can total, sort and filter them. CSV The same table as a CSV file, for any spreadsheet, Tally import or your CA's software. They export what the screen shows: the period, cu"},{"u":"reports.html#profit-loss","p":"Reports","s":"Profit & Loss","t":"profit-loss\"> Did the business make money in the period? Choose the period in the box at the top (see Choosing the period ). If you bill in more than one currency, a Currency choice appears, since different currencies are never added together. Four cards at the top give the answer: Card What it is Revenue (ex. tax) Your sales without GST (and without any TCS collected on the invoices). Credit notes are subtracted. Expenses (ex. GST) Your expenses without the GST on them. Net Profit or Net Loss Revenue minus expenses. Green for a profit; red with a minus sign for a loss. Margin Profit as a perc"},{"u":"reports.html#pl-statement","p":"Reports","s":"Profit & Loss Statement","t":"pl-statement\"> The card below the four figures sets the sum out line by line, the way an accountant would: Line Meaning Total Revenue Everything billed in the period, GST included, less credit notes. Less: GST Collected The GST (and TCS) on those invoices. It belongs to the government. Net Revenue What you actually earned from sales. Total Expenses Expenses with their GST. Less: GST on Expenses (ITC) The GST on those expenses, which comes back to you as input tax credit. Net Expenses What the expenses really cost you. Net Profit / Net Loss Net Revenue minus Net Expenses. With more than one cur"},{"u":"reports.html#monthly-breakdown","p":"Reports","s":"Monthly Breakdown","t":"monthly-breakdown\"> One row for each month that had sales or expenses in the period, oldest first, with Revenue , Expenses and Profit/Loss for that month, all without GST. A profit shows in green, a loss in red. Months with nothing in them are left out. The card appears only when the period has some activity. Print / PDF , Excel and CSV export it with a Total row at the bottom. Pick the year Filter By Fiscal Year , and the year. Read the months Look for months in red: those are the months you spent more than you sold. Send it to your CA Click Excel and email the file."},{"u":"reports.html#outstanding","p":"Reports","s":"Outstanding & Aging","t":"outstanding\"> Every unpaid or part-paid sales invoice, whatever its date, grouped by how late it is. Use it each week to decide whom to call first. The period box does not apply here: this is what is owed today . Five cards at the top: Card Money owed on invoices that are Total Outstanding All of them added up Current (0-30d) Not yet due, or up to 30 days past the due date (green) 31-60 days 31 to 60 days late (amber) 61-90 days 61 to 90 days late (purple) 90+ days More than 90 days late (red): the ones to chase first Days are counted from the invoice's due date ; an invoice with no due date c"},{"u":"reports.html#outstanding-receivables","p":"Reports","s":"Outstanding Receivables","t":"outstanding-receivables\"> The table lists each unpaid invoice, the most overdue at the top: Column Meaning Client Who owes it Invoice No , Date , Due Date Which invoice, and when it was due Amount The invoice total, with GST Paid What they paid so far (a dash if nothing) Outstanding What is still owed, in red Days Overdue Current if not late yet, otherwise the days late, such as 45d . Rows more than 30 days late are highlighted, and more than 90 days late even more strongly. Print / PDF , Excel and CSV export the list (landscape), with a Currency column and the date \"unpaid as on\" in the title"},{"u":"reports.html#party-outstanding","p":"Reports","s":"Party Outstanding","t":"party-outstanding\"> The same money owed, laid out the way Tally does it: one row per party (client), A to Z, one column per month, a Total for each party on the right and a Total for each month at the bottom. Each unpaid amount sits in the month of its invoice, so you can see at a glance that, say, Mehta Traders still owes ₹12,000 from June and ₹8,500 from August. The card is titled Party outstanding by month . Its boxes: Box What it does Financial year (Apr-Mar) / Calendar year (Jan-Dec) Twelve columns from April to March (the default), or January to December. Year Which year: FY 2026-27 and "},{"u":"reports.html#supplier-outstanding","p":"Reports","s":"What you owe suppliers","t":"supplier-outstanding\"> The same table the other way round. In the first box of the card, pick You owe suppliers (it starts on Clients owe you ). The card is then titled Owed to suppliers by month : one row per supplier, A to Z, with what you still have to pay them in the month of their bill, an Earlier column for older unpaid bills, and totals. What is owed on a bill is its total, less TDS you keep back, less the payments recorded on it . A Paid bill is left out. A bill marked Paid before payments could be recorded owes nothing. A bill marked Partial then, with no payments recorded, shows its "},{"u":"reports.html#clients","p":"Reports","s":"Client Analytics","t":"clients\"> Who buys the most, and who owes the most, in the period chosen at the top. Revenue here includes GST (it is what the client was billed), less their credit notes."},{"u":"reports.html#top-clients","p":"Reports","s":"Top clients by revenue","t":"top-clients\"> The ten clients who were billed the most in the period, highest first, with Revenue and the number of Invoices (credit notes are not counted as invoices). Use it to know whom to look after: a discount or a call to your best ten pays back the most. \"No client data for this period.\" means there were no sales in that period and currency."},{"u":"reports.html#worst-payers","p":"Reports","s":"Highest outstanding (worst payers)","t":"worst-payers\"> The ten clients who owe you the most on invoices from this period, with Outstanding and % Unpaid : what share of what they were billed is still unpaid. 80% unpaid is a customer to stop giving credit to. Outstanding is after any TDS they deducted. \"Everyone is up to date.\" means nobody owes anything on this period's invoices. For money owed from any date, see Outstanding & Aging ."},{"u":"reports.html#all-clients","p":"Reports","s":"All clients breakdown","t":"all-clients\"> Every client billed in the period, the number in brackets being how many. Columns: Client , Invoices , Revenue , Paid , Outstanding (a dash if nothing), Last Invoice date. Highest revenue first. Print / PDF , Excel and CSV export it. Something wrong? One customer appears on two rows: the name is typed differently on some invoices (\"Sharma Traders\" and \"Sharma Traders Pvt Ltd\"). Clients are grouped by the exact name on the invoice. To see one client's whole history, open their ledger ."},{"u":"reports.html#products","p":"Reports","s":"Product Performance","t":"products\"> What you sold, by item, in the period chosen at the top. Revenue here is the line's taxable value: after line discounts and without GST, so it matches your invoices. Credit notes are subtracted (returned quantities come off too). Delivery charges and other charge lines are not a product and are left out. Items are grouped by the name on the invoice line."},{"u":"reports.html#top-products","p":"Reports","s":"Top revenue producers","t":"top-products\"> The ten items that brought in the most money, with Revenue and Qty sold . Rest the mouse on a name to see its HSN code. \"No product data for this period.\" means no sales in that period."},{"u":"reports.html#most-units","p":"Reports","s":"Most units sold","t":"most-units\"> The ten items sold in the largest quantity, with Qty sold and Txns (on how many invoice lines it appeared). A cheap item that sells in large numbers shows here even if it is not in the revenue top ten. Quantities of different units (kg, pieces, boxes) are not converted, so compare like with like."},{"u":"reports.html#all-products","p":"Reports","s":"All products","t":"all-products\"> Every item sold in the period, the number in brackets being how many, highest revenue first: Column Meaning Product The item name as on the invoice HSN The HSN or SAC code (the GST code for the goods or service), from the first invoice line that has one Qty sold Total quantity, less returns Revenue Taxable value, without GST Avg rate Revenue ÷ quantity: the average price you really got Txns Number of invoice lines Last sold Date of the latest invoice with it Print / PDF , Excel and CSV export it. Something wrong? The same item appears twice: it was typed with different names on "},{"u":"reports.html#stock","p":"Reports","s":"Stock","t":"stock\"> Closing stock of every product at the end of a month, and what it is worth. Useful at year end (closing stock for your accounts or a bank loan), and to check stock against the shelf. The card is titled Closing stock as on and the date. Choose the month in the box next to the title: this month and the 35 before it. A past month shows its last day; the current month shows today's stock. Column Meaning Product , HSN/SAC , Unit From the product list , A to Z. Unit shows Nos when none is set. Closing qty Worked back from today's stock, using the dates of your invoices, purchase bills and pr"},{"u":"reports.html#tds-tcs","p":"Reports","s":"TDS & TCS","t":"tds-tcs\"> Three lists of tax that is cut from, or added to, a payment, so you can match your books with the income tax department's records and with your CA's returns. Open Reports and click TDS & TCS . New to TDS and TCS? Read GST basics: TDS and TCS first; it explains them with an example. In plain words: TDS (Tax Deducted at Source) : when a business client pays you for contract work, professional fees, rent, commission and the like, it keeps back a small part (for example 10% under 194J) as income tax and deposits it against your PAN . That money is not lost: you claim it in your income ta"},{"u":"reports.html#tds-by-clients","p":"Reports","s":"TDS deducted by your clients","t":"tds-by-clients\"> One row per sales invoice on which the client deducts TDS: Date , Invoice No , Client , the client's PAN (read from its GSTIN), the Section (194J, 194C...), Rate , the Taxable value it is worked out on (the value before GST) and the TDS amount. Under the list, By client and By quarter add them up. How to reconcile it. The TDS a client deducts reaches your PAN only when the client deposits it and files its own TDS return. Check it once a quarter: Pick the quarter Choose the financial year and, say, Q2 (Jul-Sep) . Open your tax statement Log in at incometax.gov.in and open Form "},{"u":"reports.html#tcs-collected","p":"Reports","s":"TCS you collected","t":"tcs-collected\"> One row per sales invoice with TCS: the same columns as above, with the TCS amount, and totals By client and By quarter . This is money you collected for the government: deposit it and report it in your TCS return (Form 27EQ for income-tax TCS; GSTR-8 for GST TCS under CGST section 52). Since 10 July 2024 the section 52 rate is 0.5% (it was 1%); new invoices start at 0.5%, older ones keep the rate they were made with. See GST TDS and GST TCS ."},{"u":"reports.html#tds-on-purchases","p":"Reports","s":"TDS you deducted from suppliers","t":"tds-on-purchases\"> One row per purchase bill on which you ticked TDS deducted : Date , Bill No , Supplier , the supplier's PAN (read from its GSTIN), Section , Rate , Taxable , TDS and what you actually Paid to supplier (bill total less TDS). Under the list, By section and By quarter add them up: these are the figures for your TDS payments and your quarterly TDS return (Form 26Q). Record it on the bill On the purchase bill, tick TDS deducted , pick the section and check the rate (see TDS on a purchase bill ). Deposit it Pay each month's TDS by the 7th of the next month (30 April for March) on "},{"u":"reports.html#cost-centres","p":"Reports","s":"By cost centre","t":"cost-centres\"> A cost centre is a branch, a site or a project: \"Branch: Jalandhar\", \"Site A - Ludhiana\", \"Project Mehta House\". Tag your invoices, purchase bills and expenses with one, and this tab shows what each one sold, spent and earned. The feature is off to start. Turn it on. Settings, Features, under Reports tick Cost centres . Add your cost centres. A Cost centres section appears in Settings, under Features. Type a Name , an optional Code , and click + Add cost centre . Each business has its own list. Tag your documents. The new invoice form (Invoice Details), the purchase bill form an"},{"u":"income-tax.html","p":"Income tax","s":"Income tax helper","t":"Estimate your income tax under the old and new regimes, presumptive taxation (44AD, 44ADA, 44AE), advance tax, bank statement import, and an ITR-4 summary to file from."},{"u":"income-tax.html#which-year","p":"Income tax","s":"Which year the figures are for","t":"which-year\"> The line under the page title says the year: FY 2025-26 · AY 2026-27 . FY (financial year) is the year you earned the money, 1 April 2025 to 31 March 2026. AY (assessment year) is the year after, when you file the return for it. If today falls in a later financial year, an amber banner at the top says These figures are for FY 2025-26, not the current FY ... . It means: The slabs, rebate and capital-gains rates used are those of FY 2025-26. Rates for the newer year are not built in yet, so nothing is worked out with them. The business income filled in from your invoices counts only"},{"u":"income-tax.html#tabs","p":"Income tax","s":"The five tabs","t":"tabs\"> Open Income Tax from the sidebar. The buttons at the top switch between five tabs; rest the mouse on one to see what it does. The small ? at the end of the row opens this guide at the tab you are on. Tab What it does Regime Calculator Old and new regimes side by side, and which costs less Presumptive (§44AD/ADA) Income under sections 44AD, 44ADA and 44AE, without full books Advance Tax The instalments due, and interest for paying late Bank Statement Import Read a bank CSV and sort each transaction ITR Summary The year in one place, and the ITR-4 summary PDF The tabs work together: the P"},{"u":"income-tax.html#regime-calculator","p":"Income tax","s":"Regime Calculator","t":"regime-calculator\"> Since FY 2023-24 every individual can choose between two ways of working out income tax: New regime (section 115BAC) Old regime Rates Lower slab rates, wider slabs Higher slab rates Deductions Almost none: only the standard deduction on salary (₹75,000) and employer NPS, 80CCD(2) 80C (PPF, LIC, ELSS...), 80D health insurance, home-loan interest, donations and the rest; standard deduction ₹50,000 Zero tax up to ₹12 lakh of income (rebate under 87A, up to ₹60,000) ₹5 lakh (rebate up to ₹12,500) How to choose it The default; nothing to do Business owners file Form 10-IEA befor"},{"u":"income-tax.html#your-income","p":"Income tax","s":"Your income","t":"your-income\"> First three questions about you. They change the old-regime slabs and some deduction limits: Box What it changes Your age on 31 March Under 60 , 60 to 79 (senior citizen) or 80 or older (super senior citizen) . Old-regime tax-free limit ₹2.5 lakh, ₹3 lakh or ₹5 lakh. Also the 80D, 80DDB, 80TTA and 80TTB limits. My parents (whose health insurance I pay) are 60 or older Raises the 80D limit for their insurance from ₹25,000 to ₹50,000. I am a government employee Employer NPS, 80CCD(2), allowed up to 14% of salary instead of 10%. Then your income for the year, in rupees: Box What to "},{"u":"income-tax.html#capital-gains","p":"Income tax","s":"Capital gains (special rates)","t":"capital-gains\"> Profit from selling shares or equity mutual funds is taxed at its own rate, not your slab rate, under both regimes: Box What it is Tax STCG on listed equity (§111A) Short-term gain: shares or equity funds held 12 months or less 20% flat LTCG on listed equity (§112A) Long-term gain: held more than 12 months First ₹1.25 lakh free, 12.5% on the rest Gains on property, gold or debt funds are not entered here; ask your CA. With capital gains you may need ITR-2 or ITR-3 instead of ITR-4; see Can you file ITR-4?"},{"u":"income-tax.html#deductions","p":"Income tax","s":"Deductions (Old Regime only)","t":"deductions\"> Each box is an amount you can subtract from income under the old regime. They do not reduce new-regime tax. Under each box is its limit ( Cap ) and what it covers; if you type more than the limit, only the limit is counted. Box For Limit used §80C PPF, ELSS, LIC premium, EPF, children's tuition fees, home-loan principal, NSC ₹1,50,000 §80CCD1B Your own extra NPS contribution ₹50,000 §80D Health insurance for self, family and parents ₹25,000 + ₹25,000; ₹50,000 for each part that is 60 or older §80TTA Savings-account interest, under 60 ₹10,000 (nothing if 60+) §80TTB Bank and post-o"},{"u":"income-tax.html#recommended","p":"Income tax","s":"Recommended regime","t":"recommended\"> The card at the top right says Recommended: NEW Regime (green) or OLD Regime (purple), and Saves you ₹... compared to the other regime . If both cost the same, new is recommended. New recommended : nothing to do. It is the default when you file. Old recommended : with business income, file Form 10-IEA on incometax.gov.in before the return's due date, or the new regime applies anyway. Salaried people without business income choose in the return itself. The Advance Tax tab and the ITR Summary use the recommended regime's tax."},{"u":"income-tax.html#old-vs-new","p":"Income tax","s":"Old Regime and New Regime cards","t":"old-vs-new\"> Each card works out the tax step by step. The recommended one has a coloured border. Line Meaning Gross Total Income Salary after standard deduction, business, house property and other sources added up (capital gains are taxed separately below) Standard Deduction ₹75,000 (new) or ₹50,000 (old) off salary; only if you have salary Chapter VI-A The deductions allowed: all the boxes above for old, only 80CCD(2) for new Taxable Income Income the slabs apply to Slab Tax Tax by the slabs below STCG (20%) , LTCG (12.5%) Capital-gains tax, shown only when you entered gains §87A Rebate The "},{"u":"income-tax.html#presumptive","p":"Income tax","s":"Presumptive income","t":"presumptive\"> \"Presumptive\" means the law presumes your profit is a fixed share of your turnover, so you do not keep full books of account or get them audited. You declare that share (or more) as income and file the simple ITR-4 (Sugam) . Most small shops, traders and professionals use it. Fill in the left card ( Section ), check the right card ( Presumptive computation ), then click Use ₹... as Business Income to send the figure to the Regime Calculator."},{"u":"income-tax.html#presumptive-sections","p":"Income tax","s":"Section: 44AD, 44ADA or 44AE","t":"presumptive-sections\"> Click the button that fits your work. The boxes below change with it. Button For Income presumed Limit §44AD Trading, retail, wholesale and manufacturing 6% of turnover received digitally (UPI, NEFT, RTGS, cheque), 8% of cash turnover ₹3 crore turnover if cash is no more than 5% of it, otherwise ₹2 crore §44ADA Professionals: CA, doctor, lawyer, architect, engineer, consultant 50% of gross receipts ₹75 lakh receipts if cash is no more than 5%, otherwise ₹50 lakh §44AE Transporters owning up to 10 goods vehicles ₹1,000 per tonne per month for each heavy vehicle (over 12,0"},{"u":"income-tax.html#presumptive-computation","p":"Income tax","s":"Presumptive computation","t":"presumptive-computation\"> The right card shows the working: 44AD and 44ADA: Turnover / gross receipts , Deemed income @ 6% / 8% (or @ 50% ), and Declared income : the deemed income, or your actual profit if higher. 44AE: Heavy vehicles (₹1,000 × tonnes × months) , Light vehicles (₹7,500 × months) and Declared income . A yellow box warns when something is wrong: turnover over the limit (you then need regular books, ITR-3 and a tax audit under section 44AB), cash above 5% when that costs you the higher limit, more than 10 vehicles, or an actual profit lower than the presumed share. Use ₹... as B"},{"u":"income-tax.html#why-presumptive","p":"Income tax","s":"Why presumptive taxation?","t":"why-presumptive\"> The box at the bottom right lists what you gain, and the one catch: No full books of account and no tax audit (section 44AB). Advance tax in one go, by 15 March, instead of four instalments. The simple ITR-4 (Sugam) form instead of ITR-3. The catch (44AD): once you opt in, keep using it for 5 years. If you leave early, you cannot come back to 44AD for the next 5 years."},{"u":"income-tax.html#advance-tax","p":"Income tax","s":"Advance tax","t":"advance-tax\"> Advance tax means paying income tax during the year, in parts, instead of all at the end. If your tax for the year, after TDS already cut, is ₹10,000 or more, you must pay it in four instalments: Due by Paid in total by then 15 June 15% 15 September 45% 15 December 75% 15 March 100% If you use presumptive taxation (44AD or 44ADA), you may pay all of it by 15 March instead. Paying late or short costs interest of 1% a month under sections 234B and 234C. You pay advance tax on incometax.gov.in with challan 280 (e-Pay Tax). The tab uses the Total Tax of the recommended regime from th"},{"u":"income-tax.html#advance-schedule","p":"Income tax","s":"Advance Tax Schedule","t":"advance-schedule\"> The top card. It says Based on your recommended NEW Regime total tax of ₹... . Item What it does Presumptive (pay 100% by 15 March) Tick it if you use 44AD or 44ADA: the schedule becomes one instalment on 15 March. TDS already deducted Tax already cut from your salary, interest, rent or contract payments. Find it in Form 26AS or the AIS on incometax.gov.in. Total tax liability , Less: TDS credit , Net advance-tax liability The tax, the TDS, and what is left to pay as advance tax. If what is left is under ₹10,000, a green note says no advance tax required and nothing else sho"},{"u":"income-tax.html#advance-payments","p":"Income tax","s":"Payments made","t":"advance-payments\"> Record each advance-tax payment you have made, so the schedule and the interest are right. Add a line Click + Add payment . A line appears with today's date. Date Change it to the date on your challan. Amount Type what you paid. Remove The × at the end of a line removes it. \"No advance-tax payments recorded yet.\" shows until you add one. The payments are remembered in this browser."},{"u":"income-tax.html#interest-234","p":"Income tax","s":"Interest under §234B / §234C","t":"interest-234\"> What paying late or short costs, worked out from the schedule and your payments: §234C — installment shortfall : 1% a month on what was short at each date, for 3 months (1 month for the March instalment). The June and September instalments are forgiven if you paid at least 12% and 36% by then. §234B — post year-end delay (1% per month) : if by 31 March you had paid less than 90% of the tax, 1% a month on what is unpaid, from 1 April until today. Total interest : the two added up. Shortfalls are rounded down to the nearest ₹100 first, as the rules say. The interest is an estimate"},{"u":"income-tax.html#bank-import","p":"Income tax","s":"Bank statement import","t":"bank-import\"> Turn a year of bank transactions into the figures the calculator needs: interest, rent received, 80C and 80D payments, business receipts. Download a CSV From net-banking or your bank's app, save the statement for the year as CSV. Excel files must be saved as CSV first; PDFs are not accepted. Drop it in Drag the file onto the box Drop a bank-statement CSV here or click to select , or click it and choose the file. SBI, HDFC, ICICI, Axis, Kotak, PNB and Yes Bank formats are recognised, and most others with Date, Narration, Debit, Credit and Balance columns work too. It is read on yo"},{"u":"income-tax.html#bank-csv","p":"Income tax","s":"How to get the CSV","t":"bank-csv\"> Shown under the drop box until you import a file: Net-banking : Accounts, Statements, download as CSV (or as Excel, then open it in Excel and save as CSV). Mobile app : Account statement, Share, Export CSV. Choose the dates of the financial year, 1 April 2025 to 31 March 2026. The file is read in your browser; nothing is sent to a server. Import one account at a time. For two accounts, import the first, push it, then import the second and push it."},{"u":"income-tax.html#bank-review","p":"Income tax","s":"Reviewing the transactions","t":"bank-review\"> After the import the card is titled with the bank and the count, such as HDFC — 412 transactions . Below it, a strip of coloured totals per category, then a table with Date , Description , Debit (red), Credit (green) and Category . The app guesses each category from the words in the description; change any by picking from the Category box on its row. The totals follow. Category Guessed from words like On push Salary income salary, payroll Not pushed (enter salary from Form 16) Business receipts Never guessed: set it on your sales receipts Added to Business / Professional Income B"},{"u":"income-tax.html#itr-summary","p":"Income tax","s":"ITR Summary and the ITR-4 PDF","t":"itr-summary\"> The whole year in one place, for the business selected in the sidebar. Four cards at the top, for FY 2025-26, all without GST: Card From Sales excl. GST (FY 2025-26) Your rupee invoices, less credit notes; estimates, challans and cancelled invoices left out. TCS is taken out too. Trading Purchases Your purchase bills , taxable value Business Expenses Your expenses without GST, except Personal / Drawings and Asset Purchase Net Business Income Sales less purchases less expenses (never below zero)"},{"u":"income-tax.html#income-breakdown","p":"Income tax","s":"Income breakdown","t":"income-breakdown\"> Sales, less trading purchases and business expenses, gives = Net business income . Then what you typed in the calculator: + Salary declared , + Rent received , + Other sources and + Capital gains (STCG + LTCG) . These last four are greyed when empty. If you entered expenses under Asset Purchase (a computer, a machine, furniture), a note says they are not deducted here: an asset is written off over the years as depreciation (section 32). Ask your CA for the depreciation figure and enter it as a business expense. The net business income here is from your books. It is not copie"},{"u":"income-tax.html#tax-snapshot","p":"Income tax","s":"Tax snapshot","t":"tax-snapshot\"> Recommended regime , Tax under NEW Regime (or OLD), Tax under other regime and You save vs other regime , all from the Regime Calculator. Below, a grey box. If your sales are under ₹2 crore and your business type is not professional, it says You may qualify for Section 44AD presumptive taxation ; see the Presumptive tab. It also gives the due dates: 31 July 2026 for the return when no audit is needed, 31 October 2026 with a tax audit, and the advance-tax dates."},{"u":"income-tax.html#itr4-pdf","p":"Income tax","s":"ITR-4 (Sugam) Filing Summary PDF","t":"itr4-pdf\"> Download ITR-4 Summary makes a PDF with each ITR-4 field worked out, in the order of the form, to copy into incometax.gov.in or hand to your CA: Assessee : business name, GSTIN and PAN from Settings . Part A — General : PAN (or \"Fill from your profile\"), filing status, Aadhaar reminder. Nature of Business : the presumptive section and turnover, when you filled the Presumptive tab. B — Income : salary less standard deduction, house property, business (the presumptive income if you filled that tab, otherwise the calculator's figure), other sources, gross total income. C — Deductions :"},{"u":"income-tax.html#not-included","p":"Income tax","s":"Not included yet","t":"not-included\"> The last card lists what the helper does not do, so you know what to get elsewhere: reading Form 16, a capital-gains module with broker imports, a house-property module for several properties, ITR-1, ITR-2 and ITR-3, the ITR JSON file the portal uploads, and Form 26AS reconciliation. File the return itself on incometax.gov.in or through your CA."},{"u":"settings.html","p":"Settings","s":"Settings","t":"Every tab of Settings, card by card, in the order the tabs appear: Business type, Company, Profiles, Terms, Print & PDF, Features, Stock, Region, App lock, Backups, Google Drive, Import/Export and Updates. Each card in the app has a ? next to its title that opens the matching part of this page."},{"u":"settings.html#save-bar","p":"Settings","s":"Settings tabs and the Save all changes bar","t":"save-bar\"> Open Settings from the sidebar. Settings is split into tabs , a row of buttons at the top of the page: Business type , Company , Profiles , Terms , Print & PDF , Features , Stock , Region , App lock , Privacy & internet , Backups , Google Drive , Import/Export and Updates . Click one to show that tab. The tab you are on is filled in blue. On a phone or a small screen the buttons wrap onto two or three lines; nothing is hidden. The app remembers the tab you had open until you close the browser tab, so coming back to Settings opens the same tab. The ? buttons. The ? at the top right o"},{"u":"settings.html#business-type","p":"Settings","s":"Business type","t":"business-type\"> The first tab. Pick what kind of business you run, and the app shows the screens and features that business needs and hides the rest, so the menu stays short. Use it when you first set the app up, or when the menu shows things you never use. The card shows Your business type: with the type that is saved now, or Not chosen yet . The Business type tab. The saved type is shown in blue; the Save all changes bar is at the bottom. Pick a type Click one of the seven cards. Each says in one line who it is for. Check what will change A yellow box, Not saved yet , lists what will be turn"},{"u":"settings.html#company-details","p":"Settings","s":"Company Details","t":"company-details\"> The first card on the Company tab: your business name and address, printed at the top of every invoice. Fill it in once when you start. Change it if you move, get a GSTIN, or change your phone number. Field What to put Business Name * Your shop or company name, as it should print. The only field you must fill. Country India for most users. The list follows your Region . Changing the country changes the names of the fields below (for example VAT number instead of GSTIN). Address Street, building and area. Two lines are enough. City, PIN Code Your town and 6-digit PIN code. Sta"},{"u":"settings.html#gstr-details","p":"Settings","s":"GSTR filing details","t":"gstr-details\"> A grey box inside Company Details, shown only when the country is India. It is used for one thing: the GSTR-1 and GSTR-3B JSON files you upload to the GST portal. Field What it does Aggregate turnover (AATO) is above ₹5 crore Tick it if your total sales last year, for all your GSTINs together on one PAN, were more than ₹5 crore. The line below then says 6-digit HSN : every item needs an HSN code of at least 6 digits. Unticked, 4 digits are enough. The GST portal refuses a GSTR-1 where an HSN is too short. Save with Save Profile or Save all changes . (Older versions also asked fo"},{"u":"settings.html#lut","p":"Settings","s":"LUT for exports and SEZ supplies","t":"lut\"> A second grey box inside Company Details, shown only when the country is India. Fill it in if you export, or sell to units in a Special Economic Zone (SEZ), without charging IGST . What a LUT is. A Letter of Undertaking (form GST RFD-11 ) is a promise to the GST department that you will follow the export rules. With a LUT, exports and SEZ supplies are billed without IGST (they are \"zero-rated\"), so you do not pay the tax and then wait months for a refund. Without one, you must charge IGST and claim it back. It is free, filed online in a few minutes, and valid for one financial year : fil"},{"u":"settings.html#payment-accounts","p":"Settings","s":"Payment Accounts: bank and UPI","t":"payment-accounts\"> The bank accounts and UPI IDs your clients pay into. The default one prints in the bank details block of every new invoice; with a UPI ID, rupee invoices also carry a QR code the client scans to pay the exact amount. Add every account you use: you pick which one goes on each invoice. Add the first account Click + Add account . A form opens; see Add account for each field. Save the account Click Save account . The account appears in the list. The first account is marked ⭐, the default. Add more if you have them Each one you add is listed under the first. Accounts save themsel"},{"u":"settings.html#add-account","p":"Settings","s":"Add account and Edit account","t":"add-account\"> The form that opens from + Add account or the pencil on an account. Field What to put Label (shown in the dropdown) Your own name for the account, such as HDFC Current — 1234 . Only you see it, in the account picker. Account Holder Name The name the bank has on the account. Leave it blank to use your business name. Fill it in when they differ, for example a proprietor's own name. Bank Name Such as State Bank of India. Account Type Optional: Savings, Current, Cash Credit (CC), Overdraft (OD), NRE or NRO. Account Number The full number. The list shows only the last digits. Outside "},{"u":"settings.html#paid-from-abroad","p":"Settings","s":"Getting paid from abroad","t":"paid-from-abroad\"> Two optional boxes in a payment account help clients outside India pay you: SWIFT / BIC : the code a foreign bank needs to send money to your bank. Ask your bank for it; it is printed with the bank details. IBAN : Indian banks do not use IBANs. Fill this only if you have an account abroad that has one (for example a Wise or Payoneer euro account). It prints under SWIFT. Purpose code : the RBI code for what the money is for. The bank asks for it on every payment from abroad: the client's bank when sending, or your bank when it credits you and issues the FIRC / e-BRC. Pick fro"},{"u":"settings.html#invoice-numbers","p":"Settings","s":"Invoice Number Format","t":"invoice-numbers\"> How your invoice numbers look, and where they start. Set it before your first real invoice. You can change it later; numbers already given never change. The box at the top, Next tax invoice: , shows exactly the number your next tax invoice will get, and changes as you change the settings below. With a brand prefix it also shows the next quotation, delivery challan and credit note. Format Style Button Looks like When to use it Branded Sequential INV/2026-27/0001 The default. Numbers start again each financial year. Simple Sequential INV/0001 One running number, no year. Random"},{"u":"settings.html#own-numbering","p":"Settings","s":"Shared numbering or own numbering for this business","t":"own-numbering\"> Shown under Numbering for your business when you have more than one business in Business Profiles . Every business uses Shared numbering to start: one series for all of them. The line below names who shares it, such as Shared by Firm 1, Firm 2 ; saving a change then asks Change numbering for all 2 businesses? To keep one business's numbers separate: Select the business Pick it at the top of the sidebar. Choose own numbering Click Own numbering for this business . Give it a prefix Type a Prefix for this business , such as its initials KS . It is required and must differ from eve"},{"u":"settings.html#number-customize","p":"Settings","s":"Customize prefix, separator & padding","t":"number-customize\"> Click ⚙ Customize prefix, separator & padding under the format to open it. The defaults are fine for most businesses. Setting What it does Brand Prefix Up to 10 capital letters and digits, such as ACME . Tax invoices print it alone ( ACME/2026-27/0001 ); every other document adds its type ( ACME-QUO/… , ACME-DC/… , ACME-CN/… ). Leave it empty to use each type's own prefix: INV, QUO, EST, BOS, COMP, CN and DC. With own numbering, the business's prefix is set above instead. Separator The mark between the parts: / , - or # . Include Financial Year Yes ( 2026-27 ), Short ( 26-27"},{"u":"settings.html#branding","p":"Settings","s":"Branding: logo, signature and stamp","t":"branding\"> The last card on the Company tab. Your logo prints at the top of the invoice, and your signature and company stamp (seal) at the bottom, above the signatory line. Upload Click Upload Logo , Upload Signature or Upload Stamp and pick a picture from your computer: PNG or JPG, up to 5 MB. The message says Logo uploaded — click Save Profile to keep it. Set the size Drag the slider under the picture between S and L. Logo 24 to 80 pixels high (48 to start), signature 30 to 110 (60), stamp 30 to 120 (70). Save Click Save Profile or Save all changes . Until you save, the pictures are not kep"},{"u":"settings.html#sign-layout","p":"Settings","s":"Signature and stamp layout","t":"sign-layout\"> Appears under the stamp once both a signature and a stamp are uploaded. It decides where the stamp goes: Side by side : the signature and stamp next to each other. The default. Stamp above the signature : the stamp on top, the signature under it. Stamp on the signature : the stamp printed over the signature, as a real rubber stamp often is. The white Preview box below shows the result at the sizes you set. Save with Save Profile or Save all changes ."},{"u":"settings.html#business-profiles","p":"Settings","s":"Business Profiles","t":"business-profiles\"> The Profiles tab. If you run more than one business, or more than one GSTIN, save each one as a profile and switch between them. Each profile keeps its own name, address, GSTIN, bank accounts, logo, signature and stamp. Each saved profile is a card with its name, state and GSTIN, and its address. The one in use has a blue border and an Active badge. Button What it does + Add New Profile Saves the business now on the Company tab into the list first (so it is never lost), then opens the Company tab with an empty form for the new business. Save as Profile Saves the Company tab"},{"u":"settings.html#multiple-businesses","p":"Settings","s":"More than one business: separate books","t":"multiple-businesses\"> Each business has its own books . Invoices, totals, purchases, expenses, receipts, recurring invoices, reports and GST returns all follow the business selected at the top of the sidebar. Manage profiles… there opens the Profiles tab. Your client list is shared by all businesses. Records made before you had several businesses show under all of them until you assign them ."},{"u":"settings.html#terms","p":"Settings","s":"Terms & Conditions Templates","t":"terms\"> The Terms tab. The terms you print at the bottom of invoices, such as payment due dates, interest on late payment and returns, kept as templates so you pick one instead of typing it each time. On a new invoice your first template is loaded for you; see Terms and notes on an invoice . Quick Start Under Quick Start — Pick a template for your business , one click adds a ready-made set of Indian terms: Services (IT, Consulting, Freelance) , Goods & Products (Retail, Wholesale) , Manufacturing & Trading , Export / International or Freelancer (Simple) . It is saved straight away; clicking th"},{"u":"settings.html#print-settings","p":"Settings","s":"Print & PDF","t":"print-settings\"> The Print & PDF tab sets the look of every printed invoice and PDF: designs, thermal receipts, watermarks, copies, colours, languages and formats. It has its own page with a section for each card: Print and PDF settings ."},{"u":"settings.html#features","p":"Settings","s":"Features","t":"features\"> The Features tab: what shows in the menu and on the screens, and in what order. Turn off what you never use to keep the app simple, or turn on extras such as Purchase orders or E-invoicing. Tick and untick Tick what you want to see and untick what you do not. A yellow box, Not saved yet , lists what will be turned on and off. Save Click Save all changes at the bottom. Only then does the menu change. Discard undoes your ticks. Unticked things disappear from the menu and the screens. Nothing is deleted : your data is kept, and ticking it again brings it all back. Each switch has a lin"},{"u":"settings.html#features-menu","p":"Settings","s":"Menu: show, hide and reorder","t":"features-menu\"> The Menu part lists every item of the sidebar in two boxes, Top of the menu and Bottom of the menu , in the order they appear, and a third box, Buttons at the top right , for the User Guide, Notifications, Lock and Dark mode buttons. The tick box shows or hides the item. The ▲ and ▼ arrows on the left move the item up or down. Default order , shown once you have moved something, puts the menu back in the usual order. Dashboard , New invoice , Clients , Settings , Help & Support and Lock app (shown only when a PIN is set) say (always shown) and have no tick box. You can still mo"},{"u":"settings.html#features-inside-screens","p":"Settings","s":"Features inside screens","t":"features-inside-screens\"> Switches for parts of a screen, grouped by the screen they appear on: Screen Switch What it shows Invoice screen TDS / TCS Tax deducted or collected at source on an invoice. See TDS and TCS . E-way bill The button to download the e-way bill file for goods you send. E-invoicing (IRN) Only if your yearly turnover is above ₹5 crore. Off to start. See E-invoicing . UPI QR code The scan-to-pay QR code on invoices. Purchases screen Purchase orders Orders to suppliers, turned into bills when goods arrive. Off to start. See Purchase orders . GSTR-2B matching Matching your pur"},{"u":"settings.html#stock","p":"Settings","s":"Low-stock alerts","t":"stock\"> The Stock tab. Warns you when a product is running out, so you reorder in time. It powers the 🔔 bell at the top right and the low-stock list on the Dashboard, and the Products screen colours a product amber when it is at or below the number you set. Turn it on or off Show low-stock alerts is ticked to start. Pick the threshold Click a chip: 0 (only when fully out), 3 (very tight), 5 (recommended) or 10 (loose), or type any number from 0 in the box. The line above says Alert when stock ≤ 5 . Save Click Save on the card, or Save all changes . The message Low-stock alert settings saved a"},{"u":"settings.html#region","p":"Settings","s":"Region Preference","t":"region\"> The Region tab. Choose whether you bill only in India, only abroad, or both. It changes the country lists and which features you see. Your data is not touched, and you can change it any time. Button What you get 🇮🇳 India only GST, rupees first, GSTR-1 and 3B, e-way bill, UPI QR code. 🌍 International VAT and other tax names, several currencies, no India-only features or switches. 🌐 Both / Auto All countries, chosen on each invoice. The default. Click one: it saves straight away, with the message Region preference: … . No Save button is needed. Region, Print & PDF and your other dis"},{"u":"settings.html#lock","p":"Settings","s":"App lock (PIN)","t":"lock\"> The App lock tab. For a computer other people also use: the app asks for a 6 or 8 digit PIN each time it opens. It is off to start. The card says whether it is on. Turning it on Start Click Turn on PIN lock . Choose the length Under Digits , pick 6 or 8. Type the PIN twice In New PIN and New PIN again . Only digits are accepted. Save Click Save PIN . The message PIN saved. It is asked each time the app opens. appears. This browser tab stays unlocked; other tabs and the next start ask for it. When it is on Lock now locks the app straight away, when you step away. So do Lock on the Dashbo"},{"u":"settings.html#privacy-internet","p":"Settings","s":"Privacy & internet","t":"privacy-internet\"> The Privacy & internet tab says, in one table, everything the app uses the internet for and when. Tick Offline mode and the app never goes online by itself: no update check, no automatic copy of each PDF to Google Drive. Check for Updates and other things you click still work when you click them. It also tells you how to check this yourself in two minutes. The full answer is on Is it safe? ."},{"u":"settings.html#backups","p":"Settings","s":"Backups","t":"backups\"> The Backups tab holds the Backup Management + Trash Bin card: the automatic daily backups ( Backup now , Restore , Delete ), a folder on another drive for a second copy of each, and the trash bin for deleted invoices. Each part is explained on the Backups page: Daily backups and restoring one Keeping a copy in another folder Trash bin"},{"u":"settings.html#google-drive","p":"Settings","s":"Cloud Backup (Google Drive)","t":"google-drive\"> The Google Drive tab. Keeps a copy of your invoice PDFs in your own Google Drive, so you can open them from your phone or another computer, and they survive if this computer is lost. Easiest Way — Google Drive for Desktop (Recommended) No setup in the app is needed. Install Google Drive Click Download Google Drive for Desktop on the card (free, from Google) and install it. Sign in With your Google account. A Google Drive (G:) drive appears on your computer. Sync the PDFs Move the app's Saved Invoices folder into Google Drive, or set Google Drive to back up that folder. Done Ever"},{"u":"settings.html#google-drive-api","p":"Settings","s":"Advanced: Direct API Upload","t":"google-drive-api\"> For people comfortable with Google Cloud. Click Advanced: Direct API Upload (for developers) to open it. It lets the app upload each invoice PDF itself, and save a copy of an exported backup to Drive. Make a Client ID Click Open Google Cloud Console , create a project, enable the Drive API, and create an OAuth Client ID of type Web application , with the app's address as an allowed origin. The card shows that address in grey; it is the one in your browser's address bar, such as http://localhost:… . Paste it Into Google OAuth Client ID . It ends in .apps.googleusercontent.com"},{"u":"settings.html#data","p":"Settings","s":"Import/Export (Data Management)","t":"data\"> The Import/Export tab. Export Backup… saves your data to one file you keep anywhere; Import Backup… brings a file back. Your data stays on your computer: nothing is sent to us. Step by step: Export Backup and Import Backup ."},{"u":"settings.html#updates","p":"Settings","s":"App Updates","t":"updates\"> The Updates tab. Checks whether a newer version of the app is out, and installs it. Check Click Check for Updates . It needs internet. Next to the button you see Current: v… | Latest: v… . Update If there is a newer version, a green box says New version v… is available! . Click Update Now . Wait The message says Updating… your data is backed up first. This takes about a minute. Reload When it says Update finished , reload the page ( F5 ) to use the new version. Your invoices, data and saved PDFs are never touched by an update. For the other ways to update, see Updating . Something wr"},{"u":"backup.html","p":"Backups and updates","s":"Backups, updates and moving PC","t":"Your data is plain files on your own computer. Here is how it is backed up, how to keep a copy somewhere safe, update the app, and move to a new computer."},{"u":"backup.html#where-data-lives","p":"Backups and updates","s":"Where your data is","t":"where-data-lives\"> Everything is in the _system\\data folder inside the app's folder. The installer hides _system to keep things tidy; in File Explorer, turn on View, Show, Hidden items to see it. Open Data Folder in the Control Panel opens it for you. Downloaded PDFs are also kept in the app's Saved Invoices folder, one folder per client."},{"u":"backup.html#automatic-backups","p":"Backups and updates","s":"Daily backups (Backup Management)","t":"automatic-backups\"> Every day the app copies all your data, invoices, clients, products, purchases, expenses, settings and the trash, into a dated backup, and keeps the last 30 days. The first backup of the day is made a few seconds after the app starts, and a computer left on overnight makes the next one soon after midnight. You do not have to do anything. They are on the Backups tab of Settings, in the 💾 Backup Management + 🗑 Trash Bin card: Part of the card What it does Backup now Makes today's backup straight away, for example before a big change. The message says Manual backup triggered"},{"u":"backup.html#restore-daily-backup","p":"Backups and updates","s":"Restoring a daily backup","t":"restore-daily-backup\"> Each row of 📅 Daily backups shows the date and time it was made, and also in your backup folder when a second copy exists. Use Restore when something went badly wrong, for example many records deleted by mistake, and you want all your data back as it was on that day. Pick the day Find the last day your data was right and click Restore on its row. Confirm The app asks Restore all data from backup …? and explains that it overwrites your current data. Click Restore backup . Reload When it says Backup restored — please reload the page , press F5 . Before restoring, the app "},{"u":"backup.html#backup-copy","p":"Backups and updates","s":"Keeping a copy somewhere else","t":"backup-copy\"> Every day, automatically, on another drive. On the Backups tab of Settings, under Also keep a copy of every daily backup in this folder : Type a folder On another drive, a USB disk or a synced folder, such as D:\\ReazixBilling or E:\\ . Save it Click Save folder . The app checks it can write there and copies today's backup at once. The message says where the copies go. Each daily backup is then also copied into Reazix Billing Backups\\ date inside that folder, keeping 30 days. The line under the box shows where. If a copy fails (a USB disk not plugged in), the card says so in red. S"},{"u":"backup.html#export-import","p":"Backups and updates","s":"Export Backup and Import Backup (Data Management)","t":"export-import\"> On the Import/Export tab of Settings, the Data Management card saves your data to one file, or brings a file back. Use it to keep a copy on a pen drive, to move data to another computer, or to bring back just your clients or products from an older backup. Your data is on this computer only. Nothing is uploaded to us or anyone else; the only time anything leaves your computer is when you tick Also save a copy to my Google Drive , which goes to your own Drive. The file is plain text (JSON) you can keep anywhere. Export Backup… : see Export Backup . Import Backup… : see Restore fr"},{"u":"backup.html#export-backup","p":"Backups and updates","s":"Export Backup","t":"export-backup\"> Open it Click Export Backup… . A window lists every part of your data, all ticked. Choose what to include Untick anything you do not want. Select all and Clear all tick or untick every one. Google Drive copy (optional) Tick Also save a copy to my Google Drive if you set up Direct API Upload . Download Click Download Backup . The file reazix-backup- date .json goes to your Downloads folder. Copy it somewhere safe. Part What is in it Active business profile Name, address, GSTIN, bank, logo, signature All business profiles Every business in Business Profiles Invoices / bills Tax i"},{"u":"backup.html#restore-from-backup","p":"Backups and updates","s":"Restore from Backup","t":"restore-from-backup\"> Pick the file Click Import Backup… and choose a .json backup file. Check what is in it The Restore from Backup window shows when the file was made and, for each part, how many items it holds. Parts the file has are ticked; empty parts say empty and cannot be ticked. Choose what to restore Untick anything you want to keep as it is now. Select all (with data) and Clear all help. Restore Click Restore selected . The message lists what came back, such as Restored: 120 invoice(s), 45 client(s) . Records in the file replace the matching records in the app; records the file does"},{"u":"backup.html#trash","p":"Backups and updates","s":"Trash bin","t":"trash\"> Invoices deleted from a client's account on the Clients screen, or from the invoice list, go to the trash for 30 days, then are removed for good. They are listed under 🗑 Trash bin on the Backups tab of Settings, with the invoice number, client and date deleted. Restore puts the invoice back where it was. The stock its delete returned is taken out again. The message says Invoice restored . Delete forever removes it and its PDF straight away, after asking. This cannot be undone. For an invoice already given to a client, cancel it instead of deleting it, so its number stays in your recor"},{"u":"backup.html#move-pc","p":"Backups and updates","s":"Moving to a new computer","t":"move-pc\"> On the old computer Click Export for Move in the Control Panel , or Move to another PC in the launcher under More options . It saves your data and settings as one ZIP on your Desktop. Copy it to a pen drive or cloud storage. On the new computer Install the app as usual. Bring your data in In the new Control Panel, click Choose Backup ZIP under Restore Backup and pick the file. You can use an exported backup file instead: export on the old computer, and import it in Settings on the new one. One computer at a time Do not run the same data on two computers at once, for example through a"},{"u":"backup.html#update","p":"Backups and updates","s":"Updating","t":"update\"> Any of these installs the newest version: The Update to v… button that appears in the sidebar when a new version is out. It shows what changed, with Update Now , Remind me later and Skip this version . Update Now in Settings, App Updates . Update Now in the Control Panel . In the launcher, More options , then Update to the latest version . Every update first saves a backup of your data in Documents\\Reazix Billing Backups , then replaces the app. It never touches your data folder or your saved PDFs. It takes about a minute; reload the page when it finishes. To update by hand instead: d"},{"u":"control-panel.html","p":"Control Panel","s":"Control Panel","t":"Update, back up, restore, move to another PC, open your folders, and stop the app, from inside the app."},{"u":"control-panel.html#about","p":"Control Panel","s":"What it is","t":"about\"> Control Panel in the sidebar does the launcher's jobs without leaving the app. At the top it shows your system, Node.js version, the port the app runs on, and how much space your data takes."},{"u":"control-panel.html#actions","p":"Control Panel","s":"The buttons","t":"actions\"> Card Button What it does Update Software Update Now Downloads the latest version. Your data is backed up first and never touched. Backup Data Create Backup Saves your data as a dated ZIP in Documents\\Reazix Billing Backups . Restore Backup Choose Backup ZIP Pick a backup ZIP to restore. What you have now is saved first, as a safety net. Move to Another PC Export for Move Saves your data and settings as one ZIP on your Desktop. See Moving to a new computer . Open Data Folder Open Opens the folder with your bills, clients, products and settings. Open Backups Folder Open Opens Documents"},{"u":"control-panel.html#each","p":"Control Panel","s":"Each button in detail","t":"each\"> One section per card: what it does, when to use it, what to click, and what to do if something looks wrong. Nothing here deletes your bills, clients or products. Anything that changes your data saves a copy first."},{"u":"control-panel.html#update","p":"Control Panel","s":"Update Software","t":"update\"> What it does. Downloads the newest version from billing.reazix.com and puts it in place of the old one. Your data folder is not changed. When to use it. When a new version is out or a problem you reported has been fixed. You need internet. Click Update Now . The button shows Updating... ; wait until it finishes. It can take a few minutes. Windows: a black window opens. It first saves a backup of your data, pre-update- date .zip , in Documents\\Reazix Billing Backups , then downloads and applies the update. It ends with [OK] Update complete! Mac and Linux: it does the same, saving the b"},{"u":"control-panel.html#backup","p":"Control Panel","s":"Backup Data","t":"backup\"> What it does. Saves all your bills, clients, products and settings as one dated ZIP file, backup- date_time .zip , in the Documents\\Reazix Billing Backups folder (Mac and Linux: Documents/Reazix Billing Backups ). When to use it. Before a big change, at the end of the month, or any time you want a copy to keep on a pen drive. The app also makes its own daily backup; this is an extra one at a moment you choose. Click Create Backup . It shows Backing up... for a moment. The result panel below says Backup - OK , with the file name and size in its output. A folder window usually opens wit"},{"u":"control-panel.html#restore","p":"Control Panel","s":"Restore Backup","t":"restore\"> What it does. Replaces the data in the app with the data from a backup ZIP you choose. When to use it. After moving to a new computer, or to go back to how things were on an earlier day. It works with ZIPs made by Create Backup or Export for Move . Windows. Click Choose Backup ZIP . A file window opens in your Reazix Billing Backups folder. Pick the ZIP and click Open . (Close the window to cancel; nothing changes.) The app first saves what you have now as pre-restore- date .zip in the same folder. This is your way back if you chose the wrong file. It then replaces the data with the "},{"u":"control-panel.html#move","p":"Control Panel","s":"Move to Another PC","t":"move\"> What it does. Saves your data as one ZIP on your Desktop named MOVE-ReazixBilling- date_time .zip , ready to carry to a new computer. When to use it. When you buy a new computer, or want the same books on a second one. Windows: click Export for Move . A black window shows the progress and the size, then a folder window opens with the ZIP highlighted on your Desktop. Copy the ZIP to a pen drive, or send it to yourself by email or cloud storage. On the new PC, install the app ( Install guide ), open the Control Panel and use Choose Backup ZIP ( Restore Backup ) to pick this file. Mac and "},{"u":"control-panel.html#restart","p":"Control Panel","s":"Restart the App","t":"restart\"> What it does. Turns the app off and on again in a few seconds, then reloads the page by itself. When to use it. When something is not working: a page will not load, a button does nothing, or after an update or restore. Save any bill you are typing. Then click Restart . The button shows Restarting... . After a few seconds the page reloads with the app running again, on the same address. Is it safe? Yes. Everything is saved as you work. A bill still being typed and not saved is not kept. Something wrong? If it says the app did not come back within 30 seconds, open it again from its Des"},{"u":"control-panel.html#stop","p":"Control Panel","s":"Stop Server","t":"stop\"> What it does. Turns the app off. The page stops answering until you open the app again. When to use it. After an update or restore, so the new version or data is loaded when you start it again. Also when the app seems stuck, or you want to shut it down cleanly. Finish and save any bill you are typing. Then click Stop Server . Windows: it finds the app's process on your port and ends it. Mac and Linux: the app stops itself a moment after replying; the result panel says Stopped. Open the app again from its icon or launcher. The browser page will then show errors such as \"Failed to fetch\"."},{"u":"control-panel.html#remove","p":"Control Panel","s":"Remove the App","t":"remove\"> What it does. Uninstalls Reazix Billing from this computer in one go: the app, its Desktop and Start-menu icons (Mac: the app in Applications; Linux: the menu entry) and the start-with-computer entry. You choose what else goes. Click Remove… . A list opens below the cards. (On Windows the launcher window has the same: More options → Remove the app... .) Tick what to delete as well. Nothing is ticked at first, so by default only the program goes and your books stay : My invoices, clients, products and settings : the data folder, with the daily backups inside it. Saved invoice PDFs : th"},{"u":"control-panel.html#result","p":"Control Panel","s":"The result panel","t":"result\"> After you click an action, a panel appears at the bottom with a green tick and OK , or a red mark and Failed , next to the action's name. A short pop-up message appears too. Output : what the script printed, such as where a backup file was saved. Errors : shown only when something went wrong. Copy this text when you report a problem . A red line of text: the reason in plain words, for example that the script is not in the app folder. The panel is cleared each time you click another button, so it only describes the last action. Something wrong? Check \"Not available here\" , a backup or "},{"u":"control-panel.html#scripts-missing","p":"Control Panel","s":"\"Update and backup scripts not found\"","t":"scripts-missing\"> The Control Panel runs scripts that come with the downloaded ZIP, in the _system folder. This message appears when they are missing, for example when the app was started from source code or copied without them. Install from the downloaded ZIP to get them, or use Export Backup in Settings for your data. Versions 1.10.44 to 1.10.71 showed this message, then called \"Launcher scripts not detected\", on every installed copy by mistake. Update to 1.10.72 or later using the launcher's Update to the latest version . On Linux and macOS only Update and Backup have scripts, so Restore, M"},{"u":"print-settings.html","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Print and PDF settings","t":"The app-wide defaults for how every invoice looks on paper and in a PDF: business-type presets, designs, thermal receipts, copies, watermarks, fonts, colours, languages and formats. Each part of the Print & PDF tab in Settings has a ? that opens its section here. Each invoice can still override the basics from its own Customize panel."},{"u":"print-settings.html#how-it-saves","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Print & PDF Settings: how they save","t":"how-it-saves\"> Open Settings and click the Print & PDF tab. Use it once when you start, to make your invoices look the way you want, and again whenever you change printer or paper. There is no Save button: every change is kept the moment you make it. The Live preview on the right updates as you change things, using a sample invoice with your business name, so you can see the effect without touching a real invoice. On a narrow screen the preview moves below the settings. Three buttons sit at the top of the card: Button What it does 🚀 Run setup wizard Shows the first-run setup wizard again the "},{"u":"print-settings.html#business-type","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Business type","t":"business-type\"> The first box, ⚡ Business type . Picking the kind of business you run sets a dozen or so print settings in one go, and hides options that do not apply to you. Use it first; every setting below stays editable afterwards. Pick a type Click a card. The app asks Apply \"…\" preset? and says how many settings it will change. Confirm Click Apply preset . The card is marked ACTIVE and the preview changes. Business type Set up for Main settings it applies Retail Shop / Kirana A counter with a thermal printer Bold capitals, prints straight after saving, \"Qty × Rate\" lines, no HSN, \"Thank "},{"u":"print-settings.html#visual-style","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Visual style","t":"visual-style\"> The second box, 🎨 Visual style : eight ready-made designs that set the colours and type for both PDFs and thermal receipts in one click. Each card shows a small invoice in its own colours; the one in use is marked ACTIVE . Click a card to use it, then change anything below. Design Suits Look Aurora Freelancers, tech Cool slate with electric blue Editorial Law, consulting Charcoal on warm ivory, capitals Executive Enterprise, B2B Deep navy with soft champagne Whisper Designers, studios Off-white, one hairline, nothing else Sunset Retail, cafes, salons Warm terracotta on cream, w"},{"u":"print-settings.html#thermal","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Thermal receipts","t":"thermal\"> Four groups, Typography , Layout , Content and Footer , that only affect 58 mm and 80 mm receipt printers (the small roll printers at shop counters). A4 and A5 PDFs are not changed by them. They are hidden when your business type prints A4 or A5 PDFs (Freelancer, Service, Wholesale, Manufacturing); a grey note says so. Pick Retail or Restaurant, or Show all options , to see them. For setting a printer up from scratch, see Thermal receipt printing . Switch the preview to Thermal (80mm) to see your changes."},{"u":"print-settings.html#thermal-typography","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Typography (Thermal receipts)","t":"thermal-typography\"> Setting Options Default Font family Monospace (Courier), made for thermal printers, or sans-serif (like Arial). For A4/A5 PDFs use PDF font family . Monospace Font size Small (fits more), Medium, Large, Extra Large (easier for older customers) Medium Font weight Normal, Bold, Ultra bold. Thermal heads print bold much darker, so bold is recommended. Bold ALL CAPS mode Every line in capitals, like big supermarket receipts Off"},{"u":"print-settings.html#thermal-layout","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Layout (thermal)","t":"thermal-layout\"> Setting Options Default Line spacing Compact (saves paper), Normal, Comfortable Normal Header alignment Centre, or left Centre Thermal ink darkness Standard, Dark (for older printers), Extra-dark. Darkens the logo and QR code so faded prints come out darker. Standard Force ALL CAPS in header Business name always in capitals On"},{"u":"print-settings.html#thermal-content","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Content (thermal)","t":"thermal-content\"> Tick or untick what prints on the receipt: Show business logo , Show HSN code per item (needed on GST tax invoices; turn off for informal counter receipts), Show \"Qty × Rate\" line per item , Show amount in words , Show bank details and Show UPI QR code . All are on to start. With the QR on, UPI QR size is Small, Medium (the default) or Large. With both HSN and \"Qty × Rate\" off, items print as a compact single line."},{"u":"print-settings.html#thermal-footer","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Footer (thermal)","t":"thermal-footer\"> Setting What it does Default Custom footer message Printed above the cut line. Leave blank for none. \"Thank you for your business!\" Show cut mark (\"✂ cut here\") For printers without an automatic cutter. Turn off if yours cuts by itself. On Feed lines after cut None, 1, 2, 3, 4 or 6 blank lines so the paper tears cleanly 2 Show tagline A line of your choice under the business name, typed in Tagline text Off"},{"u":"print-settings.html#pdf-features","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"PDF & universal print features","t":"pdf-features\"> The grey box 📄 PDF & universal print features holds the groups below. They apply to every paper size, A4, A5, Letter, Legal and thermal, unless a group says otherwise. Each group title has its own ? . Some groups only show for certain business types : Multi-copy for Wholesale and Manufacturing, Customer feedback QR and Reprint tracking for Retail and Restaurant, Dual currency for Freelancer and Service. With no business type chosen, everything shows."},{"u":"print-settings.html#auto-print","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Auto-print","t":"auto-print\"> Auto-print on save : with this on, Save & Download also sends the invoice straight to your default printer, with no extra click. Made for busy shop counters. Off by default. It can also be turned on for one client only, in their details."},{"u":"print-settings.html#watermark","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Watermark","t":"watermark\"> A large, faint diagonal word across every page of the PDF, such as PAID or DRAFT. Turn it on Tick Show watermark . More settings appear. Choose the word Pick one under Watermark text : PAID, DUPLICATE (the default), DRAFT, OVERDUE, COPY, ORIGINAL, CANCELLED or REPRINT. Or tick Use custom text instead of preset and type your own in Custom watermark text , such as FOR INTERNAL USE. Choose how strong Opacity : very faint (5%) to very strong (40%); medium (15%) is the default. If you choose your own text and leave the box empty, no watermark prints. Watermarks are never printed on ther"},{"u":"print-settings.html#copies","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Multi-copy (GST rule 48)","t":"copies\"> GST rules expect three copies of an invoice for goods (for the buyer, the transporter and yourself) and two for services. Tick Print multiple copies with labels and choose the Number of copies : 2 (Original + Duplicate, for services) or 3 (Original + Duplicate + Triplicate, for goods; the default). The PDF then holds every page once for each copy, labelled in a small box at the top right: ORIGINAL FOR RECIPIENT DUPLICATE FOR TRANSPORTER TRIPLICATE FOR SUPPLIER Shown for the Wholesale and Manufacturing business types, or with none chosen."},{"u":"print-settings.html#multi-page","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Multi-page invoices","t":"multi-page\"> Setting What it does Default Page numbers on pages 2+ Prints \"Page 2 of 3\" at the bottom right of the second page onwards. The first page is not numbered. On Business name header on pages 2+ Repeats your business name, with a line under it, at the top of every page after the first On Both only appear when an invoice runs to more than one page. Page breaks always fall between rows, and never through the signature, stamp or an image."},{"u":"print-settings.html#margins","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Print margins (mm)","t":"margins\"> Top , Bottom , Left and Right , in millimetres, from 0 to 100 (all 0 to start). Use them when printing on pre-printed letterhead paper, to move the invoice clear of the printed logo, or to leave room for binding. For example, a top margin of 40 starts the invoice 4 cm down the page."},{"u":"print-settings.html#verification-codes","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Verification codes","t":"verification-codes\"> Invoice number as QR : an 18 mm QR code at the bottom right of the last page, captioned \"Verify invoice\". It holds the invoice number, or, if you type a Verification URL (optional) such as https://mycompany.com/verify/{invoice_number} , that address with the number filled in. Off by default. Invoice number as barcode text : prints the invoice number large, in a typewriter font, at the bottom left of the last page, for filing. It is text, not a scannable barcode. Off by default. Neither is the GST e-invoice QR code; that comes with E-invoicing ."},{"u":"print-settings.html#feedback-qr","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Customer feedback QR","t":"feedback-qr\"> Tick Feedback / review QR to print a QR code at the bottom left of the PDF that opens any web address, such as your Google review page or a WhatsApp chat. Paste the address in URL to encode ; it only prints once an address is entered. Label above QR , \"Rate us · Give feedback\" unless you change it, prints with the code. Shown for the Retail and Restaurant business types, or with none chosen."},{"u":"print-settings.html#signature","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Digital signature","t":"signature\"> A default signature, used when a business has none of its own. Show signature on invoice is on to start. Upload a picture (PNG, JPG, WebP or SVG, up to 2 MB) with Upload signature ; Remove signature takes it off. Signatory name , such as Rakesh Kumar · Director , prints under it; left blank, the business name is used. A signature and stamp uploaded in Settings, Branding for a business take priority over this one."},{"u":"print-settings.html#terms-page","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Terms & Conditions on a separate page","t":"terms-page\"> Print T&C on a separate page moves long terms and notes to a page of their own, instead of squeezing them under the totals. Only affects invoices that have terms. Off by default. Your terms themselves are kept in Terms & Conditions Templates ."},{"u":"print-settings.html#pdf-font","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"PDF font family","t":"pdf-font\"> Font used in generated PDFs : Helvetica (clean, the default), Times New Roman (traditional and formal), or Courier (typewriter style). It applies to A4, A5, Letter and Legal PDFs; thermal receipts have their own font setting ."},{"u":"print-settings.html#thermal-compatibility","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Layout & printer compatibility","t":"thermal-compatibility\"> Compact upper header (fit more items on page 1) : tightens the space above the items table so more rows fit on the first page. Use it when invoices often spill onto page 2. Off by default. Thermal buffer-safe mode : for cheap or old receipt printers that jam or stop half-way on large print jobs. Prints in black and white at lower quality. Off by default. Thermal print method : Direct HTML , the default, sends sharp text straight to the printer. If your printer or browser mishandles it, choose Via PDF ."},{"u":"print-settings.html#prefixes","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Custom prefix per invoice type","t":"prefixes\"> Each document type numbers separately, with a built-in prefix: INV for Tax Invoice, QUO for Quotation, EST for Proforma / Estimate, BOS for Bill of Supply, COMP for Composition, CN for Credit Note and DC for Delivery Challan. Type your own in the box next to a type to replace it: letters, numbers, hyphens and underscores only, up to 8 characters. Leave it blank to use the built-in one. A new prefix starts its own count from 1. The rest of the number (year, separator, digits) follows Invoice Number Format ."},{"u":"print-settings.html#reprint","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Reprint tracking","t":"reprint\"> Show REPRINT badge on reprints : once an invoice has been printed before, this prints a red \"REPRINT · Copy #2\" (and so on) at the top of each page, so a copy cannot pass as the original. Off by default. The app counts every print either way. Shown for the Retail and Restaurant business types, or with none chosen."},{"u":"print-settings.html#pdf-quality","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"PDF quality vs file size","t":"pdf-quality\"> Print quality : Draft (about half the file size, fine for email and WhatsApp), Standard (balanced), or HD (sharpest text, largest file, best for printing and keeping). HD is the default."},{"u":"print-settings.html#dual-currency","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Dual currency display","t":"dual-currency\"> For rupee invoices to clients abroad. Tick Show foreign-currency equivalent to show the total in a second currency too. Secondary currency : USD, EUR, GBP, AED, SGD, AUD or JPY. Rate (1 USD = ? INR) : you set it, 83 to start. There is no live exchange rate; update it yourself. Display position : on a line below the ₹ amount, or in brackets after it. Shown for the Freelancer and Service business types, or with none chosen. On an invoice billed in another currency (for example US dollars), the same switch adds the rupee total to the invoice's EXCHANGE RATE line, at that invoice's"},{"u":"print-settings.html#letterhead","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Company letterhead","t":"letterhead\"> If you have printed stationery, upload it as a picture and invoices print on top of it. Turn it on Tick Use pre-printed letterhead image . Upload Under Upload letterhead , pick a PNG, JPG or WebP picture of the full A4 page, up to 3 MB. Until you do, a yellow warning says the switch does nothing yet. Avoid printing your details twice Hide invoice header block , on by default, drops the app's own header because the letterhead already has your name and address. Remove letterhead takes the picture off. Use Print margins to keep the invoice clear of the letterhead's printed parts."},{"u":"print-settings.html#template","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"PDF template style (visual design)","t":"template\"> Template changes the header and table style of A4 and A5 PDFs: Modern (a coloured header, the default), Classic (professional), Minimal (lots of white space), Corporate (formal blue), Minimalist (grey), Boxed grid (ruled boxes, like a quotation pad) and Tally style (order boxes, an HSN tax summary and a declaration). A design chosen under Visual style sets this for you. Thermal receipts have their own compact layout."},{"u":"print-settings.html#print-darkness","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Print darkness","t":"print-darkness\"> Force darker text on printed PDF darkens grey labels and addresses so they do not fade on paper printers. On by default. It only changes the PDF, not the screen. Turn it off if your printer already prints greys crisply."},{"u":"print-settings.html#pdf-font-scale","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"PDF font scale","t":"pdf-font-scale\"> A slider for the Overall size of the PDF, from 80% to 140% (100% to start). Smaller fits more on a page; larger is easier to read. The on-screen preview always shows 100%; download a PDF to see the result."},{"u":"print-settings.html#colours","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"PDF Style Editor: your own colours","t":"colours\"> To match your brand, tick Use custom colours and set six colours with the colour picker or a hex code such as #1e40af . The preview changes as you go. Reset colours to defaults undoes them. Colour Used for Primary text Client name, item names, totals Muted text Labels, addresses, dates and numbers Accent colour Section titles and the table header Accent text Text on the accent colour, usually white Header background Behind the business name and invoice title Divider lines Lines between sections and table rows Keep text dark on a light background so it prints clearly."},{"u":"print-settings.html#labels-language","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Section labels and language","t":"labels-language\"> Language preset prints the section labels in English, Hindi, Tamil, Marathi or Bengali. You can also type your own wording for six labels: BILL TO , PLACE OF SUPPLY , BANK DETAILS , AMOUNT IN WORDS , TERMS & CONDITIONS and NOTES . The grey text in each box shows the current wording. Your own wording wins over the language; clear the box to go back."},{"u":"print-settings.html#formats","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Formatting: date, number, currency","t":"formats\"> Setting Options Date format 02 Apr 2026 (Indian, the default), 02-Apr-2026, 02/04/2026, 04/02/2026 (US), 2026-04-02, or ISO 8601 Number grouping 1,00,000.00 (Indian, the default), 100,000.00 (Western), 100.000,00 (European) Decimal places 0, 2 (the default), 3 or 4 Currency symbol position Before the number (₹100, the default) or after it"},{"u":"print-settings.html#round-off","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Totals: round off invoice totals","t":"round-off\"> Under 🧮 Totals . Round off invoice totals : when on, new invoices round the grand total to the nearest rupee and print the difference as a Round-off line, such as −0.40. It is on for new installs and saves as soon as you click. You can still turn it off for one invoice in Customize , under Totals. Changing it never alters invoices you have already saved."},{"u":"print-settings.html#row-density","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Row density","t":"row-density\"> Vertical spacing in tables + sections : Compact (fits more per page), Normal (the default) or Comfortable (easier to read). It changes both the PDF and the on-screen preview."},{"u":"print-settings.html#tax-rates","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Custom tax rate presets","t":"tax-rates\"> The built-in GST rates are 0, 0.1, 0.25, 3, 5, 12, 18, 28 and 40%. Since 22 September 2025 most goods are at 5%, 18% or 40%; 12% and 28% stay for older invoices (see GST basics: what rate do I charge? ). Add your own, such as 1.5% or 7.5%: type the numbers separated by commas, such as 1.5, 7.5 , and click Add . Each must be between 0 and 100. They appear in the rate list on every invoice. The × next to a rate removes it."},{"u":"print-settings.html#templates","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"My saved templates","t":"templates\"> Save your whole print setup under a name, so you can switch between setups (for example one for A4 and one for the receipt printer). Reset defaults clears the saved templates too. Name it Type a name, such as Retail v1 . Save it Click Save current as template . It appears in the list. Load brings one back after asking. It replaces your current settings, so save the current setup first if you want to keep it. The bin deletes a template."},{"u":"print-settings.html#preview","p":"Print and PDF settings","s":"Live preview","t":"preview\"> On the right of the tab (below the settings on a narrow screen). Three tabs: 📄 PDF (A4) , 🖨 Thermal (80mm) , and ⊞ Split view with both side by side. It shows a sample invoice numbered TEST/PRINT/0001 with three items, using your business name, so terms and notes are not shown. Some settings, such as font scale , only show in a downloaded PDF."},{"u":"shortcuts.html","p":"Getting around","s":"Getting around the app","t":"The sidebar, switching business, notifications, quick search with Ctrl + K, keyboard shortcuts and dark mode."},{"u":"shortcuts.html#sidebar","p":"Getting around","s":"The sidebar","t":"sidebar\"> From top to bottom: Your business , with a pencil to edit it. If you have more than one, click the name to switch . The screens : Dashboard, New Invoice, Clients, Products, Expenses, Purchases, Recurring, Receipts, Cash book, Reports, GST Returns and Income Tax. Features you turn off disappear from here. Update to v… , when a new version is out. Help & Support , Control Panel and Settings . A dot on Control Panel : green when the app is running, red when it is not (hover over it to read which). At the end of the Dashboard, below the invoices, a small line shows the app's version, a l"},{"u":"shortcuts.html#support","p":"Getting around","s":"Help & Support","t":"support\"> How to reach Reazix: Email contact@reazix.com opens your email program, and reazix.com opens our website. The page also explains your updates, has Report a problem and Ask for a feature (both open an email to us), What's new and the Problem log. See Help & Support ."},{"u":"shortcuts.html#switch-business","p":"Getting around","s":"Switching business","t":"switch-business\"> With more than one business saved, click its name at the top of the sidebar and choose another. Every screen changes to that business's invoices, purchases, expenses, receipts, recurring invoices, reports and returns. Manage profiles… opens Settings ."},{"u":"shortcuts.html#notifications","p":"Getting around","s":"Notifications","t":"notifications\"> The 🔔 bell at the top right of every screen has a small red count when something needs you. It is your daily to-do list: who has not paid, what is due soon, which return to file, what to re-order. The app works it out by itself when it opens and again every 10 minutes; nothing is sent to you by SMS or email. Click it to open the Notifications window. Each line is a button: click it and the window closes and takes you to the screen where you deal with it. Line What it means Clicking it opens 🔁 N recurring invoices auto-generated today The app made invoices from your recurring "},{"u":"shortcuts.html#command-palette","p":"Getting around","s":"Quick search: Ctrl + K","t":"command-palette\"> Press Ctrl + K anywhere, even while typing, and start typing. You can: go to any screen, or start a new invoice; open an invoice by its number or client; find a client by name or GSTIN, or a product by name or HSN, which opens their list; jump to Settings, switch dark mode, or see what is new in an update. Open it Press Ctrl + K (Mac: ⌘ + K ). A box opens with Type a command or page name… Type a few letters For example gst , an invoice number such as 0012 , or part of a client's name. The list narrows as you type. Pick one Move with ↑ ↓ and press Enter , or click it. The box "},{"u":"shortcuts.html#keyboard","p":"Getting around","s":"Keyboard shortcuts","t":"keyboard\"> Ctrl + K Quick search Ctrl + N New invoice Ctrl + S Save the invoice (on the invoice screen) Ctrl + P Download the PDF (on the invoice screen) Ctrl + Shift + L Lock the app (when a PIN is set) Ctrl + / Show or hide the Keyboard Shortcuts window, which lists these Esc Close a dialog Enter Confirm a dialog On the invoice screen there are more: see Keyboard shortcuts on this screen . On a Mac, use ⌘ instead of Ctrl ."},{"u":"shortcuts.html#dark-mode","p":"Getting around","s":"Dark mode","t":"dark-mode\"> The moon button at the top right of every screen switches the app to dark colours, and the sun button switches back. Invoices and PDFs always print in their normal colours. The Dashboard in dark mode. The sun button at the top right switches back."},{"u":"shortcuts.html#install-as-app","p":"Getting around","s":"Opening it like a desktop app","t":"install-as-app\"> It already is one. The Reazix Billing icon (the blue R ) on your Desktop and in the Start menu starts the app and opens it in its own window, with no tabs or address bar. Don't use the browser's own Install app button (in Chrome or Edge's address bar). That makes a second icon which opens a window but cannot start the app, so after a restart it only shows \"Needs a Quick Start\". If you have one, right-click it and choose Uninstall ."},{"u":"shortcuts.html#app-not-running","p":"Getting around","s":"\"Needs a Quick Start\"","t":"app-not-running\"> If the app's engine is not running, the page says Reazix Billing Software Needs a Quick Start . Your data is safe. Double-click the Reazix Billing icon on your Desktop or in the Start menu: it starts the app, and the page carries on by itself once it is running. An app icon made by Chrome or Edge cannot start the app; use ours, and remove the other one (right-click it, then Uninstall )."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"Troubleshooting and questions","t":"Every message the app, the launcher and the installer can show, what it means, and the steps to fix it yourself."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#installing","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"Installing","t":"installing\"> Messages from the launcher and the black install window, the first time you set the app up."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#files-missing","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"\"Please extract the ZIP first\" or \"Some files are missing\"","t":"files-missing\"> You may see: \"Please extract the ZIP first\" , \"Some files are missing\" , \"The _system folder is not next to this launcher\" , \"_system folder is missing. Please re-extract the ZIP or re-download from billing.reazix.com.\" (Mac and Linux), \"Missing file: start-windows.ps1\" or \"Could not find start-windows.ps1\" . The launcher was opened from inside the ZIP, or the ZIP was only partly extracted, so the rest of the app is not next to it. Close the launcher. Right-click the ZIP and choose Extract All… . Open the extracted Reazix-Billing folder and double-click the launcher there. Keep"},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#windows-protected","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"\"Windows protected your PC\"","t":"windows-protected\"> Windows shows this the first time for any program without a paid certificate. Nothing is wrong. Click More info , then Run anyway . If it still will not open, right-click the launcher, choose Properties , tick Unblock and click OK . See \"Windows protected your PC\" ."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#install-failed","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"The install stopped with an error","t":"install-failed\"> The black window shows PROBLEM: and what went wrong. Fix it, then click Install again; it carries on where it stopped. \"The app cannot reach the internet to download its packages\" , \"Could not download Node.js\" or \"The download did not work\" : the first install needs the internet. Check the connection (open any website). On an office network, a proxy or firewall may block it; ask whoever runs the network to allow registry.npmjs.org and nodejs.org . \"The app packages did not install\" : the internet, disk and folder look fine, so antivirus is the usual cause. Add the Reazix-Bill"},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#already-installed","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"\"Already installed on this computer\"","t":"already-installed\"> You may see: \"Already installed on this computer\" in the launcher, or \"Reazix Billing is already installed on this computer, in: ...\" in the black window. You extracted a new ZIP into a new folder. Your invoices are in the copy it names, so it does not make a second, empty copy. Click Update the installed copy . It uses the files you just extracted, so no download is needed. When it finishes, open the app from your Reazix Billing shortcut as usual. The new folder is not needed after that. You can delete it."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#old-node","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"\"Node.js is too old\" or \"npm ERR!\"","t":"old-node\"> You may see: \"The Node.js v... on this PC is too old for this app\" , \"Node.js v... on this machine is too old\" , \"npm ... on this machine is too old\" , \"Unsupported engine\" , npm ERR! , a file named npm-debug.log , or \"SyntaxError: Unexpected token\" when the app starts. The app runs on Node.js 18 or newer (with npm 7 or newer). An older Node.js on the computer cannot install or run it. Windows, v1.10.81 or newer: click Install or Open App again, with the internet on. The app fetches a current Node.js into its own folder by itself (about 30 MB, once) and leaves your other Node.js alo"},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#starting","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"Starting the app","t":"starting\"> The launcher or the browser cannot reach the app, or the app asks for a PIN."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#not-answered","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"\"Still starting...\" or \"The server has not answered in 90 seconds\"","t":"not-answered\"> You may see: \"Still starting... (30 seconds. The first start after an update is the slow one.)\" , \"The server has not answered in 90 seconds\" , or, on versions before v1.10.69, \"Server did not respond in 15s\" . The first start after an install or update is slow, because antivirus checks every new file. Wait a minute, then open http://localhost:47371 in your browser. If it does not open, close the black window and click Open App again. From v1.10.81 this also finishes an install that an update left half done. If the window shows a PROBLEM: above that line, the entries under The i"},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#cannot-connect","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"\"Failed to fetch\", \"App Not Running\" or \"Needs a Quick Start\"","t":"cannot-connect\"> You may see: \"Failed to fetch\" (Chrome, Edge), \"NetworkError when attempting to fetch resource\" (Firefox) or \"Load failed\" (Safari), often after words like Restore failed: or Export failed: ; a red dot on Control Panel in the menu; a page saying \"Reazix Billing Software Needs a Quick Start\" ; \"Could not check the PIN. Is the app still running?\" ; or the browser's own \"This site can't be reached\" or a blank page. The app's engine (the server on your computer) is not running: the computer was restarted, the app was stopped, or it closed. Nothing already saved is lost. Double-cli"},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#port-in-use","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"\"Port 47371 is busy\" or \"address already in use\"","t":"port-in-use\"> You may see: \"Port 47371 is busy, trying 47372...\" , EADDRINUSE or \"address already in use\" . These lines only appear when the app is started from a Terminal or Command Prompt. Another program, or a second copy of Reazix Billing, already uses that port (the \"door\" the browser knocks on). The app picks the next free one by itself and saves it in data\\port.txt ; the launcher reads that file, so Open App goes to the right address. Always open the app with its Reazix Billing icon (or the launcher's Open App ), not a bookmark of localhost:47371 , which may now be the other program. If"},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#pin-forgotten","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"PIN problems: \"Wrong PIN\" or a forgotten PIN","t":"pin-forgotten\"> You may see: \"Wrong PIN. Try again.\" , \"Too many wrong tries. Wait 30 seconds and try again.\" (after 5 wrong PINs in a row), \"Could not check the PIN. Is the app still running?\" , or in Settings \"Current PIN is wrong\" , \"The two PINs do not match\" , \"The PIN must be 6 digits\" (or 8). The PIN lock asks for the PIN once per browser tab. \"Could not check the PIN\" means the app is not running: see Failed to fetch . Forgot the PIN? It can be removed on this computer without losing anything: Open the Reazix-Billing folder, the one with the launcher in it. Make a new empty file there "},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#updating","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"Updating","t":"updating\"> Problems during or right after an update. An update never changes your data folder, and backs it up first."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#update-failed","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"An update went wrong","t":"update-failed\"> You may see: \"Update failed — ...\" in the app, \"ERROR: could not reach billing.reazix.com. Are you online?\" , \"Could not check for updates. Check internet connection.\" , or \"The new version is in place, but it is not ready to run yet\" . Your data folder is never changed by an update, and a backup was saved in Documents\\Reazix Billing Backups before it started. Check the internet, then run the update again. This fixes most problems. If the window showed a PROBLEM: , fix that first (see The install stopped with an error ), then click Open App : it finishes the install by itself. "},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#update-not-showing","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"\"Update complete\", but the old version is still there","t":"update-not-showing\"> You may see: \"[OK] Update complete! Restart the app (Stop Server -> Open App) to run the new version.\" or \"Update finished. Reload the page to use the new version.\" The new files are in place, but the running app or your browser still has the old version. Press Ctrl + F5 (Mac: ⌘ + Shift + R ). Still the old number at the bottom of the Dashboard? Stop the app (launcher, More options → Stop the app , or Stop Server in the Control Panel), then click Open App . If the app does not start after that, see The server has not answered ."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#app-out-of-date","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"\"Failed to fetch dynamically imported module\"","t":"app-out-of-date\"> You may see: \"Failed to fetch dynamically imported module\" , \"error loading dynamically imported module\" or \"Loading chunk ... failed\" , or a screen that will not open after an update. The browser kept parts of the old version after an update. The app normally reloads itself once to fix this. Press Ctrl + F5 (Mac: ⌘ + Shift + R ). If it comes back, close every tab of the app, then open it again from its Reazix Billing icon."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#scripts-not-found","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"\"Update and backup scripts not found\" or \"Not available here\"","t":"scripts-not-found\"> You may see: \"Update and backup scripts not found.\" in the Control Panel, buttons that say Not available here , or \"Not available here: the script for this action is not in the app folder. Download the latest ZIP to get it.\" The Control Panel runs scripts that come with the downloaded ZIP, and they are not in this copy. On Mac and Linux only Update and Backup have scripts, so Restore, Move and Stop always say Not available here. Update with the launcher's More options → Update to the latest version , or by hand with the downloaded ZIP . For your data in the meantime, use Ex"},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#saving","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"Saving and working in the app","t":"saving\"> Messages while making invoices, saving settings or importing."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#screen-problem","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"\"This screen ran into a problem. Your data is safe.\"","t":"screen-problem\"> One screen of the app hit an error and was stopped, so the rest of the app keeps working. Nothing that was already saved is lost. Click Try again . If the panel comes back, click Go to Dashboard and carry on with other work. Click Report this problem so it gets fixed. The report is filled in for you, and private details (GSTIN, PAN, phone, email, UPI ID and bank account numbers) are removed before it leaves. You can read it before you send it."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#duplicate-number","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"\"Invoice number ... already exists\"","t":"duplicate-number\"> You may see: \"Invoice number INV/0007 was already used — saved as INV/0008 instead.\" , \"Invoice number ... already exists. Change it before saving.\" , \"Invoice number ... is already used by another invoice. This invoice is still saved as ...\" , \"A bill with this invoice number already exists\" , or \"An invoice with this number exists again. Rename or delete it first.\" (restoring from the trash). Two invoices cannot share a number, and the app never overwrites the other one. A new invoice simply moves on to the next free number by itself. For an invoice you are editing, change"},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#payload-too-large","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"\"Request body too large\"","t":"payload-too-large\"> Usually after Failed to save , Restore failed: or Import failed: . Something you saved was bigger than the app accepts in one go: up to 5 MB for an everyday save, up to 500 MB for restoring a backup file. The usual cause is a very large logo, signature or stamp picture, because every invoice keeps a copy of your business details with their pictures. Make the picture smaller, ideally under 500 KB: crop it to just the logo or signature, or save it as a JPG. A free site such as tinypng.com can shrink it. Upload the smaller picture in Settings and save. Try what failed again. F"},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#disk-full","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"\"The disk is full\"","t":"disk-full\"> You may see: \"The disk is full\" , ENOSPC , \"no space left on device\" , \"Drive C:\\ is almost full\" (install), or \"the disk is full\" in an update message. The drive the app is on has no free space, so the app could not write. The app writes each file in full or not at all, so nothing already saved is lost or half-written. Free some space: empty the Recycle Bin (Mac: Bin), delete old downloads and videos you do not need. Backups you have already copied somewhere else can be deleted from Documents\\Reazix Billing Backups . Try again."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#no-permission","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"\"The app is not allowed to write to its data folder\"","t":"no-permission\"> You may see: \"The app is not allowed to write to its data folder\" , \"The app cannot write to its own folder\" (install), EACCES , EPERM , \"permission denied\" or \"operation not permitted\" . Windows or antivirus is stopping the app from changing its own files. Usual causes: the app folder is inside C:\\Program Files , on a read-only or synced drive, or antivirus Controlled folder access blocks it. Stop the app (launcher, More options → Stop the app ). Move the whole Reazix-Billing folder to Documents or D:\\ , and open the launcher from there. The old Desktop shortcut points at the "},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#csv-import","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"A CSV import did not work","t":"csv-import\"> You may see: \"CSV file is empty or has no data rows\" , \"Failed to parse CSV file\" , \"Could not read ...\" , \"Import stopped after ...\" , or for bank statements \"Could not parse this CSV\" or \"No transactions found\" . The file is not a plain CSV, or its first row is not the column headings. In Excel, use File → Save As → CSV (Comma delimited) . An .xlsx file renamed to .csv does not work. Keep the column headings in the first row and the data from the second row down. After \"Import stopped after ...\", the rows before it are saved. Fix the row the message names and import the rest. Fo"},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#ocr-failed","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"Reading a bill photo failed","t":"ocr-failed\"> You may see: \"OCR failed: ...\" , \"Please upload an image (PNG, JPG, WebP).\" or \"Image is over 8MB\" . Use a sharp, straight, well-lit JPG or PNG under 8 MB, cropped to the bill. If the message mentions fetch , network or worker , press Ctrl + F5 and try again; if it persists, see Failed to fetch . If it still fails, enter the bill by hand."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#printing","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"Printing and PDFs","t":"printing\"> Print does nothing, or the PDF is not right."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#print-blocked","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"Print does nothing, or \"Print failed\"","t":"print-blocked\"> You may see: \"Your browser blocked the print window. Allow pop-ups for this app and try again.\" , \"Allow pop-ups for this page to print the report\" , \"Print failed — try Download PDF instead\" , \"Failed to generate PDF.\" or \"Could not generate any PDFs\" . Allow pop-ups for the app: click the blocked pop-up icon at the right end of the address bar, choose Always allow for localhost , and try again. Use Download PDF and print the PDF instead. Press Ctrl + F5 and try again. For receipt printers, see Receipt printer problems ."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#pdf-file-in-use","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"\"Its PDF in Saved Invoices could not be updated\"","t":"pdf-file-in-use\"> You may see: \"Invoice saved, but its PDF in Saved Invoices could not be updated. Use Save & Download.\" or \"A saved PDF could not be marked CANCELLED. Close the PDF if it is open, then cancel again.\" The invoice itself is saved. Only its PDF copy could not be replaced, usually because that PDF is open in a PDF reader. Close the PDF in Adobe Reader, Edge or your browser. Click Save & Download again, or repeat the cancel or undo."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#missing-on-pdf","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"Something is missing from the PDF","t":"missing-on-pdf\"> Logo, signature or stamp : check it is uploaded and saved in Settings , and ticked under Customize. UPI QR code : needs a UPI ID on the account, a rupee invoice, and UPI QR ticked under Customize. Bank details or PAN : tick Bank details under Customize; the account needs a bank name. Anything on a receipt printer : receipts leave some things out on purpose. See What a receipt leaves out ."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#image-problem","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"A logo or signature picture will not upload","t":"image-problem\"> You may see: \"This doesn't look like an image\" , \"Image is ... MB — over the 5MB cap\" , \"Image too large (max 2MB)\" , \"Image too large (max 3MB)\" , \"Image must be under 500KB\" , or \"Could not decode this image\" . Use a PNG or JPG. An iPhone photo (HEIC) must be turned into a JPEG first: share it to Files as a JPEG, or on the iPhone set Settings → Camera → Formats → Most Compatible for new photos. Make it smaller, ideally under 500 KB: crop it or shrink it with a free site such as tinypng.com. Upload it again."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#gst-returns-problems","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"GST, tax and returns","t":"gst-returns-problems\"> Wrong tax on an invoice, and messages from GST Returns."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#wrong-tax","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"The invoice has the wrong tax split","t":"wrong-tax\"> Check your own state in Settings . Check the client's state , or their GSTIN, which fills the state in. If goods go to a different state from the client's address, set Place of Supply on the invoice. For a client abroad, set their country : it is then an export, charged as IGST. For an SEZ unit, tick SEZ on the client. See How GST is worked out ."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#state-missing","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"\"Set your business State in Settings\"","t":"state-missing\"> You may see: \"Set your business State in Settings — required for correct CGST/SGST vs IGST split.\" or \"Set your GSTIN in Settings first\" (E-Way Bill). The app needs your state to choose CGST + SGST or IGST, and your GSTIN for E-Way Bill files. Open Settings, Company Details . Fill in State (and GSTIN , which fills the state in), and save. Go back to the invoice; the tax is worked out again."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#no-tax","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"No GST is charged at all","t":"no-tax\"> The Tax % column is probably turned off under Customize . Turning it off removes GST from the invoice, and your choice carries over to new invoices. Tick it again. Bills of supply and delivery challans never charge GST."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#gstr1-blocked","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"\"GSTR-1 export blocked — fix these first\"","t":"gstr1-blocked\"> You may also see \"GSTR-1 JSON exported. ⚠ ...\" : the file was made, with warnings worth reading. An invoice number is too long or has characters the portal refuses, or an item has a GST rate the portal does not accept. The message names the first ones. Open the invoice the message names and fix its number or rate. Export again. See Checks before the file is made ."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#gstr2b-wrong-file","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"\"That doesn't look like a GSTR-2B JSON\"","t":"gstr2b-wrong-file\"> You may see: \"That doesn't look like a GSTR-2B JSON. Expected docdata.b2b array.\" or \"Failed to parse GSTR-2B JSON\" . The file chosen is not the GSTR-2B JSON from the GST portal: often the Excel or PDF version, or a different return. On the GST portal, download GSTR-2B for the month as a JSON file. If it comes as a ZIP, extract it first. Choose that .json file. See GSTR-2B ."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#nothing-to-export","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"\"No data to export for this period\"","t":"nothing-to-export\"> You may see: \"No data to export for this period\" , \"No invoices to export\" , \"No B2B data to export\" , \"No TDS entries in this period\" , or \"Nothing to export\" . The chosen period has nothing of that kind for this business. Check the period at the top. Check the business at the top of the sidebar: each business has its own invoices. See Switching business ."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#gst-labels","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"It says VAT instead of GST, or the other way round","t":"gst-labels\"> Change Region in Settings, and check your country in Company Details. Tax names follow the seller's country."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#backups","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"Backups, restore and Google Drive","t":"backups\"> Daily backups, backup files and restoring."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#restore-failed","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"A backup or restore failed","t":"restore-failed\"> You may see: \"This file doesn't look like a Reazix Billing backup.\" , \"Could not read the file\" , \"Import failed: ...\" , \"Restore failed: ...\" , \"Backup failed: ...\" or \"No data folder found - nothing to back up.\" A restore saves what you have now first, so a failed one changes nothing. Read the end of the message: Failed to fetch , Request body too large , disk full and permission each have their own entry. For Import Backup , choose the reazix-backup- date .json file saved by Export Backup. A ZIP from the launcher or Control Panel is restored with Choose Backup ZIP in the Co"},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#backup-folder","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"\"Cannot write to that folder\" (backup copy folder)","t":"backup-folder\"> You may see: \"Give the full folder path, for example D:\\Backups\" , \"Choose a folder outside the app's data folder.\" , \"Cannot write to that folder: ...\" , or \"Folder saved, but copying today's backup failed: ...\" . Type the whole path, starting with the drive letter, such as D:\\ReazixBilling ; on a Mac or Linux, a path starting with / . Choose a folder outside the app's own folder. For a USB disk, plug it in first. Settings says when a copy fails. For a permission code such as EACCES , choose a folder in your own Documents or another drive. See Keeping a copy somewhere else ."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#google-drive","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"Google Drive upload failed","t":"google-drive\"> You may see: \"Google Drive not configured.\" , \"Enter your Google OAuth Client ID first\" , \"Drive auth failed — backup downloaded locally only\" , \"Google Drive: Please reconnect in Settings\" or \"Google Drive upload failed: ...\" . The file was still saved on this computer. Only the copy to Drive did not happen. Check the internet. In Settings, Google Drive , connect again (and fill in the Client ID if it is empty). Save or export again."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#damaged-file","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"\"Skipped damaged file\" in the log","t":"damaged-file\"> You may see a log line like: \"Skipped damaged file data/bills/INV_0007.json (not valid JSON)\" , and that one invoice, client or product is missing from its list. One saved file was damaged, by a power cut, a disk error or editing it by hand. The app skips it so everything else still opens. Note the file name in the line (for example bills/INV_0007.json ). Open the data folder: Open Data Folder in the Control Panel . Open backups , then the newest date folder, then the same subfolder ( bills ). Copy that file. Paste it into the same subfolder of the data folder, replacing the dam"},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#mac","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"Mac","t":"mac\"> Messages macOS shows before the app starts."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#mac-blocked","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"The Mac will not open the launcher","t":"mac-blocked\"> \"could not be executed because you do not have appropriate access privileges\" : open Terminal (Applications → Utilities), type chmod +x with a space after it, drag Reazix Billing - MAC into the Terminal window, press Return , and open the file again. Downloads from v1.10.82 do not need this. See the step-by-step example . \"cannot be opened because Apple cannot check it for malicious software\" or \"unidentified developer\" : the app is not signed by Apple. Hold Control , click Reazix Billing - MAC , choose Open , then Open again. Only the first time. Or use System Settings → Privacy"},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#linux","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"Linux and NAS","t":"linux\"> Messages in the Terminal."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#linux-permission","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"\"Permission denied\" or \"bash: not found\"","t":"linux-permission\"> You may see: \"Permission denied\" when starting ./Reazix Billing - LINUX.sh , or \"bash: not found\" on a NAS. Start it through bash, which needs no permission change: cd ~/Reazix-Billing && bash \"Reazix Billing - LINUX.sh\" . No bash (Alpine, some NAS systems): install it, for example sudo apk add bash . \"Permission denied\" while the app writes files: see The app is not allowed to write ."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#linux-update-failed","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"The Linux update stopped","t":"linux-update-failed\"> The update says ERROR: and, in most cases, \"Nothing was changed.\" If it fails while applying, the old app files are put back. \"Updating needs \"unzip\" (or python3)\" : run sudo apt install unzip (Alpine: apk add unzip ) and update again. \"Could not download the update\" : check the internet and try again. \"could not be extracted (damaged download, or the disk is full)\" : free some space (see The disk is full ) and try again. \"Update Node.js as shown above\" : see Node.js is too old . \"npm install failed.\" : check the internet and the free space, then run sh ~/Reazix-Billing/_"},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#problem-log","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"Problem log and reporting a problem","t":"problem-log\"> The app keeps a list of recent problems on this computer: a save that failed, a screen that went wrong, the app server not answering. Open Help & Support in the sidebar and scroll to the Problem log card. Use it when something did not work and you want to know why, or when you want to send the details to get it fixed. Private details are removed before anything is kept: GSTIN, PAN, phone numbers, email addresses, UPI IDs and bank account numbers. Nothing is sent anywhere unless you click Report . On the card What it is or does The list Newest first. Each line shows the date and t"},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#report-problem","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"Reporting a problem","t":"report-problem\"> In the Problem log, click Report next to the problem (or Report this problem on the panel that showed it). Your email program opens a message to contact@reazix.com, already filled in with the version, your computer and the error details. Private details (GSTIN, PAN, phone, email, UPI ID, bank account) are removed first. Add what you did just before it happened, check the text, and send it. Reporting without the Problem log: the form asks for the version (bottom of the Dashboard, or Settings, App Updates ), your computer, what you did and what you saw, and a screenshot (hide yo"},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#copy-details","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"Sending the details another way","t":"copy-details\"> No email program on this computer? Click Copy details (or Copy in the Problem log), paste it into an email to contact@reazix.com or a WhatsApp message, and add what you did just before it happened. Read it before sending; it is plain text."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#questions","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"Questions","t":"questions\"> Things people ask that are not errors."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#other-devices","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"Can I use it on my phone or another computer?","t":"other-devices\"> The app runs on the computer it is installed on, and only that computer can open it. It has no user accounts, so it is deliberately not shared over your network, where anyone connected could read your books. (The optional PIN lock locks the screen on this computer only.) To work on another computer, move your data there."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#internet","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"Does it need the internet?","t":"internet\"> Only to install and to update. Invoices, reports, GST returns and even reading bills from photos all work offline. Google Drive upload uses the internet too."},{"u":"troubleshooting.html#privacy","p":"Troubleshooting","s":"Is my data sent anywhere?","t":"privacy\"> No. There is no account, no tracking and no server of ours. Your data stays in the app's folder unless you choose Google Drive, which copies files into your own Drive, or you send a problem report yourself. The full answer, with every address the app connects to, is in Is it safe?"},{"u":"limitations.html","p":"What it does not do","s":"What the app does not do","t":"So you can plan around them: the things this app leaves to the government portals, your CA, or other tools."},{"u":"limitations.html#e-invoicing","p":"What it does not do","s":"E-invoicing (IRN and signed QR)","t":"e-invoicing\"> The app does not connect to the Invoice Registration Portal, so it cannot get an IRN or the signed QR code. If your turnover makes e-invoicing compulsory for you, generate the IRN on the IRP and keep it with the invoice."},{"u":"limitations.html#portal-filing","p":"What it does not do","s":"Filing returns for you","t":"portal-filing\"> It makes the GSTR-1 and GSTR-3B files and figures. It does not log in to the GST portal or file anything. You, or your CA, upload and file on gst.gov.in."},{"u":"limitations.html#eway-generation","p":"What it does not do","s":"Generating e-way bills","t":"eway-generation\"> It makes the file for the e-way bill portal. The e-way bill number itself is generated on the portal."},{"u":"limitations.html#not-in-gstr1","p":"What it does not do","s":"Things not in the GSTR-1 file","t":"not-in-gstr1\"> Exports (Table 6A) must be added on the portal with the shipping bill details. Nil-rated, exempt and non-GST supplies (Table 8), such as bills of supply, are not included. Debit notes are not supported as a document type. Advances received before invoicing are not tracked."},{"u":"limitations.html#accounting","p":"What it does not do","s":"Full accounting","t":"accounting\"> There is no double-entry ledger, balance sheet, trial balance, cash or bank book, bank reconciliation or journal entries yet. It covers invoicing, receivables, purchases, expenses, stock and GST. For the rest, give your CA the Excel or CSV exports."},{"u":"limitations.html#multi-user","p":"What it does not do","s":"Several people, or several computers","t":"multi-user\"> There are no user accounts or roles (an optional PIN can lock the screen), and the app only opens on the computer it runs on. One computer holds the books; see moving to a new computer . Hosting it online (Railway, Render, a server) is not supported yet; see why ."},{"u":"limitations.html#income-tax-limits","p":"What it does not do","s":"Income tax","t":"income-tax-limits\"> The income tax helper estimates tax for FY 2025-26, including for seniors (60 to 79) and super seniors (80 and above). It does not file your return or produce the ITR file the portal takes. See Income tax helper ."},{"u":"limitations.html#stock-limits","p":"What it does not do","s":"Stock","t":"stock-limits\"> Stock is one count per product. There are no batches, expiry dates, serial numbers or warehouses. Stock is valued at purchase price in Reports, Stock ."},{"u":"glossary.html","p":"Glossary","s":"Glossary","t":"The GST and tax terms used in the app and in these pages, in plain words."},{"u":"glossary.html#terms","p":"Glossary","s":"Terms A to Z","t":"terms\"> Term Meaning AATO Annual aggregate turnover: your total sales in a year across all your GSTINs on one PAN. B2B / B2C Sales to a GST-registered business / to someone unregistered, such as a consumer. B2C Large An inter-state sale to an unregistered buyer above ₹1 lakh (₹2.5 lakh before 1 August 2024), reported invoice by invoice in GSTR-1. Bill of supply A bill without GST, for exempt goods or services, or from a composition dealer. CGST, SGST, UTGST, IGST Central, State and Union Territory GST are charged together on a sale within one state or territory. Integrated GST is charged on a "},{"u":"support.html","p":"Help & Support","s":"Help & Support","t":"How to reach Reazix, what your purchase includes, and what changed in each update."},{"u":"support.html#contact","p":"Help & Support","s":"Contact Reazix","t":"contact\"> Reazix Billing is made by Reazix . For a question, a problem, or something you need the app to do, email contact@reazix.com . Your invoices stay on your computer: we never see them unless you send them to us. Before sending a screenshot, hide your GSTIN and bank details. In the app, Email contact@reazix.com opens your email program with the subject filled in, and reazix.com opens our website."},{"u":"support.html#updates","p":"Help & Support","s":"Updates","t":"updates\"> Your purchase includes 3 years of updates. When a new version is ready the app tells you: click Update in the sidebar, and your invoices and settings are kept. See Updating the app ."},{"u":"support.html#feedback","p":"Help & Support","s":"Report a problem or ask for a feature","t":"feedback\"> Report a problem : opens an email to us. Say which version, which computer, and what you did. For a problem the app logged, Report in the Problem log is better: it fills in the details for you. Ask for a feature : opens an email to us. Requests from customers decide what comes next."},{"u":"support.html#whats-new","p":"Help & Support","s":"What's new","t":"whats-new\"> The What's new card in the app lists the last six updates, read from the changelog that comes with your copy of the app. The newest is open; click any version number to open or close it. Each shows its date, a one-line summary and the changes grouped under headings such as Added and Fixed . The card shows what your copy contains. If it stops at an older version, you have not updated yet: see Updating the app ."},{"u":"support.html#in-the-app","p":"Help & Support","s":"In the app","t":"in-the-app\"> The same page is in the app: Help & Support , near the bottom of the sidebar. From top to bottom it has Contact Reazix , Updates , Safe and private , Tell us what you need , What's new and the Problem log ."},{"u":"security.html","p":"Is it safe?","s":"Is it safe? Security and privacy","t":"Plain answers for anyone who wonders whether it is safe to keep their business books in it: where your data is, what the app connects to, and how to check it yourself."},{"u":"security.html#your-data-stays","p":"Is it safe?","s":"Your data stays on your computer","t":"your-data-stays\"> Saved as files on your PC. Every invoice, client, product, payment and setting is a file in the _system\\data folder inside the app's folder. Saved invoice PDFs go in the Saved Invoices folder next to it. No account, no login, no signup. The app never asks for an email address or a password to use it. No cloud server. We do not run a server that holds your books. There is nothing of yours on our side to leak or to lose. Google Drive only if you set it up. If you choose to connect your own Google Drive (Settings → Google Drive), copies of your invoice PDFs and backups go to you"},{"u":"security.html#no-internet-needed","p":"Is it safe?","s":"It works without internet","t":"no-internet-needed\"> Everything you do day to day works offline: making and printing invoices, PDFs, payments, stock, purchases, expenses, reports, GSTR-1 and GSTR-3B files, backups, and reading a supplier's bill from a photo (OCR). The app runs on your computer and opens in your browser, but it is not a website. Internet is needed only to install the app, to update it, and for the optional things listed below. When you are offline the app simply skips them; your work is not affected. Everything the app needs to run, even its font, is inside the app folder."},{"u":"security.html#offline-mode","p":"Is it safe?","s":"Offline mode: never go online by itself","t":"offline-mode\"> Click the Wi-Fi button at the top right of any screen and then Turn Offline mode on , or tick Offline mode in Settings → Privacy & internet . The button turns orange, with a line through it, while it is on. From then on the app makes no internet connection by itself: no automatic check for a new version; no automatic copy of each invoice PDF to Google Drive. Things you click still work when you click them: Check for Updates and Update , the ? help pages, Report , WhatsApp and other links, and Save to Drive . The setting is kept in the app's data folder, so the app's own server o"},{"u":"security.html#what-it-connects-to","p":"Is it safe?","s":"Every address the app connects to","t":"what-it-connects-to\"> This is the complete list. Apart from these, the app talks only to itself on your own computer. By itself, while the app is open Address When Why, and what is sent billing.reazix.com (Reazix) About 5 seconds after the app opens, every 6 hours while it stays open, and when you click Check for Updates in Settings Asks billing.reazix.com which version is the newest, so the app can tell you an update is ready. Nothing about you or your business is sent. Offline mode stops it. Only when you do something Address When Why billing.reazix.com (Reazix) When you install, or click Up"},{"u":"security.html#no-tracking","p":"Is it safe?","s":"No tracking, no ads, nothing sent to us","t":"no-tracking\"> No analytics. The app does not count your clicks, screens or invoices, and does not report how you use it. No ads , and no paid version that unlocks features. No data sent to us. We never see your invoices, clients, amounts, GSTIN or bank details. We do not even know how many people use the app."},{"u":"security.html#why-free","p":"Is it safe?","s":"How is Reazix paid? What is the catch?","t":"why-free\"> There is no catch, and your data is not the product. One payment. You buy the app once and use it for life. Your purchase includes 3 years of updates. No servers holding your books. The app runs on your computer, so there is no cloud that holds your data. Tracking you would gain us nothing. We do not sell ads or data, so there is nothing to collect."},{"u":"security.html#network","p":"Is it safe?","s":"Other computers cannot open it","t":"network\"> The app has a small built-in server that your browser talks to. It listens only on this computer's own internal address, 127.0.0.1 , so other computers on your Wi-Fi or office network cannot open the app or read your data. It also refuses requests from other websites: a web page you visit cannot quietly read your books from the app in the background. This is also why several people cannot use it from different computers at the same time. See Several people, or several computers ."},{"u":"security.html#host-online","p":"Is it safe?","s":"Can I put it online, on Railway, Render or a server?","t":"host-online\"> No, please don't try. People ask whether they can host the app on a website service (Railway, Render, a VPS, with Supabase as the database) so they can open it from anywhere. Today that is not safe, and it would not work properly: There is no login on the server. The app was made for one computer, so its server does not ask who you are. The PIN only locks the screen in your browser. Put online, anyone who found the web address could read, change or delete all your invoices, clients and bank details. It only listens on your own computer ( 127.0.0.1 , see above ), so a hosting serv"},{"u":"security.html#check-yourself","p":"Is it safe?","s":"Check it yourself","t":"check-yourself\"> You don't have to trust what we write. Any of these takes a few minutes and needs no technical skill except the last two. Switch the internet off. Turn off Wi-Fi (or unplug the cable), close the app and open it again. Make an invoice, download its PDF, print it, record a payment and open Reports. Everything works. That is because nothing the app does with your books needs the internet. Turn on Offline mode (above) and leave it on. The app then goes online only when you click something that needs it. Watch its connections. On Windows, open Resource Monitor (press Windows key + "},{"u":"security.html#install-safety","p":"Is it safe?","s":"Is the install safe?","t":"install-safety\"> No administrator rights. The install line puts the app in your own user folder (Windows: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\Programs\\Reazix Billing ; Mac: Applications in your home folder). It does not change Windows system files, add a Windows service or ask for an admin password. From the official place only. The install line downloads the script and the app from billing.reazix.com, over a secure (HTTPS) connection. Your data is never touched. Installing over an existing copy backs up your data to Documents\\Reazix Billing Backups first and replaces only the app's own files. Why Windows or the M"},{"u":"security.html#backups-and-lock","p":"Is it safe?","s":"Backups and the PIN lock","t":"backups-and-lock\"> Daily automatic backups. Every day the app copies all your data into a dated backup and keeps the last 30 days. See Daily backups . A copy on another drive. Choose a second folder (another drive, a USB disk, a synced folder) and every daily backup is copied there too, so a failed hard disk does not take your books with it. See Keeping a copy somewhere else . Before every update , the installer and the updater back up your data first. PIN lock (optional). On a computer others use, turn on a 6 or 8 digit PIN in Settings → App lock. The PIN is stored only as a scrambled check v"},{"u":"security.html#problem-reports","p":"Is it safe?","s":"Problem reports","t":"problem-reports\"> When something goes wrong, the app notes it in the Problem log on your computer. Nothing is sent anywhere by itself. Only when you click Report does it open an email to Reazix in your email program, filled in with the error and your app, browser and computer type. Before that, private details are removed: GSTIN, PAN, phone numbers, email addresses, UPI IDs, IFSC codes, long numbers such as bank account numbers, and your Windows user name. You see the form before anything is posted, and it is sent only if you send the email."},{"u":"security.html#updates-and-security-fixes","p":"Is it safe?","s":"Updates and security fixes","t":"updates-and-security-fixes\"> Regular updates. Your purchase includes 3 years of updates, with urgent fixes sooner. The app tells you when one is ready; see Updating . Watched for known problems. Security alerts watch the code libraries the app uses, and a known security problem in one of them is fixed in an update. Only what the app needs. The download contains the built app and only the packages its server needs to run. Developer tools are left out."},{"u":"security.html#what-you-should-do","p":"Is it safe?","s":"What you should do","t":"what-you-should-do\"> Download only from the official places : billing.reazix.com or the install line on these pages. Copies on other websites, on YouTube links or forwarded on WhatsApp are not ours and may have been changed. Keep Windows or macOS up to date , and keep its built-in antivirus on. Put a password on your computer account , and turn on the app's PIN lock if others use the same PC. Keep a backup copy on another drive or a USB disk (see Keeping a copy somewhere else ). Keep the app updated : click Update when it tells you a new version is ready."},{"u":"security.html#report-a-security-issue","p":"Is it safe?","s":"Found a security problem?","t":"report-a-security-issue\"> Please report it privately, not in a public issue, so it can be fixed before anyone misuses it: Email : contact@reazix.com with SECURITY in the subject. Use made-up data when you describe it, never real invoices or GSTINs."}];
